{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115175926,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f533ce38001B14m6zzMFkwPSK","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f533c5eb001MzTNwinWPkE32N","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9575fb9fa127594c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-166\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Deep Review Strategy: expansive-depth program, fan-out lineage deepseek\"\n3: description: \"Session tracking for the detached deep-review lineage that reviews the expansive-depth program's runtime, command YAML, agents and mirrors.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.1.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: Range 21c4b325b5a..de32abbb74d -- the expansive-depth program across `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop`, `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/agents` and the `.claude`, `.codex`, `.pi`, `.dsh` and `.vibe` agent mirrors. Runtime code and tests, command YAML and presentation, skill docs, playbooks and catalogs are in scope; specs/ evidence and spec-packet artifacts are excluded.\n36: \n37: This is the detached fan-out lineage `deepseek`. The same range is reviewed in parallel by an `opus` lineage; the cross-lineage merge is the authoritative rollup.\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n42: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n43: - [ ] security\n44: - [ ] traceability\n45: - [ ] maintainability\n46: \n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: - Spec-packet artifacts under `specs/`: excluded from the target, used only as traceability evidence when a code finding needs the governing contract.\n51: - Generated artifacts the range rebuilt (compiled routing, skill graph, graph metadata, compiled command contracts): pruned as generated artifacts, not reviewable work.\n52: - Fixes: this loop reports findings only. Implementation is a separate follow-up.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n57: - Legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1, or `maxIterations` 24, whichever comes first.\n58: - `maxDurationMinutes` 120 from `createdAt`.\n59: - Frontier veto: while a dealt node stays open or active the loop continues with reason `frontierOpen`; the three dealt nodes (F-1-003, F-1-005, F-1-007) each owe one pass per canonical dimension before they close.\n60: - Dimension order: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability, rotating across the three frontier nodes; the operator review focus (overengineering, operator UX, cross-CLI parity) is covered inside every iteration.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n65: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n66: - [x] correctness\n67: \n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n69: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n70: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n72: - P1 (Required): 0\n73: - P2 (Suggestions): 4\n74: - Resolved: 0\n75: \n76: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n81: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n82: \n83: ---\n84: \n85: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n86: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n91: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n92: ### Duplicate `node -e` extend scripts across the two YAML assets: the duplication predates the range and the copies track real config-shape differences (research nests lineage fields and has an inbox), so it is not a range-introduced overengineering finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n93: - What was tried: Duplicate `node -e` extend scripts across the two YAML assets: the duplication predates the range and the copies track real config-shape differences (research nests lineage fields and has an inbox), so it is not a range-introduced overengineering finding.\n94: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n95: - Do NOT retry: Duplicate `node -e` extend scripts across the two YAML assets: the duplication predates the range and the copies track real config-shape differences (research nests lineage fields and has an inbox), so it is not a range-introduced overengineering finding.\n96: \n97: ### Flat partition-guard set collision: a missing depth-1 node cannot be masked by another lineage's node because depth-1 ids are minted once by the shared seed; only child ids repeat per lineage, and those are qualified before the set is built. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n98: - What was tried: Flat partition-guard set collision: a missing depth-1 node cannot be masked by another lineage's node because depth-1 ids are minted once by the shared seed; only child ids repeat per lineage, and those are qualified before the set is built.\n99: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n100: - Do NOT retry: Flat partition-guard set collision: a missing depth-1 node cannot be masked by another lineage's node because depth-1 ids are minted once by the shared seed; only child ids repeat per lineage, and those are qualified before the set is built.\n101: \n102: ### Locale-dependent ordering of merged lists: the merge sorts with code-unit `compareText` everywhere, so only the partition assignment (finding 2) is exposed. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n103: - What was tried: Locale-dependent ordering of merged lists: the merge sorts with code-unit `compareText` everywhere, so only the partition assignment (finding 2) is exposed.\n104: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n105: - Do NOT retry: Locale-dependent ordering of merged lists: the merge sorts with code-unit `compareText` everywhere, so only the partition assignment (finding 2) is exposed.\n106: \n107: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n108: \n109: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: \n117: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n118: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n119: Frontier node F-1-005 (depth 1, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-reducers, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-reducers): Are the state reducers, upsert, convergence and iteration verification changes correct and free of duplicated logic: node status derivation, dimension coverage, extension bookkeeping, frontier_drained stops and the ledger schema and projection changes? - review the correctness dimension\n120: \n121: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n122: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n123: \n124: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n125: \n126: - Target pointers: `21c4b325b5a..de32abbb74d` over `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop`, `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/agents` and the `.claude`, `.codex`, `.pi`, `.dsh`, `.vibe` agent mirrors. The range adds ~25k lines across 232 files; the frontier nodes partition the reviewable work.\n127: - Behavior claims: `SKILL.md` §Expansive Depth Mode, `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md` §Expansive Depth Frontier, `references/convergence/convergence.md` §Expansive Depth Mode, and the `deep-review.yaml`/`deep-research.yaml` steps that implement them.\n128: - Reuse and conventions: `append-mode-event.cjs` is the only state-log writer; `reduce-state.cjs` owns registry/dashboard/strategy; `sk-git`, `sk-code` and `sk-doc` conventions apply to their surfaces.\n129: - Review risks and gaps: the range is larger than any single iteration can read; each iteration records what it could not read rather than treating absence as a pass.\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n134: \n135: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n136: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n137: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n138: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n139: | `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n140: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n141: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n142: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n143: \n144: ---\n145: \n146: ## 14. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n147: \n148: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n149: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n150: | [pending first pass] | - | - | - | pending |\n151: \n152: ---\n153: \n154: ## 15. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n155: - Max iterations: 24\n156: - Convergence threshold: 0.1\n157: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n158: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n159: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z, parentSessionId=(none), generation=1, lineageMode=new\n160: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n161: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n162: - Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n163: - Severity threshold: P2\n164: - Review target type: files\n165: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n166: - Started: 2026-11-19T18:41:16.000Z","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-166\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Deep Review Strategy: expansive-depth program, fan-out lineage deepseek\"\n3: description: \"Session tracking for the detached deep-review lineage that reviews the expansive-depth program's runtime, command YAML, agents and mirrors.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.1.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: Range 21c4b325b5a..de32abbb74d -- the expansive-depth program across `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop`, `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/agents` and the `.claude`, `.codex`, `.pi`, `.dsh` and `.vibe` agent mirrors. Runtime code and tests, command YAML and presentation, skill docs, playbooks and catalogs are in scope; specs/ evidence and spec-packet artifacts are excluded.\n36: \n37: This is the detached fan-out lineage `deepseek`. The same range is reviewed in parallel by an `opus` lineage; the cross-lineage merge is the authoritative rollup.\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n42: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n43: - [ ] security\n44: - [ ] traceability\n45: - [ ] maintainability\n46: \n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: - Spec-packet artifacts under `specs/`: excluded from the target, used only as traceability evidence when a code finding needs the governing contract.\n51: - Generated artifacts the range rebuilt (compiled routing, skill graph, graph metadata, compiled command contracts): pruned as generated artifacts, not reviewable work.\n52: - Fixes: this loop reports findings only. Implementation is a separate follow-up.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n57: - Legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1, or `maxIterations` 24, whichever comes first.\n58: - `maxDurationMinutes` 120 from `createdAt`.\n59: - Frontier veto: while a dealt node stays open or active the loop continues with reason `frontierOpen`; the three dealt nodes (F-1-003, F-1-005, F-1-007) each owe one pass per canonical dimension before they close.\n60: - Dimension order: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability, rotating across the three frontier nodes; the operator review focus (overengineering, operator UX, cross-CLI parity) is covered inside every iteration.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n65: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n66: - [x] correctness\n67: \n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n69: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n70: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n72: - P1 (Required): 0\n73: - P2 (Suggestions): 4\n74: - Resolved: 0\n75: \n76: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n81: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n82: \n83: ---\n84: \n85: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n86: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n91: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n92: ### Duplicate `node -e` extend scripts across the two YAML assets: the duplication predates the range and the copies track real config-shape differences (research nests lineage fields and has an inbox), so it is not a range-introduced overengineering finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n93: - What was tried: Duplicate `node -e` extend scripts across the two YAML assets: the duplication predates the range and the copies track real config-shape differences (research nests lineage fields and has an inbox), so it is not a range-introduced overengineering finding.\n94: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n95: - Do NOT retry: Duplicate `node -e` extend scripts across the two YAML assets: the duplication predates the range and the copies track real config-shape differences (research nests lineage fields and has an inbox), so it is not a range-introduced overengineering finding.\n96: \n97: ### Flat partition-guard set collision: a missing depth-1 node cannot be masked by another lineage's node because depth-1 ids are minted once by the shared seed; only child ids repeat per lineage, and those are qualified before the set is built. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n98: - What was tried: Flat partition-guard set collision: a missing depth-1 node cannot be masked by another lineage's node because depth-1 ids are minted once by the shared seed; only child ids repeat per lineage, and those are qualified before the set is built.\n99: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n100: - Do NOT retry: Flat partition-guard set collision: a missing depth-1 node cannot be masked by another lineage's node because depth-1 ids are minted once by the shared seed; only child ids