 \"graph\"` and lineage B never writes the key; the merged report renders no mode, so a reader cannot tell that B ran without a graph.\n47: \n48: 4. **The merge re-implements the reducer's traceability summary arithmetic** -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:982 -- `mergeTraceability` recomputes `required`, `executed`, `pass`, `partial`, `fail`, `blocked`, `notApplicable` and `gatingFailures` from merged results with an eight-line block that duplicates `reduce-state.cjs:1652-1665` verbatim, including the `gateClass === 'hard'` predicate. Two copies of one counting rule drift the moment either side adds a status or a gate class; the merged registry is exactly the surface a release report reads.\n49: Finding class: instance-only\n50: Scope proof: the two blocks are textually identical apart from the undecided-set constant name (`TRACEABILITY_UNDECIDED` versus `TRACEABILITY_UNDECIDED_STATUSES`); `reduce-state.cjs` exports `buildTraceabilityRollup`, so the merge could call it instead of copying it.\n51: Affected surface hints: [\"fanout-merge.cjs mergeTraceability\", \"reduce-state.cjs buildTraceabilityRollup\"]\n52: Case: a future status is added to `TRACEABILITY_UNDECIDED_STATUSES` only; the reducer stops counting it as executed while the merge keeps counting it, and the same run reports two different executed totals.\n53: \n54: ## Traceability Checks\n55: \n56: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n57: |----------|--------|----------|\n58: | `spec_code` | pass | 009 `plan.md` section 3 lists the six merge rules and the code matches each: dimension OR (`fanout-merge.cjs:946`), strongest-restriction traceability (`:966`), sorted-union search coverage (`:999`), per-bug-class candidate merge (`:1014`), per-lineage divergence (`:1039`), lineage-qualified ruled-out rows (`:1047`). 011 REQ-008's round-robin partition, `frontier_scope:` binding and `frontier_partition` summary are present (`fanout-run.cjs:347`, `:1826`, `:3896`); REQ-019's per-share budget with D 4 and the 12/7 floors is implemented (`:378`, `:381`). |\n59: \n60: ## Integration Evidence\n61: \n62: - `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:363-416` (`step_fanout_spawn`) passes `--review-focus-file`, `--review-target-file`, `--fanout-config-json-file` and `--depth-mode`, which are the flags this iteration read.\n63: - `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:28` owns `{frontier_block}` for the native per-iteration prompt; the detached CLI lineage prompt is built by `fanout-run.cjs:1791` and carries no such block.\n64: - `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:928` (`compareText`) is the ordering helper the merged lists use.\n65: \n66: ## Edge Cases\n67: \n68: - The fan-out config labels are unique per run, so the partition map cannot collide on a label; the round-robin index still depends on the order of `expandedLineages`, which follows the config's executor order.\n69: - A lineage dealt no node is accepted by design (the runner warns and runs it at the loop default); this iteration did not treat that as a defect.\n70: - The review target is a commit range, so `partitionFrontierNodes` reads the seeded store rather than the diff; an empty store yields an empty partition and no `frontier_scope` line, which the runner tolerates.\n71: \n72: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n73: \n74: - `expansiveLineageBudgets` keeps an explicit matrix `iterations` value (`Number.isInteger` is safe because `executor-config.ts:865` validates `z.number().int().positive().nullable()`), and it uses the documented D 4 and 12/7 floors.\n75: - `writeLineageFrontierStore` refuses to overwrite an existing store, so a resumed lineage keeps the nodes it already closed, and a review lineage correctly gets no inbox.\n76: - `mergeResearchFrontier` qualifies child ids with the lineage label, so two lineages' `F-2-002` children cannot collide, and the guard compares only the globally unique depth-1 ids.\n77: \n78: ## Ruled Out\n79: \n80: - Flat partition-guard set collision: a missing depth-1 node cannot be masked by another lineage's node because depth-1 ids are minted once by the shared seed; only child ids repeat per lineage, and those are qualified before the set is built.\n81: - Duplicate `node -e` extend scripts across the two YAML assets: the duplication predates the range and the copies track real config-shape differences (research nests lineage fields and has an inbox), so it is not a range-introduced overengineering finding.\n82: - Locale-dependent ordering of merged lists: the merge sorts with code-unit `compareText` everywhere, so only the partition assignment (finding 2) is exposed.\n83: \n84: ## Next Focus\n85: \n86: - Dimension: correctness on F-1-005 (reducers, convergence, verification and the ledger/projection layer).\n87: - Reason: iteration 1 cleared the fan-out runner/merge surface at the P2 level; the reducer and convergence path decides node status, dimension coverage and the stop decision, so it carries the next correctness risk.\n88: - Required evidence: `reduce-state.cjs` node-status and frontier projection, `convergence.cjs` stop arithmetic, `verify-iteration.cjs` and `dispatch-iteration.cjs` guards.\n89: - Rotation status: F-1-003 remains open with correctness covered; F-1-005 and F-1-007 have no dimension covered yet.\n90: \n91: Review verdict: PASS"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115182058,"end":1795115182368}}}}
