{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115194358,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53416fb001pyj4Kdexdbuwf3","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5341035001rr7VOpYdVi9qsy","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83fac4a31025ca99","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md","offset":420,"limit":160},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md, lines 420-579\n420: - In **auto mode**: written silently for post-hoc review\n421: \n422: #### Step 5: Loop Decision\n423: \n424: - If convergence check returns STOP: exit to synthesis\n425: - If STUCK_RECOVERY: apply review-specific recovery strategies (see Section 3a), reset stuck count, continue\n426: - Otherwise: increment iteration counter, go to Step 1\n427: \n428: ### Stuck Recovery (Review-Specific)\n429: \n430: **Threshold:** 2 consecutive no-progress iterations (`noProgressThreshold = 0.05`).\n431: \n432: | Failure Mode | Detection | Recovery Strategy |\n433: |-------------|-----------|-------------------|\n434: | Same dimension stuck | Last 2 iterations reviewed the same dimension with ratios `< 0.05` | **Change granularity**: if reviewing at file level, zoom into functions, if reviewing functions, zoom out to module level |\n435: | Traceability plateau | Required protocols remain partial while ratios stay `< 0.05` | **Protocol-first replay**: re-run the unresolved traceability protocol directly against the conflicting artifacts |\n436: | Low-value advisory churn | Last 2 iterations found only P2 work | **Escalate severity review**: explicitly search for P0/P1 patterns or downgrade unsupported severity claims |\n437: \n438: **Selection logic**:\n439: \n440: ```\n441: function selectReviewRecoveryStrategy(stuckIterations, state, config):\n442:   lastFocuses = [i.focus for i in stuckIterations[-2:]]\n443: \n444:   // Same dimension stuck? Change granularity\n445:   if len(set(lastFocuses)) <= 1:\n446:     return { strategy: \"change_granularity\", dimension: lastFocuses[0] }\n447: \n448:   // Required protocol plateau?\n449:   if hasRequiredProtocolPlateau(state.traceabilityChecks):\n450:     return { strategy: \"protocol_first_replay\" }\n451: \n452:   // Default: escalate severity\n453:   return { strategy: \"escalate_severity_review\" }\n454: ```\n455: \n456: **Recovery evaluation**:\n457: - If recovery iteration finds any new P0/P1 or materially advances required traceability coverage: recovery successful. Reset stuck count. Continue.\n458: - If recovery iteration finds only P2 or nothing: recovery failed. If all dimensions are already covered, exit to synthesis. Otherwise, move to the next unreviewed dimension.\n459: \n460: ---\n461: \n462: ### Expansive Depth Frontier (opt-in)\n463: \n464: Under `--depth-mode=expansive` the loop keeps a frontier of sub-target nodes beside the review target. The flag writes `antiConvergence.depthMode: \"expansive\"` and the caps in `expansiveDepth`: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a review root up to 8 depth-1 children because the seed asks for 3 to 8 sub-targets, a `budgetSplit` of 0.5/0.35/0.15 across the depth bands and `maxFrontierNodes`, which defaults to half of `maxIterations` unless the config sets a number. Two flags set the caps when the config is created: `--frontier-max-depth=N` writes `maxDepth` and `--frontier-max-nodes=N` writes `maxFrontierNodes`; both take a positive integer, need `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run, and are refused on a fan-out config. The depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap, but every seed that is not pruned counts toward the run cap. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(7, 2 × D × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes and D the four canonical dimensions plus each custom name the config's `reviewDimensions` list adds, each counted once, and the seed step prints the derived budget. Since D is never below four, the ceiling of 24 binds from the first seed, so one run cannot fund every node at every depth of a wide review; split a wide review with fan-out, where each lineage with no matrix `iterations` value sizes its own budget from its share of the seed, with D fixed at the canonical four because a lineage reviews only those. A lineage dealt no seed node, or a run whose seeds were all pruned, runs at its loop default instead: 12 iterations for a native lineage and 7 for a CLI one or a single run. The node cap stays half the budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n465: \n466: `step_frontier_seed` decomposes the review target into depth-1 sub-target nodes before iteration 1, through `runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review`. On a plain run it sits in `phase_init` after `step_create_config`; on a fan-out run it runs before `step_fanout_spawn`. A merge that carries no diff of its own is pruned `merge-no-own-diff` and an index rebuild `generated-artifact`, because neither is reviewable work.\n467: \n468: `step_read_state` reads `active_frontier_node` from `registry.frontier.activeNodeId` and sets `next_dimension` to that node's next uncovered dimension, so the iteration reviews depth the node has not spent yet. On the last iteration under a cap of 2 or more, while a core traceability protocol is unfinished and `traceability` is among the run's dimensions, `next_dimension` is `traceability` instead. A configured subset that leaves traceability out is not steered, so the last iteration reviews the configured dimensions in order. `step_frontier_activate` marks the node `active` before the dispatch, and the prompt pack's `{frontier_block}` names the node; a leaf proposes `frontier_proposal` rows only when its block is non-empty.\n469: \n470: `step_frontier_admit` runs before the reducer and applies six checks in order: relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget, cycle. Relevance includes a node's scope sitting inside a file-list review target. The first failure prunes the proposal under that check's name. A review run has no inbox, so the store alone queues an admitted node, and `runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs --target review` writes it, apart from the starting store `fanout-run.cjs` writes for each fan-out lineage.\n471: \n472: Next Focus reads, in precedence order: blocked-stop recovery, the pivot, the active frontier node, the leaf's `nextFocus` when it names an uncovered dimension or every dimension is covered, and otherwise the first uncovered dimension. The `frontierOpen` veto holds the loop at CONTINUE while a node stays open, and never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off`, `--stop-policy=max-iterations` or the review floor. Stuck recovery closes the active node `exhausted` with reason `stuck` before recovery continues. Once no node is open or active and at least one is answered, a run with no other candidate gets the hard `frontier_drained` candidate, which the legal-stop gates and the graph decision still decide.\n473: \n474: On a fan-out run the depth-1 nodes are dealt round-robin in node-id order, `frontier_scope:` binds each lineage's node ids beside `review_focus:` in its prompt, and the partition is recorded as `frontier_partition` in `orchestration-summary.json`. Each lineage dealt at least one node gets its store before it spawns, the merge returns a merged `frontier`, and a partition guard names any dealt node no lineage reports. A lineage reviews the canonical four only, because fan-out binds `review_dimensions: all` in every lineage, so a lineage node needs four iterations and 50% of each lineage's `maxIterations` should reach `ceil(nodes / lineages) * 4`; below that the depth-1 band cannot fund the nodes it was dealt.\n475: \n476: ---\n477: \n478: ## 4. PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n479: \n480: ### Purpose\n481: \n482: Compile all iteration findings into the final `{artifact_dir}/review-report.md`. The synthesis phase owns the canonical review report output.\n483: \n484: ### Steps\n485: \n486: #### Step 1: Finding Registry Deduplication\n487: \n488: Consolidate findings across all iterations:\n489: \n490: 1. Read all iteration files: `{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-*.md`\n491: 2. Group findings by file + line range + root cause\n492: 3. Merge duplicates, keeping the highest severity and all evidence\n493: 4. Assign final finding IDs: `F001`, `F002`, ...\n494: 5. Preserve the audit trail: note which iterations contributed to each merged finding\n495: \n496: #### Step 2: Severity Reconciliation\n497: \n498: Use adjudicated `finalSeverity` for any P0/P1 that was downgraded during claim adjudication (Step 4a of the iteration loop). The original severity from the iteration file is preserved in the audit appendix.\n499: \n500: #### Step 3: Replay Validation\n501: \n502: Recompute the convergence outcome from JSONL state before finalizing the report:\n503: \n504: 1. Read `deep-review-state.jsonl` and select review-mode iteration records in run order\n505: 2. Recompute `newFindingsRatio`, rolling-average votes, MAD votes, and coverage votes from stored JSONL fields only\n506: 3. Recompute `traceabilityChecks.summary` and confirm required protocol statuses match the recorded coverage vote\n507: 4. Re-run the evidence, scope, and coverage gates against stored findings and scope data\n508: 5. Compare the replayed decision and stop reason to the recorded synthesis event\n509: \n510: This synthesis-stage replay is a **full-history audit replay** over the stored JSONL state. It follows the same full-history replay discipline as the per-iteration reducer refresh above, but runs as an explicit pre-synthesis audit.\n511: \n512: Replay passes only when the recomputed decision, thresholds, and gate outcomes agree with the persisted result. If replay fails, log a warning in the audit appendix but proceed with synthesis.\n513: \n514: #### Step 4: Compile review-report.md\n515: \n516: Generate the 9 core review-report sections (defined in `review-mode-contract.yaml` under `outputs.reviewReport`) and insert `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` between `Traceability Status` and `Deferred Items` when `config.resource_map_present == true`:\n517: \n518: | # | Section | Purpose |\n519: |---|---------|---------|\n520: | 1 | Executive Summary | Verdict, active P0/P1/P2 counts, scope, `hasAdvisories` metadata |\n521: | 2 | Planning Trigger | Why the verdict routes to planning or changelog follow-up |\n522: | 3 | Active Finding Registry | Deduplicated active findings with evidence and final severity |\n523: | 4 | Remediation Workstreams | Grouped action lanes derived from active findings |\n524: | 5 | Spec Seed | Minimal spec delta derived from review results |\n525: | 6 | Plan Seed | Action-ready plan starter for remediation |\n526: | 7 | Traceability Status | Core vs overlay protocol status and unresolved gaps |\n527: | 8 | Resource Map Coverage Gate | Present only when `config.resource_map_present == true`, reports touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map |\n528: | 9 | Deferred Items | P2 advisories, blocked checks, and follow-up items |\n529: | 10 | Audit Appendix | Coverage, replay validation, convergence evidence |\n530: \n531: #### Step 5: Verdict Determination\n532: \n533: Apply the verdict contract from `review-mode-contract.yaml`:\n534: \n535: | Verdict | Condition | Next Command |\n536: |---------|-----------|--------------|\n537: | **FAIL** | Active P0 remains OR any required binary gate fails | `/speckit:plan` for remediation |\n538: | **CONDITIONAL** | No active P0, but active P1 remains or search debt is still open | `/speckit:plan` for fixes |\n539: | **PASS** | No active P0/P1 and no open search debt | `/create:changelog` |\n540: \n541: When `PASS` verdict is issued and active P2 findings remain, set `hasAdvisories = true` in the report metadata.\n542: \n543: #### Step 6: Finalize State\n544: \n545: 1. Update config status: Set `status: \"complete\"` in `deep-review-config.json`\n546: 2. Write final JSONL entry:\n547:    ```json\n548:    {\n549:      \"type\": \"event\",\n550:      \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\",\n551:      \"mode\": \"review\",\n552:      \"totalIterations\": N,\n553:      \"verdict\": \"PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL\",\n554:      \"activeP0\": N,\n555:      \"activeP1\": N,\n556:      \"activeP2\": N,\n557:      \"dimensionCoverage\": X,\n558:      \"stopReason\": \"...\",\n559:      \"timestamp\": \"...\"\n560:    }\n561:    ```\n562: 3. Refresh the dashboard: `step_refresh_completed_dashboard` reruns the reducer after the status flip, so the dashboard reports the completed status. A fan-out run skips it, and a failure only logs a warning.\n563: \n564: ---\n565: \n566: ## 5. PHASE 4: SAVE\n567: \n568: ### Purpose\n569: \n570: Preserve review context to the memory system for future session recovery and cross-session continuity.\n571: \n572: ### Steps\n573: \n574: 1. **Compose context payload**: Create a structured JSON payload with the review summary, active findings, verdict, next action, and relevant artifacts. Use `specFolder` for the target packet and include curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` when available. A full-auto save writes continuity only from `recent_action`, `next_safe_action`, `blockers` and `key_files`, so the payload carries all four. Write it to the session-scoped file `/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json`.\n575: \n576: 2. **Generate context**: Run the continuity writer on that file with `--full-auto`. Without `--full-auto` the writer only plans and writes no continuity.\n577:    ```bash\n578:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder} --full-auto\n579:    ```\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 580]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md, lines 420-579\n420: - In **auto mode**: written silently for post-hoc review\n421: \n422: #### Step 5: Loop Decision\n423: \n424: - If convergence check returns STOP: exit to synthesis\n425: - If STUCK_RECOVERY: apply review-specific recovery strategies (see Section 3a), reset stuck count, continue\n426: - Otherwise: increment iteration counter, go to Step 1\n427: \n428: ### Stuck Recovery (Review-Specific)\n429: \n430: **Threshold:** 2 consecutive no-progress iterations (`noProgressThreshold = 0.05`).\n431: \n432: | Failure Mode | Detection | Recovery Strategy |\n433: |-------------|-----------|-------------------|\n434: | Same dimension stuck | Last 2 iterations reviewed the same dimension with ratios `< 0.05` | **Change granularity**: if reviewing at file level, zoom into functions, if reviewing functions, zoom out to module level |\n435: | Traceability plateau | Required protocols remain partial while ratios stay `< 0.05` | **Protocol-first replay**: re-run the unresolved traceability protocol directly against the conflicting artifacts |\n436: | Low-value advisory churn | Last 2 iterations found only P2 work | **Escalate severity review**: explicitly search for P0/P1 patterns or downgrade unsupported severity claims |\n437: \n438: **Selection logic**:\n439: \n440: ```\n441: function selectReviewRecoveryStrategy(stuckIterations, state, config):\n442:   lastFocuses = [i.focus for i in stuckIterations[-2:]]\n443: \n444:   // Same dimension stuck? Change granularity\n445:   if len(set(lastFocuses)) <= 1:\n446:     return { strategy: \"change_granularity\", dimension: lastFocuses[0] }\n447: \n448:   // Required protocol plateau?\n449:   if hasRequiredProtocolPlateau(state.traceabilityChecks):\n450:     return { strategy: \"protocol_first_replay\" }\n451: \n452:   // Default: escalate severity\n453:   return { strategy: \"escalate_severity_review\" }\n454: ```\n455: \n456: **Recovery evaluation**:\n457: - If recovery iteration finds any new P0/P1 or materially advances required traceability coverage: recovery successful. Reset stuck count. Continue.\n458: - If recovery iteration finds only P2 or nothing: recovery failed. If all dimensions are already covered, exit to synthesis. Otherwise, move to the next unreviewed dimension.\n459: \n460: ---\n461: \n462: ### Expansive Depth Frontier (opt-in)\n463: \n464: Under `--depth-mode=expansive` the loop keeps a frontier of sub-target nodes beside the review target. The flag writes `antiConvergence.depthMode: \"expansive\"` and the caps in `expansiveDepth`: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a review root up to 8 depth-1 children because the seed asks for 3 to 8 sub-targets, a `budgetSplit` of 0.5/0.35/0.15 across the depth bands and `maxFrontierNodes`, which defaults to half of `maxIterations` unless the config sets a number. Two flags set the caps when the config is created: `--frontier-max-depth=N` writes `maxDepth` and `--frontier-max-nodes=N` writes `maxFrontierNodes`; both take a positive integer, need `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run, and are refused on a fan-out config. The depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap, but every seed that is not pruned counts toward the run cap. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(7, 2 × D × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes and D the four canonical dimensions plus each custom name the config's `reviewDimensions` list adds, each counted once, and the seed step prints the derived budget. Since D is never below four, the ceiling of 24 binds from the first seed, so one run cannot fund every node at every depth of a wide review; split a wide review with fan-out, where each lineage with no matrix `iterations` value sizes its own budget from its share of the seed, with D fixed at the canonical four because a lineage reviews only those. A lineage dealt no seed node, or a run whose seeds were all pruned, runs at its loop default instead: 12 iterations for a native lineage and 7 for a CLI one or a single run. The node cap stays half the budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n465: \n466: `step_frontier_seed` decomposes the review target into depth-1 sub-target nodes before iteration 1, through `runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review`. On a plain run it sits in `phase_init` after `step_create_config`; on a fan-out run it runs before `step_fanout_spawn`. A merge that carries no diff of its own is pruned `merge-no-own-diff` and an index rebuild `generated-artifact`, because neither is reviewable work.\n467: \n468: `step_read_state` reads `active_frontier_node` from `registry.frontier.activeNodeId` and sets `next_dimension` to that node's next uncovered dimension, so the iteration reviews depth the node has not spent yet. On the last iteration under a cap of 2 or more, while a core traceability protocol is unfinished and `traceability` is among the run's dimensions, `next_dimension` is `traceability` instead. A configured subset that leaves traceability out is not steered, so the last iteration reviews the configured dimensions in order. `step_frontier_activate` marks the node `active` before the dispatch, and the prompt pack's `{frontier_block}` names the node; a leaf proposes `frontier_proposal` rows only when its block is non-empty.\n469: \n470: `step_frontier_admit` runs before the reducer and applies six checks in order: relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget, cycle. Relevance includes a node's scope sitting inside a file-list review target. The first failure prunes the proposal under that check's name. A review run has no inbox, so the store alone queues an admitted node, and `runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs --target review` writes it, apart from the starting store `fanout-run.cjs` writes for each fan-out lineage.\n471: \n472: Next Focus reads, in precedence order: blocked-stop recovery, the pivot, the active frontier node, the leaf's `nextFocus` when it names an uncovered dimension or every dimension is covered, and otherwise the first uncovered dimension. The `frontierOpen` veto holds the loop at CONTINUE while a node stays open, and never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off`, `--stop-policy=max-iterations` or the review floor. Stuck recovery closes the active node `exhausted` with reason `stuck` before recovery continues. Once no node is open or active and at least one is answered, a run with no other candidate gets the hard `frontier_drained` candidate, which the legal-stop gates and the graph decision still decide.\n473: \n474: On a fan-out run the depth-1 nodes are dealt round-robin in node-id order, `frontier_scope:` binds each lineage's node ids beside `review_focus:` in its prompt, and the partition is recorded as `frontier_partition` in `orchestration-summary.json`. Each lineage dealt at least one node gets its store before it spawns, the merge returns a merged `frontier`, and a partition guard names any dealt node no lineage reports. A lineage reviews the canonical four only, because fan-out binds `review_dimensions: all` in every lineage, so a lineage node needs four iterations and 50% of each lineage's `maxIterations` should reach `ceil(nodes / lineages) * 4`; below that the depth-1 band cannot fund the nodes it was dealt.\n475: \n476: ---\n477: \n478: ## 4. PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n479: \n480: ### Purpose\n481: \n482: Compile all iteration findings into the final `{artifact_dir}/review-report.md`. The synthesis phase owns the canonical review report output.\n483: \n484: ### Steps\n485: \n486: #### Step 1: Finding Registry Deduplication\n487: \n488: Consolidate findings across all iterations:\n489: \n490: 1. Read all iteration files: `{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-*.md`\n491: 2. Group findings by file + line range + root cause\n492: 3. Merge duplicates, keeping the highest severity and all evidence\n493: 4. Assign final finding IDs: `F001`, `F002`, ...\n494: 5. Preserve the audit trail: note which iterations contributed to each merged finding\n495: \n496: #### Step 2: Severity Reconciliation\n497: \n498: Use adjudicated `finalSeverity` for any P0/P1 that was downgraded during claim adjudication (Step 4a of the iteration loop). The original severity from the iteration file is preserved in the audit appendix.\n499: \n500: #### Step 3: Replay Validation\n501: \n502: Recompute the convergence outcome from JSONL state before finalizing the report:\n503: \n504: 1. Read `deep-review-state.jsonl` and select review-mode iteration records in run order\n505: 2. Recompute `newFindingsRatio`, rolling-average votes, MAD votes, and coverage votes from stored JSONL fields only\n506: 3. Recompute `traceabilityChecks.summary` and confirm required protocol statuses match the recorded coverage vote\n507: 4. Re-run the evidence, scope, and coverage gates against stored findings and scope data\n508: 5. Compare the replayed decision and stop reason to the recorded synthesis event\n509: \n510: This synthesis-stage replay is a **full-history audit replay** over the stored JSONL state. It follows the same full-history replay discipline as the per-iteration reducer refresh above, but runs as an explicit pre-synthesis audit.\n511: \n512: Replay passes only when the recomputed decision, thresholds, and gate outcomes agree with the persisted result. If replay fails, log a warning in the audit appendix but proceed with synthesis.\n513: \n514: #### Step 4: Compile review-report.md\n515: \n516: Generate the 9 core review-report sections (defined in `review-mode-contract.yaml` under `outputs.reviewReport`) and insert `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` between `Traceability Status` and `Deferred Items` when `config.resource_map_present == true`:\n517: \n518: | # | Section | Purpose |\n519: |---|---------|---------|\n520: | 1 | Executive Summary | Verdict, active P0/P1/P2 counts, scope, `hasAdvisories` metadata |\n521: | 2 | Planning Trigger | Why the verdict routes to planning or changelog follow-up |\n522: | 3 | Active Finding Registry | Deduplicated active findings with evidence and final severity |\n523: | 4 | Remediation Workstreams | Grouped action lanes derived from active findings |\n524: | 5 | Spec Seed | Minimal spec delta derived from review results |\n525: | 6 | Plan Seed | Action-ready plan starter for remediation |\n526: | 7 | Traceability Status | Core vs overlay protocol status and unresolved gaps |\n527: | 8 | Resource Map Coverage Gate | Present only when `config.resource_map_present == true`, reports touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map |\n528: | 9 | Deferred Items | P2 advisories, blocked checks, and follow-up items |\n529: | 10 | Audit Appendix | Coverage, replay validation, convergence evidence |\n530: \n531: #### Step 5: Verdict Determination\n532: \n533: Apply the verdict contract from `review-mode-contract.yaml`:\n534: \n535: | Verdict | Condition | Next Command |\n536: |---------|-----------|--------------|\n537: | **FAIL** | Active P0 remains OR any required binary gate fails | `/speckit:plan` for remediation |\n538: | **CONDITIONAL** | No active P0, but active P1 remains or search debt is still open | `/speckit:plan` for fixes |\n539: | **PASS** | No active P0/P1 and no open search debt | `/create:changelog` |\n540: \n541: When `PASS` verdict is issued and active P2 findings remain, set `hasAdvisories = true` in the report metadata.\n542: \n543: #### Step 6: Finalize State\n544: \n545: 1. Update config status: Set `status: \"complete\"` in `deep-review-config.json`\n546: 2. Write final JSONL entry:\n547:    ```json\n548:    {\n549:      \"type\": \"event\",\n550:      \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\",\n551:      \"mode\": \"review\",\n552:      \"totalIterations\": N,\n553:      \"verdict\": \"PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL\",\n554:      \"activeP0\": N,\n555:      \"activeP1\": N,\n556:      \"activeP2\": N,\n557:      \"dimensionCoverage\": X,\n558:      \"stopReason\": \"...\",\n559:      \"timestamp\": \"...\"\n560:    }\n561:    ```\n562: 3. Refresh the dashboard: `step_refresh_completed_dashboard` reruns the reducer after the status flip, so the dashboard reports the completed status. A fan-out run skips it, and a failure only logs a warning.\n563: \n564: ---\n565: \n566: ## 5. PHASE 4: SAVE\n567: \n568: ### Purpose\n569: \n570: Preserve review context to the memory system for future session recovery and cross-session continuity.\n571: \n572: ### Steps\n573: \n574: 1. **Compose context payload**: Create a structured JSON payload with the review summary, active findings, verdict, next action, and relevant artifacts. Use `specFolder` for the target packet and include curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` when available. A full-auto save writes continuity only from `recent_action`, `next_safe_action`, `blockers` and `key_files`, so the payload carries all four. Write it to the session-scoped file `/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json`.\n575: \n576: 2. **Generate context**: Run the continuity writer on that file with `--full-auto`. Without `--full-auto` the writer only plans and writes no continuity.\n577:    ```bash\n578:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder} --full-auto\n579:    ```\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 580]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\", \"offset\": 420, \"limit\": 160}"},"time":{"start":1795115194107,"end":1795115194358}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115194397,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5341700001zfel2vKgY6eo2X","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5341035001rr7VOpYdVi9qsy","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a34647f73bf5439b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"frontier\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md | head -30; echo \"===node status reducer===\"; grep -n \"frontierNodeId\\|frontier_node\\|nodeStatus\\|status.*closed\\|dimensionsCovered\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs | head -40"},"output":"105:`--depth-mode=expansive` grows a depth-capped frontier of sub-target nodes beside the review target. The value lands in `antiConvergence.depthMode`, and the caps live in `expansiveDepth`: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a review root up to 8 depth-1 children because the seed asks for 3 to 8 sub-targets, a `budgetSplit` of 0.5/0.35/0.15 across the depth bands and `maxFrontierNodes`, which defaults to half of `maxIterations` unless the config sets a number. Two flags set the caps when the config is created: `--frontier-max-depth=N` writes `maxDepth` and `--frontier-max-nodes=N` writes `maxFrontierNodes`; both take a positive integer, need `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run, and are refused on a fan-out config. Once a band's spend reaches its `budgetSplit` share of `maxIterations`, the reducer closes every open or active node in that band as `exhausted` with reason `budget`, and an unspent share rolls down to the next band only after its own band holds no open node. The run cap never prunes a depth-1 seed, which only the root-children cap bounds, but every seed that is not pruned, answered ones included, counts toward the live total that later admissions are checked against. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(7, 2 × D × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes and D the four canonical dimensions plus each custom name the config's `reviewDimensions` list adds, each counted once, and the seed step prints the derived budget. Since D is never below four, the ceiling of 24 binds from the first seed, so one run cannot fund every node at every depth of a wide review; split a wide review with fan-out, where each lineage with no matrix `iterations` value sizes its own budget from its share of the seed, with D fixed at the canonical four because a lineage reviews only those. A lineage dealt no seed node, or a run whose seeds were all pruned, runs at its loop default instead: 12 iterations for a native lineage and 7 for a CLI one or a single run. The node cap stays half the budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. At about seven to eight minutes an iteration, a 24-iteration review can reach `maxDurationMinutes` (120) before its iteration cap. A fan-out parent seeds before any config exists, so its cap falls back to 10. The mode is locked against the optimizer; the `expansiveDepth` block is in neither its tunable nor its locked list. An absent flag means `default`, which runs exactly as before.\n107:After the review floor, an expansive run that still holds an open or active node turns a stop candidate into `CONTINUE` with reasonDetail `frontierOpen`, whichever candidate it was, `all_dimensions_clean` or a composite convergence vote. The veto never creates a stop of its own and never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off`, `--stop-policy=max-iterations` or the `minIterations` floor. Under stuck recovery the handler closes the active node as `exhausted` with reason `stuck`, so a node the run cannot fund stops holding the veto open.\n109:When the frontier holds at least one answered node and none is open or active, and neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite vote forms, an expansive run gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It ranks after the other two, so the floor, the legal-stop gates and the graph decision run on it as on any candidate: a failed gate gives `BLOCKED`, and a stop records `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained`. A fan-out lineage reads only its own partition, so one whose nodes are answered stops rather than running to its cap. A frontier that closed with nothing answered, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate, and a default run never forms it.\n115:Each eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. If that round misses quorum, because a seat fails to return or returns a report that does not parse, the pivot reopens once as attempt 2 with three fresh seat outputs. A second quorum miss, or three valid seats that do not agree, fails the pivot closed. `maxCouncilSeatOutputs` caps one council attempt at 3 seat outputs, so a pivot records at most 6. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n183:6. **Stop candidate** -- all dimensions covered and clean (every configured dimension covered, the four by default, no active P0/P1, coverage stabilized) is a hard candidate; otherwise the 3-signal composite vote with threshold 0.60 is a soft one. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a frontier with at least one answered node and none open or active is a third, hard candidate (`frontier_drained`) when neither forms. No candidate returns `CONTINUE` (`noStopCandidate`).\n185:8. **Frontier veto** -- under `--depth-mode=expansive`, an open or active frontier node turns the candidate into `CONTINUE` (`frontierOpen`).\n===node status reducer===\n1950:    if (record.frontierNodeId === nodeId) return true;\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"105:`--depth-mode=expansive` grows a depth-capped frontier of sub-target nodes beside the review target. The value lands in `antiConvergence.depthMode`, and the caps live in `expansiveDepth`: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a review root up to 8 depth-1 children because the seed asks for 3 to 8 sub-targets, a `budgetSplit` of 0.5/0.35/0.15 across the depth bands and `maxFrontierNodes`, which defaults to half of `maxIterations` unless the config sets a number. Two flags set the caps when the config is created: `--frontier-max-depth=N` writes `maxDepth` and `--frontier-max-nodes=N` writes `maxFrontierNodes`; both take a positive integer, need `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run, and are refused on a fan-out config. Once a band's spend reaches its `budgetSplit` share of `maxIterations`, the reducer closes every open or active node in that band as `exhausted` with reason `budget`, and an unspent share rolls down to the next band only after its own band holds no open node. The run cap never prunes a depth-1 seed, which only the root-children cap bounds, but every seed that is not pruned, answered ones included, counts toward the live total that later admissions are checked against. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(7, 2 × D × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes and D the four canonical dimensions plus each custom name the config's `reviewDimensions` list adds, each counted once, and the seed step prints the derived budget. Since D is never below four, the ceiling of 24 binds from the first seed, so one run cannot fund every node at every depth of a wide review; split a wide review with fan-out, where each lineage with no matrix `iterations` value sizes its own budget from its share of the seed, with D fixed at the canonical four because a lineage reviews only those. A lineage dealt no seed node, or a run whose seeds were all pruned, runs at its loop default instead: 12 iterations for a native lineage and 7 for a CLI one or a single run. The node cap stays half the budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. At about seven to eight minutes an iteration, a 24-iteration review can reach `maxDurationMinutes` (120) before its iteration cap. A fan-out parent seeds before any config exists, so its cap falls back to 10. The mode is locked against the optimizer; the `expansiveDepth` block is in neither its tunable nor its locked list. An absent flag means `default`, which runs exactly as before.\n107:After the review floor, an expansive run that still holds an open or active node turns a stop candidate into `CONTINUE` with reasonDetail `frontierOpen`, whichever candidate it was, `all_dimensions_clean` or a composite convergence vote. The veto never creates a stop of its own and never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off`, `--stop-policy=max-iterations` or the `minIterations` floor. Under stuck recovery the handler closes the active node as `exhausted` with reason `stuck`, so a node the run cannot fund stops holding the veto open.\n109:When the frontier holds at least one answered node and none is open or active, and neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite vote forms, an expansive run gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It ranks after the other two, so the floor, the legal-stop gates and the graph decision run on it as on any candidate: a failed gate gives `BLOCKED`, and a stop records `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained`. A fan-out lineage reads only its own partition, so one whose nodes are answered stops rather than running to its cap. A frontier that closed with nothing answered, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate, and a default run never forms it.\n115:Each eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. If that round misses quorum, because a seat fails to return or returns a report that does not parse, the pivot reopens once as attempt 2 with three fresh seat outputs. A second quorum miss, or three valid seats that do not agree, fails the pivot closed. `maxCouncilSeatOutputs` caps one council attempt at 3 seat outputs, so a pivot records at most 6. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n183:6. **Stop candidate** -- all dimensions covered and clean (every configured dimension covered, the four by default, no active P0/P1, coverage stabilized) is a hard candidate; otherwise the 3-signal composite vote with threshold 0.60 is a soft one. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a frontier with at least one answered node and none open or active is a third, hard candidate (`frontier_drained`) when neither forms. No candidate returns `CONTINUE` (`noStopCandidate`).\n185:8. **Frontier veto** -- under `--depth-mode=expansive`, an open or active frontier node turns the candidate into `CONTINUE` (`frontierOpen`).\n===node status reducer===\n1950:    if (record.frontierNodeId === nodeId) return true;\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"frontier\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md | head -30; echo \\\"===node status reducer===\\\"; grep -n \\\"frontierNodeId\\\\|frontier_node\\\\|nodeStatus\\\\|status.*closed\\\\|dimensionsCovered\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115194112,"end":1795115194397}}}}
