{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115245823,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f534deb1001iwQdpqEMM77JCZ","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f534bf1c0019XUR5Rm2UzuZx0","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2e3d69105ca08dc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"frontier_drained\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:73:| AC-018 | REQ-017 | Given an expansive review whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none open or active and that forms no other candidate, When `convergence.cjs` decides, Then it stops `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained` when every gate passes and the graph allows it, is `BLOCKED` on a failed gate, continues with an open node, forms no candidate under default or absent depth mode or when nothing was answered, and never outranks the cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, `off`, `max-iterations` or the floor | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run tests/unit/stop-decision.vitest.ts -t frontier_drained` exits 0. Observed 2026-11-18: 7 of 18 cases red before the candidate existed, all 18 green after commit `d68f9261a5c`; the answered-node cases (nothing answered, no answered count, the `frontierAnswered` fact) red first and green after commit `c22146e2543`, 21 cases in all; the golden review and research suites stay green | Met | - |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:43:| Q007 | Keep frontier_drained as a hard stop candidate (D-011-07); every quality gate and the graph decision still apply. | Not stated. A soft candidate could never add a stop, since the composite candidate forms at the score the convergence gate needs. | None | D-011-07, REQ-017 |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:65:| D-011-07 | `frontier_drained` is a hard candidate (`hardStop: true`), so `convergenceGate` passes on it as it does on `all_dimensions_clean`; the other eight gates and the graph decision still apply. | A soft candidate passes `convergenceGate` only at a weighted score of 0.60 or more, and the review composite vote forms its own candidate at that same score, so a soft drained candidate could never add a stop. Made under the operator's option-3 ruling of 2026-11-18 (Q003); the operator may veto it. | Set `hardStop: false` on the `frontier_drained` candidate in `buildStopDecision` in `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`; the candidate then never stops a run the composite vote would not. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:181:The lineage-graph fix and the gated frontier_drained candidate are committed (full suite: 3414 passed, 0 failed). A replay still predicts 3 of 6 review pilot lineages cap-stopping. The graph decision stays CONTINUE because evidence density is 0: the standard graph upsert never creates EVIDENCE_FOR links (only pi-3's leaf sent any). pi-2 and pi-6 are also blocked by real findings (an active P0, partial spec_code traceability). How do I close AC-011?\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:201:The agent made frontier_drained a HARD stop candidate (like all_dimensions_clean), so it skips the convergence-score gate but still faces all nine quality gates and the graph decision. A soft one could never add a stop, because the composite candidate already forms at the score the gate needs. Keep it hard?\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:303:- Under the flag, a frontier with at least one node and none open or active forms the hard candidate `frontier_drained` when neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite vote forms (REQ-017). It is hard because a soft candidate passes `convergenceGate` only at a weighted score of 0.60 or more, where the composite vote has already formed a candidate (D-011-07). The other eight gates and the graph decision still decide it.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:306:- A drained lineage with clean gates and a graph that allows the stop now stops before its cap with `converged` and reasonDetail `frontier_drained`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:312:- A soft `frontier_drained` candidate: it adds no stop the composite vote does not already give.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:314:**Amendment, 2026-11-18 (evidence edges)**: The operator kept `frontier_drained` as a hard candidate (D-011-07) and ruled that the review graph upsert derive evidence edges before the pilot rerun (REQ-018, D-011-09). A replay with a rebuilt graph had shown pi-5 forming `all_dimensions_clean` with all nine gates passing and the graph decision still `CONTINUE`, because evidence density was 0: the canonical projection made no `EVIDENCE_FOR` edge, and only pi-3's leaf sent any. With the edges derived from each finding's `file:line` ref, the same replay gives pi-5 `STOP converged all_dimensions_clean` at iteration 5 with the graph at `STOP_ALLOWED`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:316:**Amendment, 2026-11-18 (independent review)**: An independent review asked for six code changes and two spec notes, fixed under T035. A leaf finding id now folds the same way in every iteration and only finding endpoints move. A colliding id of another file and title keeps its own node, and only a `file:line` ref earns an edge. Skipped orphan edges are named on stderr for every loop type. `frontier_drained` now needs at least one `answered` node, so a frontier that closed with nothing answered no longer stops as `converged`; it stays a hard candidate (D-011-07). Depth-1 seeds answer only to the root-children cap. Lineage graph stores are gitignored. The `findingStability` effect is named in REQ-018 and D-011-09, and the `maxFrontierNodes: null` default config value is named as an inert default-run byte change in this spec and in phase 010's.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:110:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | Modify | Apply the existing `frontierOpen` veto to review stop candidates (`all_dimensions_clean`, composite), after the review floor that 003 adds; add the review `frontierTotal` fact and the expansive `frontier_drained` candidate (REQ-017) |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:155:| REQ-017 | Under the flag, a review run whose frontier holds at least one node and none open or active, and which forms neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite candidate, gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It never outranks the cap, failures, stuck recovery, `off`, `max-iterations` or the floor, every legal-stop gate and the graph decision still decide it, and a default run never forms it (plan ADR-006, decision-record Q003). A frontier that closed with no `answered` node, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md:100:- [x] T033 Add the expansive review candidate `frontier_drained` behind every legal-stop gate, plan ADR-006 under decision-record Q003 and the operator's option-3 ruling of 2026-11-18 (`$D/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`, the `step_check_convergence` order in `deep-review.yaml`, the review reference docs). Verify: `$R tests/unit/stop-decision.vitest.ts -t frontier_drained` exits 0. Red first: 7 of 18 cases failed (the stop, three gate blocks, the floor, the graph-continue case and the `frontierTotal` fact) before the candidate existed; green after. Cases cover a drained lineage with passing gates that stops `converged`/`frontier_drained`, BLOCKED on `hotspotSaturationGate`, `p0ResolutionGate` and `dimensionCoverageGate`, an open node that continues, an empty or uncounted partition, default and absent depth mode with no candidate, and the cap, floor, stuck recovery, `off` and `max-iterations` still winning. The hard-stop choice is D-011-07. Full runtime suite after both tasks: 190 files, 3414 passed, 11 skipped, 0 failed; `check-contract-drift.cjs` prints OK commands=2. AC-011 and the pilot criterion stay open until a live pilot rerun.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:73:| AC-018 | REQ-017 | Given an expansive review whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none open or active and that forms no other candidate, When `convergence.cjs` decides, Then it stops `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained` when every gate passes and the graph allows it, is `BLOCKED` on a failed gate, continues with an open node, forms no candidate under default or absent depth mode or when nothing was answered, and never outranks the cap, consecutive failures, stuck recovery, `off`, `max-iterations` or the floor | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run tests/unit/stop-decision.vitest.ts -t frontier_drained` exits 0. Observed 2026-11-18: 7 of 18 cases red before the candidate existed, all 18 green after commit `d68f9261a5c`; the answered-node cases (nothing answered, no answered count, the `frontierAnswered` fact) red first and green after commit `c22146e2543`, 21 cases in all; the golden review and research suites stay green | Met | - |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:43:| Q007 | Keep frontier_drained as a hard stop candidate (D-011-07); every quality gate and the graph decision still apply. | Not stated. A soft candidate could never add a stop, since the composite candidate forms at the score the convergence gate needs. | None | D-011-07, REQ-017 |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:65:| D-011-07 | `frontier_drained` is a hard candidate (`hardStop: true`), so `convergenceGate` passes on it as it does on `all_dimensions_clean`; the other eight gates and the graph decision still apply. | A soft candidate passes `convergenceGate` only at a weighted score of 0.60 or more, and the review composite vote forms its own candidate at that same score, so a soft drained candidate could never add a stop. Made under the operator's option-3 ruling of 2026-11-18 (Q003); the operator may veto it. | Set `hardStop: false` on the `frontier_drained` candidate in `buildStopDecision` in `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`; the candidate then never stops a run the composite vote would not. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:181:The lineage-graph fix and the gated frontier_drained candidate are committed (full suite: 3414 passed, 0 failed). A replay still predicts 3 of 6 review pilot lineages cap-stopping. The graph decision stays CONTINUE because evidence density is 0: the standard graph upsert never creates EVIDENCE_FOR links (only pi-3's leaf sent any). pi-2 and pi-6 are also blocked by real findings (an active P0, partial spec_code traceability). How do I close AC-011?\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:201:The agent made frontier_drained a HARD stop candidate (like all_dimensions_clean), so it skips the convergence-score gate but still faces all nine quality gates and the graph decision. A soft one could never add a stop, because the composite candidate already forms at the score the gate needs. Keep it hard?\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:303:- Under the flag, a frontier with at least one node and none open or active forms the hard candidate `frontier_drained` when neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite vote forms (REQ-017). It is hard because a soft candidate passes `convergenceGate` only at a weighted score of 0.60 or more, where the composite vote has already formed a candidate (D-011-07). The other eight gates and the graph decision still decide it.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:306:- A drained lineage with clean gates and a graph that allows the stop now stops before its cap with `converged` and reasonDetail `frontier_drained`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:312:- A soft `frontier_drained` candidate: it adds no stop the composite vote does not already give.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:314:**Amendment, 2026-11-18 (evidence edges)**: The operator kept `frontier_drained` as a hard candidate (D-011-07) and ruled that the review graph upsert derive evidence edges before the pilot rerun (REQ-018, D-011-09). A replay with a rebuilt graph had shown pi-5 forming `all_dimensions_clean` with all nine gates passing and the graph decision still `CONTINUE`, because evidence density was 0: the canonical projection made no `EVIDENCE_FOR` edge, and only pi-3's leaf sent any. With the edges derived from each finding's `file:line` ref, the same replay gives pi-5 `STOP converged all_dimensions_clean` at iteration 5 with the graph at `STOP_ALLOWED`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:316:**Amendment, 2026-11-18 (independent review)**: An independent review asked for six code changes and two spec notes, fixed under T035. A leaf finding id now folds the same way in every iteration and only finding endpoints move. A colliding id of another file and title keeps its own node, and only a `file:line` ref earns an edge. Skipped orphan edges are named on stderr for every loop type. `frontier_drained` now needs at least one `answered` node, so a frontier that closed with nothing answered no longer stops as `converged`; it stays a hard candidate (D-011-07). Depth-1 seeds answer only to the root-children cap. Lineage graph stores are gitignored. The `findingStability` effect is named in REQ-018 and D-011-09, and the `maxFrontierNodes: null` default config value is named as an inert default-run byte change in this spec and in phase 010's.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:110:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | Modify | Apply the existing `frontierOpen` veto to review stop candidates (`all_dimensions_clean`, composite), after the review floor that 003 adds; add the review `frontierTotal` fact and the expansive `frontier_drained` candidate (REQ-017) |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:155:| REQ-017 | Under the flag, a review run whose frontier holds at least one node and none open or active, and which forms neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite candidate, gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It never outranks the cap, failures, stuck recovery, `off`, `max-iterations` or the floor, every legal-stop gate and the graph decision still decide it, and a default run never forms it (plan ADR-006, decision-record Q003). A frontier that closed with no `answered` node, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md:100:- [x] T033 Add the expansive review candidate `frontier_drained` behind every legal-stop gate, plan ADR-006 under decision-record Q003 and the operator's option-3 ruling of 2026-11-18 (`$D/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`, the `step_check_convergence` order in `deep-review.yaml`, the review reference docs). Verify: `$R tests/unit/stop-decision.vitest.ts -t frontier_drained` exits 0. Red first: 7 of 18 cases failed (the stop, three gate blocks, the floor, the graph-continue case and the `frontierTotal` fact) before the candidate existed; green after. Cases cover a drained lineage with passing gates that stops `converged`/`frontier_drained`, BLOCKED on `hotspotSaturationGate`, `p0ResolutionGate` and `dimensionCoverageGate`, an open node that continues, an empty or uncounted partition, default and absent depth mode with no candidate, and the cap, floor, stuck recovery, `off` and `max-iterations` still winning. The hard-stop choice is D-011-07. Full runtime suite after both tasks: 190 files, 3414 passed, 11 skipped, 0 failed; `check-contract-drift.cjs` prints OK commands=2. AC-011 and the pilot criterion stay open until a live pilot rerun.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"frontier_drained\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115245233,"end":1795115245823}}}}
