{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795115290288,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f5358eb0001MDYMzckEF2TCIU","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53589a4001Irv157WTbhV4cY","type":"step-start","snapshot":"db43e84491fe96cf91a60802616f32522445bb9c"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115292636,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5359523001c6dFSLEbaNhT4Z","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53589a4001Irv157WTbhV4cY","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-800975ed05a4a2c6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"extend\\|extended\\|continuedFromRun\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -40"},"output":"58:  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart|completed-continue] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive), `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived) and `completed-continue` (from --extend=N: a completed run extended in place by N iterations, same sessionId and generation). `fork` is not accepted. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n59:  extend: \"[EXTEND] - Positive integer N from --extend=N. Sets lineage_mode to completed-continue and adds N iterations to a completed run. Default: unset.\"\n60:  extend_minutes: \"[EXTEND_MINUTES] - Positive integer M from --extend-minutes=M, the minutes an extension adds to the later of the prior maxDurationMinutes and the minutes already elapsed since createdAt. Only valid with --extend. Default: unset, which adds the prior maxDurationMinutes, and a run with no duration budget keeps none.\"\n311:  step_reject_extend_with_fanout:\n312:    description: \"Refuse --extend on a fan-out config before any lineage spawns\"\n321:    message: \"Usage error (extend-with-fanout): --extend extends a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n425:          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n514:      step_extend_completed_run:\n519:          --extend=N continues a finished run in the same session and generation. The\n527:          WORK_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-extend.XXXXXX\")\"\n530:            const [configPath, stateLogPath, extendRaw, extendMinutesRaw, workDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n534:            if (!/^[1-9][0-9]*$/.test(String(extendRaw))) {\n535:              fail(\"--extend needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(String(extendRaw)) + \".\");\n537:            const minutesRaw = String(extendMinutesRaw);\n539:              fail(\"--extend-minutes needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(minutesRaw) + \".\");\n542:              fail(\"--extend needs a completed run, and this run has status \" + config.status + \". Use --lineage-mode=resume to continue an unfinished run.\");\n551:            const continuedFromRun = new Set(rows\n555:            const addedIterations = Number(extendRaw);\n563:            const hasMinutes = /^[1-9][0-9]*$/.test(String(extendMinutesRaw));\n564:            const addedMinutes = hasMinutes ? Number(extendMinutesRaw) : priorMaxDurationMinutes;\n565:            // A run with no duration budget keeps none unless --extend-minutes asks for one.\n569:            const newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + addedIterations;\n573:              stem: \"deep_review.run_extended\",\n577:                continuedFromRun,\n594:              continuedFromRun,\n607:              ? \"This run stops on convergence, so it may re-stop on all_dimensions_clean right away. An extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode it was created with, and a flag passed beside --extend does not change them, so only a run created with --convergence-mode=off is sure to use the new budget.\"\n609:            console.log(JSON.stringify({ continuedFromRun, newMaxIterations, newMaxDurationMinutes, warning }));\n610:          ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \"{extend}\" \"{extend_minutes}\" \"$WORK_DIR\" > \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\" || { STATUS=$?; rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit \"$STATUS\"; }\n616:          - continued_from_run: \"continuedFromRun from the JSON output\"\n623:      step_snapshot_extended_review_report:\n637:        note: \"Keyed by generation and continuedFromRun, so a second extension of the same generation writes its own snapshot.\"\n652:        extension_rule: \"When extension_pending == true, step_extend_completed_run has just set status initialized and appended run_extended, so a synthesis_complete row followed by an extended row is consistent: classify as resume, never as invalid-state or completed-session.\"\n662:          append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n663:          extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, skip this append_jsonl: step_extend_completed_run already recorded the lifecycle action as run_extended, so the ledger carries one event per action. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to phase_loop.\"\n678:              append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n680:              extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, do not set lineage_mode to resume and do not append the resumed row, because run_extended already records this extension. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to gate_init_approval.\"\n734:        note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n888:          continuedFromRun: null\n1032:        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n2440:          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: a `completed-continue` extension keeps the prior review report as `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. See `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"58:  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart|completed-continue] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive), `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived) and `completed-continue` (from --extend=N: a completed run extended in place by N iterations, same sessionId and generation). `fork` is not accepted. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n59:  extend: \"[EXTEND] - Positive integer N from --extend=N. Sets lineage_mode to completed-continue and adds N iterations to a completed run. Default: unset.\"\n60:  extend_minutes: \"[EXTEND_MINUTES] - Positive integer M from --extend-minutes=M, the minutes an extension adds to the later of the prior maxDurationMinutes and the minutes already elapsed since createdAt. Only valid with --extend. Default: unset, which adds the prior maxDurationMinutes, and a run with no duration budget keeps none.\"\n311:  step_reject_extend_with_fanout:\n312:    description: \"Refuse --extend on a fan-out config before any lineage spawns\"\n321:    message: \"Usage error (extend-with-fanout): --extend extends a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n425:          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n514:      step_extend_completed_run:\n519:          --extend=N continues a finished run in the same session and generation. The\n527:          WORK_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-extend.XXXXXX\")\"\n530:            const [configPath, stateLogPath, extendRaw, extendMinutesRaw, workDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n534:            if (!/^[1-9][0-9]*$/.test(String(extendRaw))) {\n535:              fail(\"--extend needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(String(extendRaw)) + \".\");\n537:            const minutesRaw = String(extendMinutesRaw);\n539:              fail(\"--extend-minutes needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(minutesRaw) + \".\");\n542:              fail(\"--extend needs a completed run, and this run has status \" + config.status + \". Use --lineage-mode=resume to continue an unfinished run.\");\n551:            const continuedFromRun = new Set(rows\n555:            const addedIterations = Number(extendRaw);\n563:            const hasMinutes = /^[1-9][0-9]*$/.test(String(extendMinutesRaw));\n564:            const addedMinutes = hasMinutes ? Number(extendMinutesRaw) : priorMaxDurationMinutes;\n565:            // A run with no duration budget keeps none unless --extend-minutes asks for one.\n569:            const newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + addedIterations;\n573:              stem: \"deep_review.run_extended\",\n577:                continuedFromRun,\n594:              continuedFromRun,\n607:              ? \"This run stops on convergence, so it may re-stop on all_dimensions_clean right away. An extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode it was created with, and a flag passed beside --extend does not change them, so only a run created with --convergence-mode=off is sure to use the new budget.\"\n609:            console.log(JSON.stringify({ continuedFromRun, newMaxIterations, newMaxDurationMinutes, warning }));\n610:          ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \"{extend}\" \"{extend_minutes}\" \"$WORK_DIR\" > \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\" || { STATUS=$?; rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit \"$STATUS\"; }\n616:          - continued_from_run: \"continuedFromRun from the JSON output\"\n623:      step_snapshot_extended_review_report:\n637:        note: \"Keyed by generation and continuedFromRun, so a second extension of the same generation writes its own snapshot.\"\n652:        extension_rule: \"When extension_pending == true, step_extend_completed_run has just set status initialized and appended run_extended, so a synthesis_complete row followed by an extended row is consistent: classify as resume, never as invalid-state or completed-session.\"\n662:          append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n663:          extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, skip this append_jsonl: step_extend_completed_run already recorded the lifecycle action as run_extended, so the ledger carries one event per action. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to phase_loop.\"\n678:              append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n680:              extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, do not set lineage_mode to resume and do not append the resumed row, because run_extended already records this extension. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to gate_init_approval.\"\n734:        note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n888:          continuedFromRun: null\n1032:        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n2440:          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: a `completed-continue` extension keeps the prior review report as `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. See `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"extend\\\\|extended\\\\|continuedFromRun\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115291939,"end":1795115292636}}}}
