{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115301042,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f535b554002XvHcI67fWYtuJX","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f535a72f001T8Vvvo3HHsbCVE","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-86a32309c4bac04b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"extend\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/ --include=*.md | grep -i \"maxIterations\\|priorMaxIterations\\|adds N\\|budget\" | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:53:4. **It designed completed-run extension, which the operator asked to have built.** It adopts the reserved `completed-continue` lineage mode, spelled `--extend=N`, with a new `run_extended` ledger event. The run keeps its session and generation, and the duration budget is raised rather than resetting `createdAt`. Corrected after independent review: the new ceiling must be computed from elapsed time, `max(priorMaxDurationMinutes, elapsedMinutesAtExtension) + M`. The duration check counts idle wall-clock time since `createdAt`, so a plain `+= M` stops any extension started later than the old budget before its first dispatch (§19 item 4).\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:365:| `maxIterations += N` as the extension iteration rule | A run that converged at 7 of 10 would get 6 more iterations for `--extend=3`; use `continuedFromRun + N` | convergence.cjs:1115 | review |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:525:   - M defaults to the prior budget when `--extend-minutes` is omitted;\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:538:     - `maxIterations = continuedFromRun + N`, so `--extend=3` on a run that stopped at 7 of 10 gives 3 more iterations, not 6. Here `continuedFromRun` must be the count the cap uses: every `type: iteration` row, one per iteration number, error and timeout rows included. If it counted only completed iterations, `--extend=N` would yield fewer than N; [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1270]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:556:| **A** | Completed-run extension: `completed-continue` / `--extend=N` (§19) | `commands/deep/{research,review}.md` (`--lineage-mode` rows); both YAMLs (lineage param, `note_deferred_branches`, locked pre-classify step, `on_resume` event choice, snapshot step); both ledger schemas and types, and the stem-producer tables; `legacy-compatibility.ts`; both typed reducers (`deep-research-reducers/`, `deep-review-reducers/`); both legacy projections (`legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts`, `deep-review-state-contract.ts`); both `reduce-state.cjs` (lifecycle filters, review `LIVE_LINEAGE_MODES`); config assets (research `lineage` lists, review flat fields); docs that call the mode deferred: both `loop-protocol.md`, `review-mode-contract.yaml`, review `state-format.md`, both quick references, research `SKILL.md` and strategy asset, both agent definitions | `workflow-restart-lifecycle`, `deep-review-auto-restart-contract`, ledger-schema and upcast suites, `append-mode-event-legacy-seam`, reducer Lifecycle-section parity, double-terminal telemetry, a `run_extended` projection case, a duration-ceiling case (extension started after the old budget), playbook entry. Two `system-spec-kit` assertions break and must change with the wording: `deep-review-contract-parity.vitest.ts:126` and `deep-review-reducer-schema.vitest.ts:120-121`. The assertions that the docs mention `completed-continue` survive, because the name stays. | LOW for default runs (opt-in), but it touches shared reducers and projections; a stem missing from a projection fails silently, so the projection case is required | none |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-5.md:16:Next focus: Q5 (final iteration): turn generation-1 recommendations plus this generation's findings (iterations 1-4: corrected D1-D9, pivot yield and D1 fix, review-side findings, completed-run extension design) into concrete, independently shippable change slices. For each slice: files, behavior change, tests that prove it (existing and new), default-path risk, ordering dependencies. Put the completed-run extension (--extend=N / completed-continue) as its own slice early, since the operator wants it built first. If budget remains, note what Q4 (skill-advisor scorer and prompt-policy gate on casual chat) still needs.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-5.md:20:Focus Area: Q5 (final iteration): turn generation-1 recommendations plus this generation's findings (iterations 1-4: corrected D1-D9, pivot yield and D1 fix, review-side findings, completed-run extension design) into concrete, independently shippable change slices. For each slice: files, behavior change, tests that prove it (existing and new), default-path risk, ordering dependencies. Put the completed-run extension (--extend=N / completed-continue) as its own slice early, since the operator wants it built first. If budget remains, note what Q4 (skill-advisor scorer and prompt-policy gate on casual chat) still needs.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:16:Next focus: Q6 (primary): design completed-run extension for deep-research and deep-review. Trace step_classify_session on_completed_session, the deferred completed-continue lineage mode (config allowedModes/deferredModes, loop-protocol.md Lifecycle Branch Contract), step_apply_lifecycle_request and the ledger stems; specify an in-place extension (completed-continue or --extend=N): config fields that change, the ledger event that records it, how reducer, minIterations floor, max-duration clock and synthesis treat pre- and post-extension iterations, and the files and tests that change. Q4 (secondary, only with remaining budget): what the skill-advisor scorer (df-idf.ts) and prompt-policy gate do with casual chat prompts.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:20:Focus Area: Q6 (primary): design completed-run extension for deep-research and deep-review. Trace step_classify_session on_completed_session, the deferred completed-continue lineage mode (config allowedModes/deferredModes, loop-protocol.md Lifecycle Branch Contract), step_apply_lifecycle_request and the ledger stems; specify an in-place extension (completed-continue or --extend=N): config fields that change, the ledger event that records it, how reducer, minIterations floor, max-duration clock and synthesis treat pre- and post-extension iterations, and the files and tests that change. Q4 (secondary, only with remaining budget): what the skill-advisor scorer (df-idf.ts) and prompt-policy gate do with casual chat prompts.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-002.md:17:2. **An accepted pivot buys `min(maxIterations − triggerIteration, remaining pivot budget)` iterations — not \"about one\".** The corrected mechanics: a pivot converts a STOP into CONTINUE; it never extends `maxIterations`, and the cap at `convergence.cjs:1115` is evaluated before the pivot-eligible reasons and is excluded from pivoting (yaml:1061). On success the workflow sets `next_focus` to `restoredFocus`, re-runs the reducer, and proceeds to `step_rejected_pattern_cache` → the next iteration dispatches (yaml:1163–1169). Because the pivot re-picks focus from *existing* state and never adds questions to the registry, `all_questions_answered` stays true forever after it first fires — **every subsequent stop consumes another pivot**. The lifetime budget is `maxPivots: 3` (`divergent-pivot.ts:285`; refusal `max_pivots_exceeded` at :733) and `maxCouncilSeatOutputs: 9` (:286) caps total seat dispatches across all pivots — three pivots × three seats exactly saturates it, so a resumed pivot silently eats lifetime budget. `minRemainingIterations: 1` (:287, enforced :739) is nearly dead code: `remainingIterations == 0` means `iterationCount >= maxIterations`, which the cap catches earlier at :1115 — prepare never sees it. Generation 1's \"buys only about one iteration\" is **wrong as a general claim**; it holds only in the corner where the trigger lands at `maxIterations − 1`. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1163-1169] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:285-288,733,739] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1115,1149-1150]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-005.md:20:- Behavior: `--extend=N [--extend-minutes=M]` on a completed packet mutates config in place (status→active, `maxIterations += N`, `maxDurationMinutes += M`, `lineage.continuedFromRun = <completed count>`), appends `run_extended` through the gateway, and classify lands `resume` on next entry. Never re-stamp `createdAt`. Edge contract: under `stopPolicy:convergence` an extension with no new questions re-stops on `all_questions_answered`; document coupling to inbox injection or `--convergence-mode=off` for the extension window. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1766-1771; .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1149]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:20:2. **A confirm-mode extension path already exists inside the loop — the design only needs to extend it past `status:\"complete\"`.** `gate_pre_synthesis.on_B` = \"Run more iterations (increase max)… raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again\" → `phase_loop` (`deep-research.yaml:1766-1771`, mirrored at `deep-review.yaml:1878-1883`). This proves two things: the workflow already treats `maxIterations`/`maxDurationMinutes` as mutable despite `fileProtection.\"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\"` (config field protection binds the LEAF and the optimizer `_optimizerManaged.lockedFields`, not the workflow itself — `step_update_config_status` already `edit`s the config), and the workflow already knows the duration clock must be raised alongside the iteration budget. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1766-1771,1923-1927; .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1883; research config fileProtection block]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:30:7. **Recommended event+config shape.** Record through the gateway a new stem `deep_research.run_extended` / `deep_review.run_extended` (mirroring `run_resumed` fields: `priorTailDigest`, `sourceLineageId`=same sessionId, `generation`=same, `continuedFromRun`=completed iteration count, plus `extension:{addedIterations, priorMaxIterations, newMaxIterations, priorMaxDurationMinutes, newMaxDurationMinutes, priorStatus:\"complete\"}`). Config mutation, same sessionId/generation/createdAt: `status:\"complete\"`→`\"active\"` (any value ≠ `complete` so next classify lands `resume`); `maxIterations += N` (cumulative — convergence counts all rows); `maxDurationMinutes += M`; `lineage.continuedFromRun = <count>`; optional `lineage.extensionCount += 1`. Placement: extend `step_apply_lifecycle_request`-adjacent processing BEFORE `step_classify_session` (pre-classify mutation makes classify land `resume` naturally), or add an `on_completed_continue` classify branch — the pre-classify mutation is the smaller diff but the distinct event must still be appended through the gateway so the dashboard Lifecycle section can show the top-up. `lifecycle-taxonomy.cjs` needs no change (extension is not a STOP_REASONS value). [INFERENCE: based on findings 1-6]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/implementation-summary.md:60:`/deep:research --extend=N` and `/deep:review --extend=N` now reopen a completed run in the same session and generation. Under the loop lock and before classification, a new step counts the runs so far, sets `maxIterations` to that count plus N, and sets `maxDurationMinutes` to `max(prior budget, minutes since createdAt) + M`. It appends a `run_extended` ledger event through the gateway, and only then writes the config back with status `initialized` and lineage mode `completed-continue`. Classification then lands on resume, writes no `resumed` row, and the run continues. Before the first new dispatch the prior synthesis or review report is copied to `synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` or `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`, and an existing snapshot is never overwritten.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/implementation-summary.md:68:| `runtime/lib/deep-{research,review}-ledger-schema/*-schema.ts`, `*-types.ts` | Modified | `run_extended` stem per loop, the `extension-budget` field kind, payload types, producer rows (`spoken`) |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/implementation-summary.md:69:| `runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/legacy-compatibility.ts` | Modified | Upcasts a legacy `extended` row and refuses one without a full budget |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/acceptance-criteria.md:57:| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given a fixture run that stopped at 7 of 10 iterations, including one error row, When `--extend=3` runs, Then `maxIterations` is 10 and the loop dispatches exactly 3 more iterations | Met 2026-11-17. Cap half: 7 runs with one error row plus `--extend=3` give `maxIterations` 10 (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:807`). Dispatch half: the DR-065 live walk extended a completed 2-iteration run by 3 and dispatched exactly 3 iterations (receipts i3-i5, none duplicated), with one `run_extended` ledger event, no `resumed` row, the same sessionId and generation, and snapshot `synthesis-v1-r2.md` (`scratch/dr-065-walk.md`) | Met | - |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/acceptance-criteria.md:58:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given a fixture whose `createdAt` is 300 minutes old with a prior budget of 120, When `--extend=2` runs with no `--extend-minutes`, Then `maxDurationMinutes` is 420 (300 + 120), `step_check_max_duration` reports `reached == false` and the first extension iteration dispatches | duration case with `createdAt` 300 minutes old and a 120-minute budget: `step_check_max_duration` reports `reached: true` before, `maxDurationMinutes >= 420` after with no `--extend-minutes`, and `reached: false` after. Uses `--extend=3`; the minute rule does not depend on N. Cites `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:807` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/tasks.md:47:- [x] T005 Add the `deep_research.run_extended` stem with its payload fields and a stem-producer table row marked `spoken` with `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml` as producer (`$S/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/deep-research-ledger-schema.ts`, `deep-research-ledger-types.ts`). Verify: `rg -n 'run_extended' $S/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema` prints the schema, type and producer-table lines. Done 2026-11-17 (Pi dispatch): schema rule, `extension-budget` field kind, scope row, types and `spoken` producer row; the grep prints all lines.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/tasks.md:49:- [x] T007 Add the legacy `run_extended` row upcast (`$S/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/legacy-compatibility.ts`). Verify: the upcast case for a legacy `extended` row passes under `cd $S/runtime && npx vitest run tests/unit/deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts`. Done 2026-11-17 (Pi dispatch plus a native fixture row): legacy `extended` row upcasts, a row without a full budget is refused (`run-extended-budget-missing`); `deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts` and `deep-review-ledger-schema.vitest.ts` pass 76 of 76.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:53:4. **It designed completed-run extension, which the operator asked to have built.** It adopts the reserved `completed-continue` lineage mode, spelled `--extend=N`, with a new `run_extended` ledger event. The run keeps its session and generation, and the duration budget is raised rather than resetting `createdAt`. Corrected after independent review: the new ceiling must be computed from elapsed time, `max(priorMaxDurationMinutes, elapsedMinutesAtExtension) + M`. The duration check counts idle wall-clock time since `createdAt`, so a plain `+= M` stops any extension started later than the old budget before its first dispatch (§19 item 4).\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:365:| `maxIterations += N` as the extension iteration rule | A run that converged at 7 of 10 would get 6 more iterations for `--extend=3`; use `continuedFromRun + N` | convergence.cjs:1115 | review |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:525:   - M defaults to the prior budget when `--extend-minutes` is omitted;\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:538:     - `maxIterations = continuedFromRun + N`, so `--extend=3` on a run that stopped at 7 of 10 gives 3 more iterations, not 6. Here `continuedFromRun` must be the count the cap uses: every `type: iteration` row, one per iteration number, error and timeout rows included. If it counted only completed iterations, `--extend=N` would yield fewer than N; [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1270]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:556:| **A** | Completed-run extension: `completed-continue` / `--extend=N` (§19) | `commands/deep/{research,review}.md` (`--lineage-mode` rows); both YAMLs (lineage param, `note_deferred_branches`, locked pre-classify step, `on_resume` event choice, snapshot step); both ledger schemas and types, and the stem-producer tables; `legacy-compatibility.ts`; both typed reducers (`deep-research-reducers/`, `deep-review-reducers/`); both legacy projections (`legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts`, `deep-review-state-contract.ts`); both `reduce-state.cjs` (lifecycle filters, review `LIVE_LINEAGE_MODES`); config assets (research `lineage` lists, review flat fields); docs that call the mode deferred: both `loop-protocol.md`, `review-mode-contract.yaml`, review `state-format.md`, both quick references, research `SKILL.md` and strategy asset, both agent definitions | `workflow-restart-lifecycle`, `deep-review-auto-restart-contract`, ledger-schema and upcast suites, `append-mode-event-legacy-seam`, reducer Lifecycle-section parity, double-terminal telemetry, a `run_extended` projection case, a duration-ceiling case (extension started after the old budget), playbook entry. Two `system-spec-kit` assertions break and must change with the wording: `deep-review-contract-parity.vitest.ts:126` and `deep-review-reducer-schema.vitest.ts:120-121`. The assertions that the docs mention `completed-continue` survive, because the name stays. | LOW for default runs (opt-in), but it touches shared reducers and projections; a stem missing from a projection fails silently, so the projection case is required | none |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-5.md:16:Next focus: Q5 (final iteration): turn generation-1 recommendations plus this generation's findings (iterations 1-4: corrected D1-D9, pivot yield and D1 fix, review-side findings, completed-run extension design) into concrete, independently shippable change slices. For each slice: files, behavior change, tests that prove it (existing and new), default-path risk, ordering dependencies. Put the completed-run extension (--extend=N / completed-continue) as its own slice early, since the operator wants it built first. If budget remains, note what Q4 (skill-advisor scorer and prompt-policy gate on casual chat) still needs.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-5.md:20:Focus Area: Q5 (final iteration): turn generation-1 recommendations plus this generation's findings (iterations 1-4: corrected D1-D9, pivot yield and D1 fix, review-side findings, completed-run extension design) into concrete, independently shippable change slices. For each slice: files, behavior change, tests that prove it (existing and new), default-path risk, ordering dependencies. Put the completed-run extension (--extend=N / completed-continue) as its own slice early, since the operator wants it built first. If budget remains, note what Q4 (skill-advisor scorer and prompt-policy gate on casual chat) still needs.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:16:Next focus: Q6 (primary): design completed-run extension for deep-research and deep-review. Trace step_classify_session on_completed_session, the deferred completed-continue lineage mode (config allowedModes/deferredModes, loop-protocol.md Lifecycle Branch Contract), step_apply_lifecycle_request and the ledger stems; specify an in-place extension (completed-continue or --extend=N): config fields that change, the ledger event that records it, how reducer, minIterations floor, max-duration clock and synthesis treat pre- and post-extension iterations, and the files and tests that change. Q4 (secondary, only with remaining budget): what the skill-advisor scorer (df-idf.ts) and prompt-policy gate do with casual chat prompts.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:20:Focus Area: Q6 (primary): design completed-run extension for deep-research and deep-review. Trace step_classify_session on_completed_session, the deferred completed-continue lineage mode (config allowedModes/deferredModes, loop-protocol.md Lifecycle Branch Contract), step_apply_lifecycle_request and the ledger stems; specify an in-place extension (completed-continue or --extend=N): config fields that change, the ledger event that records it, how reducer, minIterations floor, max-duration clock and synthesis treat pre- and post-extension iterations, and the files and tests that change. Q4 (secondary, only with remaining budget): what the skill-advisor scorer (df-idf.ts) and prompt-policy gate do with casual chat prompts.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-002.md:17:2. **An accepted pivot buys `min(maxIterations − triggerIteration, remaining pivot budget)` iterations — not \"about one\".** The corrected mechanics: a pivot converts a STOP into CONTINUE; it never extends `maxIterations`, and the cap at `convergence.cjs:1115` is evaluated before the pivot-eligible reasons and is excluded from pivoting (yaml:1061). On success the workflow sets `next_focus` to `restoredFocus`, re-runs the reducer, and proceeds to `step_rejected_pattern_cache` → the next iteration dispatches (yaml:1163–1169). Because the pivot re-picks focus from *existing* state and never adds questions to the registry, `all_questions_answered` stays true forever after it first fires — **every subsequent stop consumes another pivot**. The lifetime budget is `maxPivots: 3` (`divergent-pivot.ts:285`; refusal `max_pivots_exceeded` at :733) and `maxCouncilSeatOutputs: 9` (:286) caps total seat dispatches across all pivots — three pivots × three seats exactly saturates it, so a resumed pivot silently eats lifetime budget. `minRemainingIterations: 1` (:287, enforced :739) is nearly dead code: `remainingIterations == 0` means `iterationCount >= maxIterations`, which the cap catches earlier at :1115 — prepare never sees it. Generation 1's \"buys only about one iteration\" is **wrong as a general claim**; it holds only in the corner where the trigger lands at `maxIterations − 1`. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1163-1169] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:285-288,733,739] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1115,1149-1150]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-005.md:20:- Behavior: `--extend=N [--extend-minutes=M]` on a completed packet mutates config in place (status→active, `maxIterations += N`, `maxDurationMinutes += M`, `lineage.continuedFromRun = <completed count>`), appends `run_extended` through the gateway, and classify lands `resume` on next entry. Never re-stamp `createdAt`. Edge contract: under `stopPolicy:convergence` an extension with no new questions re-stops on `all_questions_answered`; document coupling to inbox injection or `--convergence-mode=off` for the extension window. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1766-1771; .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1149]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:20:2. **A confirm-mode extension path already exists inside the loop — the design only needs to extend it past `status:\"complete\"`.** `gate_pre_synthesis.on_B` = \"Run more iterations (increase max)… raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again\" → `phase_loop` (`deep-research.yaml:1766-1771`, mirrored at `deep-review.yaml:1878-1883`). This proves two things: the workflow already treats `maxIterations`/`maxDurationMinutes` as mutable despite `fileProtection.\"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\"` (config field protection binds the LEAF and the optimizer `_optimizerManaged.lockedFields`, not the workflow itself — `step_update_config_status` already `edit`s the config), and the workflow already knows the duration clock must be raised alongside the iteration budget. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1766-1771,1923-1927; .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1883; research config fileProtection block]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:30:7. **Recommended event+config shape.** Record through the gateway a new stem `deep_research.run_extended` / `deep_review.run_extended` (mirroring `run_resumed` fields: `priorTailDigest`, `sourceLineageId`=same sessionId, `generation`=same, `continuedFromRun`=completed iteration count, plus `extension:{addedIterations, priorMaxIterations, newMaxIterations, priorMaxDurationMinutes, newMaxDurationMinutes, priorStatus:\"complete\"}`). Config mutation, same sessionId/generation/createdAt: `status:\"complete\"`→`\"active\"` (any value ≠ `complete` so next classify lands `resume`); `maxIterations += N` (cumulative — convergence counts all rows); `maxDurationMinutes += M`; `lineage.continuedFromRun = <count>`; optional `lineage.extensionCount += 1`. Placement: extend `step_apply_lifecycle_request`-adjacent processing BEFORE `step_classify_session` (pre-classify mutation makes classify land `resume` naturally), or add an `on_completed_continue` classify branch — the pre-classify mutation is the smaller diff but the distinct event must still be appended through the gateway so the dashboard Lifecycle section can show the top-up. `lifecycle-taxonomy.cjs` needs no change (extension is not a STOP_REASONS value). [INFERENCE: based on findings 1-6]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/implementation-summary.md:60:`/deep:research --extend=N` and `/deep:review --extend=N` now reopen a completed run in the same session and generation. Under the loop lock and before classification, a new step counts the runs so far, sets `maxIterations` to that count plus N, and sets `maxDurationMinutes` to `max(prior budget, minutes since createdAt) + M`. It appends a `run_extended` ledger event through the gateway, and only then writes the config back with status `initialized` and lineage mode `completed-continue`. Classification then lands on resume, writes no `resumed` row, and the run continues. Before the first new dispatch the prior synthesis or review report is copied to `synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` or `review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`, and an existing snapshot is never overwritten.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/implementation-summary.md:68:| `runtime/lib/deep-{research,review}-ledger-schema/*-schema.ts`, `*-types.ts` | Modified | `run_extended` stem per loop, the `extension-budget` field kind, payload types, producer rows (`spoken`) |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/implementation-summary.md:69:| `runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/legacy-compatibility.ts` | Modified | Upcasts a legacy `extended` row and refuses one without a full budget |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/acceptance-criteria.md:57:| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given a fixture run that stopped at 7 of 10 iterations, including one error row, When `--extend=3` runs, Then `maxIterations` is 10 and the loop dispatches exactly 3 more iterations | Met 2026-11-17. Cap half: 7 runs with one error row plus `--extend=3` give `maxIterations` 10 (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:807`). Dispatch half: the DR-065 live walk extended a completed 2-iteration run by 3 and dispatched exactly 3 iterations (receipts i3-i5, none duplicated), with one `run_extended` ledger event, no `resumed` row, the same sessionId and generation, and snapshot `synthesis-v1-r2.md` (`scratch/dr-065-walk.md`) | Met | - |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/acceptance-criteria.md:58:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given a fixture whose `createdAt` is 300 minutes old with a prior budget of 120, When `--extend=2` runs with no `--extend-minutes`, Then `maxDurationMinutes` is 420 (300 + 120), `step_check_max_duration` reports `reached == false` and the first extension iteration dispatches | duration case with `createdAt` 300 minutes old and a 120-minute budget: `step_check_max_duration` reports `reached: true` before, `maxDurationMinutes >= 420` after with no `--extend-minutes`, and `reached: false` after. Uses `--extend=3`; the minute rule does not depend on N. Cites `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:807` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/tasks.md:47:- [x] T005 Add the `deep_research.run_extended` stem with its payload fields and a stem-producer table row marked `spoken` with `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml` as producer (`$S/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/deep-research-ledger-schema.ts`, `deep-research-ledger-types.ts`). Verify: `rg -n 'run_extended' $S/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema` prints the schema, type and producer-table lines. Done 2026-11-17 (Pi dispatch): schema rule, `extension-budget` field kind, scope row, types and `spoken` producer row; the grep prints all lines.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/tasks.md:49:- [x] T007 Add the legacy `run_extended` row upcast (`$S/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/legacy-compatibility.ts`). Verify: the upcast case for a legacy `extended` row passes under `cd $S/runtime && npx vitest run tests/unit/deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts`. Done 2026-11-17 (Pi dispatch plus a native fixture row): legacy `extended` row upcasts, a row without a full budget is refused (`run-extended-budget-missing`); `deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts` and `deep-review-ledger-schema.vitest.ts` pass 76 of 76.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"extend\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/ --include=*.md | grep -i \\\"maxIterations\\\\|priorMaxIterations\\\\|adds N\\\\|budget\\\" | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115300180,"end":1795115301042}}}}
