-reducer.ts:504), so a recorded extension can lower the ceiling or raise it to any uint32. The same gap is in deep-review-ledger-schema.ts:891. Both producers derive newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + addedIterations (deep-research.yaml:522, deep-review.yaml:550). The invariant to enforce is therefore newMaxIterations === continuedFromRun + addedIterations, not priorMaxIterations + addedIterations, which would reject a legitimate extension of a run that stopped before its cap. Kept at P2: the schema comment claims to reject a missing or malformed field and does reject that class. It makes no consistency claim, and the only producers are the workflow YAMLs, so no out-of-contract caller is in reach. Case: a run_extended row with continuedFromRun 4, addedIterations 3, newMaxIterations 1000 validates and projects maxIterations 1000.\",\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/skilled-alignment-run-14/critic.prompt.md:1015:   \"out\": \"consistent ACCEPTED newMaxIterations=7\\nlowered ACCEPTED newMaxIterations=1\\noverextended ACCEPTED newMaxIterations=1000\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-8/report.md:48:- **C1** P2 judgment `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:2612`: The NEVER list forbids `modify_config_after_initialization` outright, but this workflow rewrites the config after init in the two steps this topic adds: `step_extend_completed_run` writes `maxIterations: newMaxIterations` (line 571) and `step_frontier_budget` writes `maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations` (line 950). The runtime then reads the rewritten value: `seedBudget` takes the floor fro...\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-8/report.md:49:  - Evidence: `rg -n \"modify_config_after_initialization|maxIterations: newMaxIterations|maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; rg -n \"Modify config after init\" ....` exit 0: ...ew-config.json` are read-only after initialization. The workflow makes three permitted writes: the terminal `step_update_config_status` flip to `status: complete`, the `--extend=N` rewrite, and `step_frontier_budget` setting `maxIterations` from the seed for an expansive run with a defaulted budget.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-8/report.md:55:- **L2-1** P2 judgment `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:2378`: The NEVER list still forbids `modify_config_after_initialization` outright, but the workflow rewrites the config after init in the two steps this topic adds: `step_extend_completed_run` (line 467) writes `maxIterations: newMaxIterations` and `maxDurationMinutes` (line 548), and `step_frontier_budget` (line 775) writes `maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations` (line 798). The runtime then reads ...\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-8/report.md:56:  - Evidence: `rg -n \"modify_config_after_initialization|step_frontier_budget:|step_extend_completed_run:|maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations|maxIterations: newMaxIterations\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/dee...` exit 0: 467: step_extend_completed_run: 548: maxIterations: newMaxIterations, 775: step_frontier_budget: 798: fs.writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify({ ...config, maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations }, null, 2) + \"\\n\"); 2378: - modify_config_after_initialization\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-8/critic.prompt.md:175:      \"issue\": \"The NEVER list still forbids `modify_config_after_initialization` outright, but the workflow rewrites the config after init in the two steps this topic adds: `step_extend_completed_run` (line 467) writes `maxIterations: newMaxIterations` and `maxDurationMinutes` (line 548), and `step_frontier_budget` (line 775) writes `maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations` (line 798). The runtime then reads the rewritten value: `seedBudget` takes the floor from `config.maxIterations` (frontier-admit.cjs:308) and `convergence.cjs` takes the iteration cap from `config.maxIterations` (convergence.cjs:1397). A reader who follows the rule literally skips both writes, so an expansive run keeps the defaulted budget and an `--extend=N` run keeps its old cap. The same class was already corrected in deep-research/SKILL.md and state-format.md, which now name the three permitted writes.\",\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-8/critic.prompt.md:177:        \"cmd\": \"rg -n \\\"modify_config_after_initialization|step_frontier_budget:|step_extend_completed_run:|maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations|maxIterations: newMaxIterations\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml\",\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-8/critic.prompt.md:179:        \"out\": \"467:      step_extend_completed_run:\\n548:              maxIterations: newMaxIterations,\\n775:      step_frontier_budget:\\n798:              fs.writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify({ ...config, maxIterations: budget.derivedMaxIterations }, null, 2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n2378:    - modify_config_after_initialization\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/doc-alignment-run-6/critic.prompt.md:533:        \"out\": \"567:            const next = {\\n568-              ...config,\\n569-              status: \\\"initialized\\\",\\n570-              maxIterations: newMaxIterations,\\n571-              maxDurationMinutes: newMaxDurationMinutes,\\n572-              lineageMode: \\\"completed-continue\\\",\\n573-              continuedFromRun,\\n574-            };\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/skilled-alignment-run-15/report.md:292:- **A2-3** P2 judgment `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/legacy-compatibility.ts:662`: The new fail-closed branch that refuses a legacy 'extended' row whose extension budget has a missing or non-integer field (reason run-extended-budget-missing) has no test. append-mode-event-legacy-seam.vitest.ts covers only the happy-path upcast of a complete extended row. Case: a legacy extended row without extension.newMaxIterations is never exercised, so a regression that defaulted the ceiling ...\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/skilled-alignment-run-15/report.md:335:- **B4-2** P2 literal `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:57`: The entry claims the schema refuses a run_extended event whose newMaxIterations is not continuedFromRun plus addedIterations, and it states the budget, fan-out refusal and precondition rules. Its Validation table anchors only deep-research-reducers.vitest.ts and the DR-065 playbook. The tests that pin those claims are missing from it: deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts ('refuses an extension wh...\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/014-docs-playbooks-alignment/scratch/skilled-alignment-run-15/fix-plan.md:76:- [ ] B4-2 P2 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:57 The entry claims the schema refuses a run_extended event whose newMaxIterations is not continuedFromRun plus addedIterations, and it states the budget, fan-out refusal and precondition rules. Its Vali\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/research.md:535:     - `extension: {addedIterations, priorMaxIterations, newMaxIterations, priorMaxDurationMinutes, newMaxDurationMinutes, elapsedMinutesAtExtension}`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/iterations/iteration-004.md:30:7. **Recommended event+config shape.** Record through the gateway a new stem `deep_research.run_extended` / `deep_review.run_extended` (mirroring `run_resumed` fields: `priorTailDigest`, `sourceLineageId`=same sessionId, `generation`=same, `continuedFromRun`=completed iteration count, plus `extension:{addedIterations, priorMaxIterations, newMaxIterations, priorMaxDurationMinutes, newMaxDurationMinutes, priorStatus:\"complete\"}`). Config mutation, same sessionId/generation/createdAt: `status:\"complete\"`→`\"active\"` (any value ≠ `complete` so next classify lands `resume`); `maxIterations += N` (cumulative — convergence counts all rows); `maxDurationMinutes += M`; `lineage.continuedFromRun = <count>`; optional `lineage.extensionCount += 1`. Placement: extend `step_apply_lifecycle_request`-adjacent processing BEFORE `step_classify_session` (pre-classify mutation makes classify land `resume` naturally), or add an `on_completed_continue` classify branch — the pre-classify mutation is the smaller diff but the distinct event must still be appended through the gateway so the dashboard Lifecycle section can show the top-up. `lifecycle-taxonomy.cjs` needs no change (extension is not a STOP_REASONS value). [INFERENCE: based on findings 1-6]\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/scratch/drv-070-walk.md:19:Session id `2026-11-17T22:12:11Z` and generation 1 were kept. Extend step output: `{\"continuedFromRun\":2,\"newMaxIterations\":5,\"newMaxDurationMinutes\":240,\"warning\":null}`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/scratch/drv-070-walk.md:46:extended_row={\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"extended\",\"sessionId\":\"2026-11-17T22:12:11Z\",\"generation\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"completed-continue\",\"continuedFromRun\":2,\"extension\":{\"addedIterations\":3,\"elapsedMinutesAtExtension\":12,\"newMaxDurationMinutes\":240,\"newMaxIterations\":5,\"priorMaxDurationMinutes\":120,\"priorMaxIterations\":2},\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-17T22:24:44.560Z\"}\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/scratch/dr-065-walk.md:6:- Extension step output: `{\"continuedFromRun\":2,\"newMaxIterations\":5,\"newMaxDurationMinutes\":240,\"warning\":null}`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/001-completed-run-extension/spec.md:124:| REQ-002 | An extension appends exactly one `deep_research.run_extended` or `deep_review.run_extended` event through the gateway, carrying `priorTailDigest`, the unchanged sessionId and generation, `continuedFromRun`, and `extension: {addedIterations, priorMaxIterations, newMaxIterations, priorMaxDurationMinutes, newMaxDurationMinutes, elapsedMinutesAtExtension}`. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/fable-5-2-review.md:124:19. **`maxIterations += N` over-extends a run that stopped early (§19.6).** A run that converged at 7 of 10 and is extended by 3 gets 6 more iterations. `newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + N` matches what `--extend=N` reads as.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/research-fable-5-2-draft.md:509:     - `extension: {addedIterations, priorMaxIterations, newMaxIterations, priorMaxDurationMinutes, newMaxDurationMinutes}`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/research-fable-5-2-draft.md:523:     - **Iteration budget.** `maxIterations += N` gives a run that converged at 7 of 10 six more iterations for `--extend=3`. `newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + N` matches the flag's meaning.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/opus/containment/baseline/specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T183614Z/iterations/iteration-003.md:73:- Ledger schemas: the per-mode `run_extended` stems and `extension-budget` validators (deep-research-ledger-schema.ts:1087, deep-review-ledger-schema.ts:951) follow the existing per-mode schema architecture, and both YAML steps derive `newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + addedIterations` (deep-review.yaml:568, deep-research.yaml:540), as the schemas require.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/opus/iterations/iteration-002.md:64:- `--extend` arithmetic: `newMaxIterations = distinct iteration count + N`, duration `max(prior, elapsed) + M` (`deep-review.yaml:551-565`), matching `review.md:116-117`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/containment/baseline/specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T183614Z/iterations/iteration-003.md:73:- Ledger schemas: the per-mode `run_extended` stems and `extension-budget` validators (deep-research-ledger-schema.ts:1087, deep-review-ledger-schema.ts:951) follow the existing per-mode schema architecture, and both YAML steps deriv