{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115385674,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f537022e001jEit1zLCNoeWki","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f536f9ad001VjBYopWbSy1laA","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9768e9b33134b0ac","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"derivedFrom\\|findingDetails\\|state-log\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md | head -10"},"output":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md:101:- [x] T034 Derive review evidence edges in the graph upsert, the named defect fix REQ-018 under decision-record Q003 and the operator's ruling of 2026-11-18 (`$D/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`, the review `step_graph_upsert` command and transform in `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml`, the review compiled contract). Verify: `$R tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts tests/unit/stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts` exits 0. Red first: the five evidence cases (edge and density, fold, re-upsert, no ref, undeclared target) failed with exit 3 on the unknown flags and the step case failed on the missing `--state-log`; the pi-5 replay then showed its state record carries no file refs, so a delta-sourced case and the `--delta-dir` step assertion were added and run red before the delta reader existed. The pi-2 replay showed `FIND-` leaf ids diluting the density; that fold form was added to the fold case after the first implementation, so it has no separate red run. Green after commit `7c6a2d9a7e5`. Full runtime suite: 190 files, 3421 passed, 11 skipped, 0 failed. Replays with a rebuilt graph and the derived edges: pi-5 `STOP converged all_dimensions_clean` (graph `STOP_ALLOWED`); pi-2 `BLOCKED` on `dimensionCoverageGate` and `p0ResolutionGate` (graph `STOP_ALLOWED`); pi-6 `BLOCKED` on `dimensionCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` (graph `STOP_ALLOWED`). D-011-09 records the severity, fold and orphan-skip choices.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md:101:- [x] T034 Derive review evidence edges in the graph upsert, the named defect fix REQ-018 under decision-record Q003 and the operator's ruling of 2026-11-18 (`$D/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`, the review `step_graph_upsert` command and transform in `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml`, the review compiled contract). Verify: `$R tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts tests/unit/stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts` exits 0. Red first: the five evidence cases (edge and density, fold, re-upsert, no ref, undeclared target) failed with exit 3 on the unknown flags and the step case failed on the missing `--state-log`; the pi-5 replay then showed its state record carries no file refs, so a delta-sourced case and the `--delta-dir` step assertion were added and run red before the delta reader existed. The pi-2 replay showed `FIND-` leaf ids diluting the density; that fold form was added to the fold case after the first implementation, so it has no separate red run. Green after commit `7c6a2d9a7e5`. Full runtime suite: 190 files, 3421 passed, 11 skipped, 0 failed. Replays with a rebuilt graph and the derived edges: pi-5 `STOP converged all_dimensions_clean` (graph `STOP_ALLOWED`); pi-2 `BLOCKED` on `dimensionCoverageGate` and `p0ResolutionGate` (graph `STOP_ALLOWED`); pi-6 `BLOCKED` on `dimensionCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` (graph `STOP_ALLOWED`). D-011-09 records the severity, fold and orphan-skip choices.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"derivedFrom\\\\|findingDetails\\\\|state-log\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115385390,"end":1795115385674}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115385681,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f536ffa3002itsvzah9v2GOZG","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f536f9ad001VjBYopWbSy1laA","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a78a34f2c207b630","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"EVIDENCE_FOR\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/spec.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/tasks.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/acceptance-criteria.md 2>/dev/null | head -15"},"output":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:156:| REQ-018 | Named defect fix, which also changes default review runs: the review graph upsert derives one FINDING node per finding and one `EVIDENCE_FOR` edge to the FILE node of its `file:line` ref, read from the iteration's delta finding rows and state record, so evidence density no longer depends on the leaf sending graph events. Re-upserting an iteration adds no duplicate node or edge, a finding without a ref adds no edge, a leaf finding node whose id wraps the finding id folds onto the same node, and an edge to a node neither the batch nor the stored graph declares is skipped and reported instead of failing the foreign key (all loop types). The derived FINDING nodes also enter the graph's `findingStability` signal (the share of finding nodes no CONTRADICTS edge touches), which moves in default runs too: a leaf CONTRADICTS edge on a finding now weighs against more finding nodes. Finding ids fold case-insensitively onto this iteration's and the stored findings, an id that collides with a stored finding of another file and title is keyed on the id and the iteration, and only a `file:line` ref earns an edge, with any trailing column dropped. The defect: the canonical projection built no evidence edges, so the pilot lineages whose leaves sent none got a `CONTINUE` graph decision with every legal-stop gate passing. Decision-record Q003 and the operator's ruling of 2026-11-18. Fail-first tests: `upsert-script.vitest.ts` (evidence edge, delta-sourced ref, fold, re-upsert, no ref, undeclared target) and `stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts` (the step passes the state log, delta directory and iteration). |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:74:| AC-019 | REQ-018 | Given a review iteration whose findings carry `file:line` refs in its delta or state record, When `step_graph_upsert` runs `upsert.cjs` with the state log, delta directory and iteration, Then each finding with a ref gets one `EVIDENCE_FOR` edge to a declared FILE node, a re-upsert adds no edge, a finding without a ref adds none, a leaf finding node folds onto the finding it names in any case and in any later iteration while other node kinds keep their edges, a colliding id of another file and title gets its own node, a ref without a line earns no edge, and an edge to an undeclared node is skipped with a stderr notice and no foreign-key failure for every loop type | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts tests/unit/stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts` exits 0. Observed 2026-11-18: the six evidence cases and the step case red first, green after commit `7c6a2d9a7e5`; the review follow-up cases (lowercase fold, a later RESOLVES edge, a non-finding `finding-` id, a colliding id, a ref without a line, research and context orphan edges) red first and green after commit `c22146e2543`; full runtime suite 190 files, 3432 passed, 11 skipped, 0 failed; pi-5 replay with the derived edges gives `STOP converged all_dimensions_clean`, graph `STOP_ALLOWED` | Met | - |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:156:| REQ-018 | Named defect fix, which also changes default review runs: the review graph upsert derives one FINDING node per finding and one `EVIDENCE_FOR` edge to the FILE node of its `file:line` ref, read from the iteration's delta finding rows and state record, so evidence density no longer depends on the leaf sending graph events. Re-upserting an iteration adds no duplicate node or edge, a finding without a ref adds no edge, a leaf finding node whose id wraps the finding id folds onto the same node, and an edge to a node neither the batch nor the stored graph declares is skipped and reported instead of failing the foreign key (all loop types). The derived FINDING nodes also enter the graph's `findingStability` signal (the share of finding nodes no CONTRADICTS edge touches), which moves in default runs too: a leaf CONTRADICTS edge on a finding now weighs against more finding nodes. Finding ids fold case-insensitively onto this iteration's and the stored findings, an id that collides with a stored finding of another file and title is keyed on the id and the iteration, and only a `file:line` ref earns an edge, with any trailing column dropped. The defect: the canonical projection built no evidence edges, so the pilot lineages whose leaves sent none got a `CONTINUE` graph decision with every legal-stop gate passing. Decision-record Q003 and the operator's ruling of 2026-11-18. Fail-first tests: `upsert-script.vitest.ts` (evidence edge, delta-sourced ref, fold, re-upsert, no ref, undeclared target) and `stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts` (the step passes the state log, delta directory and iteration). |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:74:| AC-019 | REQ-018 | Given a review iteration whose findings carry `file:line` refs in its delta or state record, When `step_graph_upsert` runs `upsert.cjs` with the state log, delta directory and iteration, Then each finding with a ref gets one `EVIDENCE_FOR` edge to a declared FILE node, a re-upsert adds no edge, a finding without a ref adds none, a leaf finding node folds onto the finding it names in any case and in any later iteration while other node kinds keep their edges, a colliding id of another file and title gets its own node, a ref without a line earns no edge, and an edge to an undeclared node is skipped with a stderr notice and no foreign-key failure for every loop type | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts tests/unit/stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts` exits 0. Observed 2026-11-18: the six evidence cases and the step case red first, green after commit `7c6a2d9a7e5`; the review follow-up cases (lowercase fold, a later RESOLVES edge, a non-finding `finding-` id, a colliding id, a ref without a line, research and context orphan edges) red first and green after commit `c22146e2543`; full runtime suite 190 files, 3432 passed, 11 skipped, 0 failed; pi-5 replay with the derived edges gives `STOP converged all_dimensions_clean`, graph `STOP_ALLOWED` | Met | - |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"EVIDENCE_FOR\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/spec.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/tasks.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/acceptance-criteria.md 2>/dev/null | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115384739,"end":1795115385681}}}}
