{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115395954,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5372719001Ze33PSxSOsVp6h","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53706ca0019Mvf8XWQR6fHMO","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-81bb54fba6e33f65","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && ls specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/; echo \"===frontier research reqs===\"; grep -rn \"exhausted\\|all_questions_answered\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010*/spec.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010*/tasks.md 2>/dev/null | head -15"},"output":"001-completed-run-extension\n002-research-claude-config-dir\n003-review-min-iterations-floor\n004-focus-hijack-fix\n005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment\n006-state-log-leaf-fields\n007-source-diversity-quality-class\n008-review-dimension-coverage\n009-fanout-review-coverage-merge\n010-research-frontier-mode\n011-review-frontier-mode\n012-pivot-hygiene\n013-no-redispatch-landed-iteration\n014-docs-playbooks-alignment\ndecision-record.md\ndescription.json\ngoal.md\ngraph-metadata.json\nimplementation-summary.md\nplan.md\nresearch\nresearch_archive\nreview\nreview-archive\nscratch\nspec.md\ntasks.md\n===frontier research reqs===\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:53:A deep-research run stops on `all_questions_answered` or `composite_converged` as soon as the questions written at init are answered, however narrowly. The only path that grows the counted question set, `research/inbox.jsonl`, has no runtime writer, carried-forward questions steer focus without entering the stop count, and no stop signal measures unexplored surface. So a run asked to \"find improvement opportunities\" across a whole subsystem cannot widen or deepen on its own, and narrow-and-done is indistinguishable from converged.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:142:| REQ-005 | When a frontier node reaches a terminal status (`answered`, `blocked`, `exhausted`, `abstained`, `pruned`), the reducer marks its `frontier`-origin question resolved and records the status, and the node stops counting in the graph question-coverage and source-diversity signals. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:151:| REQ-008 | `maxIterations` is split 50% / 35% / 15% across depths 0-1, 2 and 3; unused budget rolls down and never up; a spent band closes its open nodes as `exhausted: budget`; the node cap is tied to `maxIterations` or a minimum `maxIterations` for expansive runs is enforced. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:152:| REQ-009 | Under expansive mode the STUCK_RECOVERY handler closes the active node as `exhausted`, advances focus, falls through to global recovery only when no open node remains and still appends the `stuckRecovery` event that resets `stuckCount`. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:235:| R-004 | Most admitted nodes close as `exhausted: budget` at the default cap of 10 | M | H | Node cap derived as half of `maxIterations` (plan ADR-003, amended 2026-11-18) |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:263:- Does the graph close rule skip writing pruned and exhausted nodes, or re-kind them on close? Skip pruned, re-kind the rest, plan ADR-002, accepted 2026-11-17.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/tasks.md:80:- [x] T010 Add the question close rule: a terminal frontier status marks its `frontier`-origin question resolved and records the status (`$D/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`). Verify: the close case asserts an `exhausted` node's question is resolved and `all_questions_answered` becomes reachable. Done 2026-11-17: a terminal node resolves its inbox question and records `frontierStatus`. The close case gives an empty `openQuestions` with an `exhausted` node, so `all_questions_answered` is reachable. `npx vitest run deep-research-reduce-state.vitest research-depth-mode-golden.vitest` 60 of 60.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/tasks.md:84:- [x] T014 Add the depth budget split 50/35/15 with roll-down only and `exhausted: budget` closes (`$D/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs` and `$D/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`). Verify: a budget case shows an unspent depth-1 share added to depth 2 and never the reverse. Done 2026-11-17: `applyFrontierBudget` in the reducer (50/35/15, roll-down only once a band has no open node, `exhausted`/`budget` closes); `frontier-admit.cjs` keeps child budgets monotone. Roll-down case: depth 2 allotted 6.5 keeps its node open; no-roll-up case: depth 1 allotted 5 closes its node. `npx vitest run deep-research-reduce-state.vitest research-depth-mode-golden.vitest` 60 of 60.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/tasks.md:86:- [x] T016 Add the expansive STUCK_RECOVERY sub-branch that calls `frontier-admit.cjs close --status exhausted` for the active node, advances focus and keeps the `stuckRecovery` append (`Y`). Verify: the `stop-decision-yaml-contract` suite finds the close call and the `stuckRecovery` append in the sub-branch (a wording check: Vitest cannot run YAML prose), and a `frontier-admit` close case shows the node `exhausted` after the call. Done 2026-11-17: `if_stuck_recovery.if_expansive_open_node` closes the focused node with `--status exhausted --reason stuck`, re-reduces, and takes the refreshed Next Focus; the `stuckRecovery` append stays on the path. The contract case checks both (a wording check, since YAML prose does not run). The `frontier-admit` close case shows the store row. `npx vitest run stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest` 21 of 21.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/tasks.md:89:- [x] T019 Add `step_frontier_graph_upsert` after `step_graph_upsert` with the graph close rule (`Y`). Verify: the close case shows an exhausted node no longer lowers question coverage or source diversity in `coverage-graph-signals`. Done 2026-11-17: `step_frontier_graph_upsert` after `step_graph_upsert` runs `frontier-admit.cjs graph` then `upsert.cjs --events`. Pruned nodes are never written; exhausted, blocked and abstained nodes are re-kinded to a closed CLAIM (decision D-010-01). The close case in `frontier-admit.vitest` shows that question coverage and source diversity return to their base values. 19 of 19, plus `npx vitest run stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest` 21 of 21.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"001-completed-run-extension\n002-research-claude-config-dir\n003-review-min-iterations-floor\n004-focus-hijack-fix\n005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment\n006-state-log-leaf-fields\n007-source-diversity-quality-class\n008-review-dimension-coverage\n009-fanout-review-coverage-merge\n010-research-frontier-mode\n011-review-frontier-mode\n012-pivot-hygiene\n013-no-redispatch-landed-iteration\n014-docs-playbooks-alignment\ndecision-record.md\ndescription.json\ngoal.md\ngraph-metadata.json\nimplementation-summary.md\nplan.md\nresearch\nresearch_archive\nreview\nreview-archive\nscratch\nspec.md\nt