 research-depth-mode-golden.vitest` 60 of 60.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/tasks.md:86:- [x] T016 Add the expansive STUCK_RECOVERY sub-branch that calls `frontier-admit.cjs close --status exhausted` for the active node, advances focus and keeps the `stuckRecovery` append (`Y`). Verify: the `stop-decision-yaml-contract` suite finds the close call and the `stuckRecovery` append in the sub-branch (a wording check: Vitest cannot run YAML prose), and a `frontier-admit` close case shows the node `exhausted` after the call. Done 2026-11-17: `if_stuck_recovery.if_expansive_open_node` closes the focused node with `--status exhausted --reason stuck`, re-reduces, and takes the refreshed Next Focus; the `stuckRecovery` append stays on the path. The contract case checks both (a wording check, since YAML prose does not run). The `frontier-admit` close case shows the store row. `npx vitest run stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest` 21 of 21.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/tasks.md:89:- [x] T019 Add `step_frontier_graph_upsert` after `step_graph_upsert` with the graph close rule (`Y`). Verify: the close case shows an exhausted node no longer lowers question coverage or source diversity in `coverage-graph-signals`. Done 2026-11-17: `step_frontier_graph_upsert` after `step_graph_upsert` runs `frontier-admit.cjs graph` then `upsert.cjs --events`. Pruned nodes are never written; exhausted, blocked and abstained nodes are re-kinded to a closed CLAIM (decision D-010-01). The close case in `frontier-admit.vitest` shows that question coverage and source diversity return to their base values. 19 of 19, plus `npx vitest run stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest` 21 of 21.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && ls specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/; echo \\\"===frontier research reqs===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"exhausted\\\\|all_questions_answered\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010*/spec.md specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010*/tasks.md 2>/dev/null | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115394841,"end":1795115395954}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115395960,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5372a1e001neG1xvvGKeH8Ve","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53706ca0019Mvf8XWQR6fHMO","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb20c6585d1b5d01","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"frontier\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/spec.md | grep -i \"research\" | head -15"},"output":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/004-focus-hijack-fix/spec.md:77:- The frontier focus branch of the expansive-depth sub-mode - owned by `../010-research-frontier-mode/`, which builds on this phase.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/004-focus-hijack-fix/spec.md:140:| Dependency | This phase is a prerequisite of `../010-research-frontier-mode/` (parent §20, Slice J depends on D) | Frontier focus would inherit the hijack if this phase slips | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment/spec.md:141:| Risk | `../006-state-log-leaf-fields/` and `../010-research-frontier-mode/` edit the same template, and every edit changes the research contract digest | Merge conflicts on the digest lines | Regenerate the contract after each merge; never hand-resolve the digest lines |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment/spec.md:142:| Dependency | This phase is a prerequisite of `../010-research-frontier-mode/` (parent §20, Slice J depends on E; §10 requires the frontier pack block to keep the write list consistent with the agent) | The frontier pack block would extend an inconsistent list | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/006-state-log-leaf-fields/spec.md:29:| **Successor** | `../010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md` (the research frontier needs this slice first) |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/006-state-log-leaf-fields/spec.md:156:| Risk | The template and the research compiled contract are shared with `../005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment/` and `../010-research-frontier-mode/`, the four ledger files with `../001-completed-run-extension/`, and `convergence.cjs` with `../003-review-min-iterations-floor/`, `../010-research-frontier-mode/` and `../011-review-frontier-mode/` (same file, different function: this phase edits `focusAlignment` at :871-885, they edit the stop-decision floor region at :1159-1169). | Merge conflicts | Build after 001 on the ledger files. Regenerate the contract after each merge; never hand-resolve its digest lines |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/006-state-log-leaf-fields/spec.md:157:| Dependency | `../010-research-frontier-mode/` waits on this phase | Frontier stop would read starved checks | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/spec.md:134:| Dependency | This phase is a prerequisite of `../010-research-frontier-mode/` (parent §15: the sub-mode must not rely on graph `sourceDiversity` until this lands) | The frontier stop would rely on a gameable signal | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/009-fanout-review-coverage-merge/spec.md:76:- The merged `frontier` projection. No producer or shape for a review `registry.frontier` exists until Slice K creates it (`../011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md` REQ-008 and `../011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md` T019 and T022 read it), so this slice cannot define its merge rule. Slice K must deliver it itself: the `frontier` merge rule in `mergeReviewRegistries`, the `frontier.stats` its pilot reads, and the fan-out partition that `frontier_scope:` binds. The research merge (`mergeResearchRegistries`, `fanout-merge.cjs:758`) does not carry `frontier` either; that belongs to `../010-research-frontier-mode/`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:2:title: \"Feature Specification: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-research: frontier admission, veto, close rules\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:3:description: \"Deep-research stops once its init-time questions are answered, because nothing grows the counted question set during a run. This phase adds an opt-in --depth-mode=expansive that admits leaf-proposed frontier nodes into the counted set, steers focus to them, vetoes a premature stop while they are open and closes them cleanly, with default runs byte-identical.\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:5:  - \"research frontier mode\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:8:  - \"frontier admit step\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:9:  - \"frontierOpen veto\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:14:# Feature Specification: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-research: frontier admission, veto, close rules\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/004-focus-hijack-fix/spec.md:77:- The frontier focus branch of the expansive-depth sub-mode - owned by `../010-research-frontier-mode/`, which builds on this phase.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/004-focus-hijack-fix/spec.md:140:| Dependency | This phase is a prerequisite of `../010-research-frontier-mode/` (parent §20, Slice J depends on D) | Frontier focus would inherit the hijack if this phase slips | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment/spec.md:141:| Risk | `../006-state-log-leaf-fields/` and `../010-research-frontier-mode/` edit the same template, and every edit changes the research contract digest | Merge conflicts on the digest lines | Regenerate the contract after each merge; never hand-resolve the digest lines |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment/spec.md:142:| Dependency | This phase is a prerequisite of `../010-research-frontier-mode/` (parent §20, Slice J depends on E; §10 requires the frontier pack block to keep the write list consistent with the agent) | The frontier pack block would extend an inconsistent list | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/006-state-log-leaf-fields/spec.md:29:| **Successor** | `../010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md` (the research frontier needs this slice first) |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/006-state-log-leaf-fields/spec.md:156:| Risk | The template and the research compiled contract are shared with `../005-prompt-pack-contract-alignment/` and `../010-research-frontier-mode/`, the four ledger files with `../001-completed-run-extension/`, and `convergence.cjs` with `../003-review-min-iterations-floor/`, `../010-research-frontier-mode/` and `../011-review-frontier-mode/` (same file, different function: this phase edits `focusAlignment` at :871-885, they edit the stop-decision floor region at :1159-1169). | Merge conflicts | Build after 001 on the ledger files. Regenerate the contract after each merge; never hand-resolve its digest lines |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/006-state-log-leaf-fields/spec.md:157:| Dependency | `../010-research-frontier-mode/` waits on this phase | Frontier stop would read starved checks | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/spec.md:134:| Dependency | This phase is a prerequisite of `../010-research-frontier-mode/` (parent §15: the sub-mode must not rely on graph `sourceDiversity` until this lands) | The frontier stop would rely on a gameable signal | Land this phase before 010 starts |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/009-fanout-review-coverage-merge/spec.md:76:- The merged `frontier` projection. No producer or shape for a review `registry.frontier` exists until Slice K creates it (`../011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md` REQ-008 and `../011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md` T019 and T022 read it), so this slice cannot define its merge rule. Slice K must deliver it itself: the `frontier` merge rule in `mergeReviewRegistries`, the `frontier.stats` its pilot reads, and the fan-out partition that `frontier_scope:` binds. The research merge (`mergeResearchRegistries`, `fanout-merge.cjs:758`) does not carry `frontier` either; that belongs to `../010-research-frontier-mode/`.\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:2:title: \"Feature Specification: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-research: frontier admission, veto, close rules\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:3:description: \"Deep-research stops once its init-time questions are answered, because nothing grows the counted question set during a run. This phase adds an opt-in --depth-mode=expansive that admits leaf-proposed frontier nodes into the counted set, steers focus to them, vetoes a premature stop while they are open and closes them cleanly, with default runs byte-identical.\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:5:  - \"research frontier mode\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:8:  - \"frontier admit step\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:9:  - \"frontierOpen veto\"\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/010-research-frontier-mode/spec.md:14:# Feature Specification: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-research: frontier admission, veto, close rules\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"frontier\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/spec.md | grep -i \\\"research\\\" | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115395614,"end":1795115395960}}}}
