{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115525829,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f538f8420023FzeoGV1L4EBha","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f538c994001SxOGmdybmWBzu2","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97d147db5ec8d251","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","content":"# Iteration 2 - F-1-005 correctness: reducers, convergence, verification and the ledger/projection layer\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-005, dimension correctness. Node scope: `reduce-state.cjs` (review and research), `upsert.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` and the five `runtime/lib` ledger, projection and reducer folders.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (extension payload and projection duplication judged against `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4), operator UX (`--extend` output, warning text and persisted `continuedFromRun` meaning), cross-CLI/OS parity (`dispatch-iteration.cjs` claude config-dir handling and locale-dependent frontier ordering).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- frontier store projection, visit attribution, node status derivation, band budget, lineage and extension bookkeeping, strategy and dashboard rendering.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- frontier store projection, visit records, focus ranking, band budget, question-resolution close rule.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` -- review and research stop facts, `frontier_drained` candidate, `frontierOpen` veto, traceability gate, counters.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` -- review finding-evidence derivation, finding-id folding, orphan-edge skip.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs` -- route-proof source preference and delta fallback.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs` -- `cli-claude-code` config-dir validation and env pass-through.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-schema.ts` and `deep-review-ledger-types.ts` -- `run_extended` payload shape and cross-field check.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-reducers/deep-review-reducer.ts`, `deep-research-reducers`, `legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts`, `legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts` -- extension projection to the run ceiling.\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` -- `step_extend_completed_run`, `step_reduce_review_state` and `step_graph_upsert` order.\n- Traceability sources: `001-completed-run-extension` AC-004/AC-005, `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-017/REQ-018, and `deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md` section 4 (iteration status handling).\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **A `thought` iteration covers a frontier dimension and spends node depth** -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1971 -- `buildReviewFrontier` removes only `FAILED_VISIT_STATUSES` (`error`, `failed`, `failure`, `timeout`) from a node's records, then collects every surviving record's `dimensions` and projects the node `answered` once all four are present (`:1975-1984`). `thought` is a valid iteration status and the review contract states it produces no evidence: \"`thought`: Skipped entirely -- analytical iterations produce no evidence to measure\" (`deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:238`) and \"Skip if `status == \"thought\"` (no change)\" (`references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:369`). The research reducer already treats it that way for question coverage (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2614` excludes `stuck` and `thought`), but the shared visit filter at `frontier-admit.cjs:90` omits both, so the review frontier accepts a record the loop's own doctrine says proves nothing.\nFinding class: class-of-bug\nScope proof: `grep -n \"FAILED_VISIT_STATUSES\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` returns the import at `:21` and the single use at `:1971`; `frontier-admit.cjs:90` defines the set as `['error','failed','failure','timeout']`; no other status filter exists between the state rows and `buildReviewFrontier`.\nAffected surface hints: [\"reduce-state.cjs buildReviewFrontier\", \"reduce-state.cjs reviewRecordsForNode\", \"frontier-admit.cjs FAILED_VISIT_STATUSES\", \"registry.frontier answered status\", \"frontier_drained stop candidate\"]\nCase: a leaf dispatched to F-1-005 for security returns `{\"status\":\"thought\",\"dimensions\":[\"security\"],\"frontierNodeId\":\"F-1-005\"}`; the reducer counts the visit, marks security covered, and after four such records the node projects `answered`, releases the `frontierOpen` veto and lets `frontier_drained` form even though no review evidence was produced.\n\nClaim adjudication:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"contract-contradiction\",\n  \"claim\": \"A thought-status iteration is counted as a frontier visit and its dimensions as node coverage, so a node can answer without evidence.\",\n  \"evidenceRefs\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1971\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1975\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:90\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:238\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:369\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2614\"\n  ],\n  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Checked whether thought rows are filtered before the frontier projection (no status filter in main; iterationRecords carries every type:'iteration' row), whether the global dimension coverage applies a status filter (it does not, which predates this range), and whether the research reducer treats a thought visit the same way (it excludes thought from question coverage but still counts the visit for budget and ranking).\",\n  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"A thought visit may be intended to spend the node's budget because the iteration was dispatched, but the record's dimensions were not reviewed; the projection labels the node 'answered', which is the evidence claim the veto release reads.\",\n  \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade to P2 if the state-record schema or the review workflow refuses a thought status on a frontier-dispatched iteration, or if the leaf contract forbids dimensions on a thought record.\"\n}\n```\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n2. **Frontier steering and projection order by locale collation while the merge orders by code unit** -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2016 -- The active node is chosen with `left.nodeId.localeCompare(right.nodeId)` after depth, visits and iteration, and the projected node list sorts the same way (`:1924`); the research reducer mirrors both sorts (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2447`, `:2512`). The fan-out merge and its `compareText` helper order node ids by code unit (`fanout-merge.cjs:928`), so the same store can project a different active node and budget order on a host whose ICU collation orders the ids differently. This is the same root cause as R1-P2-002 on the reducer and steering surface.\nFinding class: class-of-bug\nScope proof: `grep -n \"localeCompare\" .../runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` returns `:1924` and `:2016` in the new frontier block; the research reducer returns `:2447` and `:2512`; every other node-id ordering in the merge uses `compareText`.\nAffected surface hints: [\"reduce-state.cjs pickReviewFrontierFocus/activeNodeId\", \"reduce-state.cjs readReviewFrontierStore\", \"deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs pickFrontierFocus\", \"fanout-merge.cjs compareText\"]\nCase: two nodes with equal visits and creation iteration are steered on a host whose collation orders `F-1-005` and `F-1-007` differently from the merge host, so the lineage reviews a different node order than the orchestration summary records.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | `001` AC-004/AC-005 rule `newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + N` and `max(prior, elapsed) + M`; the step implements both (`deep-review.yaml:551-568`) and the schema enforces the iteration identity (`deep-review-ledger-schema.ts:951-956`). `010` REQ-005's terminal-status close resolves the inbox question (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2652-2662`). `011` REQ-017's review-only `frontier_drained` candidate and its cap/floor order match the code (`convergence.cjs:1169-1211`). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | AC-004's cap half is the fixture rule the step implements; AC-019's evidence-edge contract is implemented in `upsert.cjs:236-300` and guarded by the integration suite named in the phase; AC-018's candidate order and gate chain match `convergence.cjs:1164-1217`. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:514-620` (`step_extend_completed_run`) writes the `run_extended` event before the config, sets `status: \"initialized\"`, `lineageMode: \"completed-continue\"` and `continuedFromRun` to the distinct iteration count, and prints the re-stop warning.\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:2057-2098` runs `step_reduce_review_state` before `step_graph_upsert`, so the reducer's frontier projection is the one the graph and the next iteration read.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts` and `deep-review-state-contract.ts` project the extension to `type: \"event\", event: \"extended\"` with the budget payload; the research legacy upcast refuses a legacy `extended` row without the full budget (`legacy-compatibility.ts:655-672`).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:210-220` and `:350-447` now accept `--claude-config-dir` for either loop type and pass `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` through the executor guard env; `buildExecutorDispatchEnv` admits it through the `CLAUDE_` allowlist (`executor-audit.ts:1455`).\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `--extend=N` sets `continuedFromRun` to the number of distinct iteration rows, so extending a run that stopped at 7 of 10 by 3 produces a ceiling of 10 and exactly 3 more dispatches. That matches AC-004 but means the new ceiling can sit below the prior cap; I did not treat it as a defect because the flag reads as \"N more iterations\", not \"raise the cap by N\".\n- The same `continuedFromRun` field is a lineage field elsewhere and an iteration count after an extension; the strategy renders it without a unit. Recorded as operator-facing ambiguity, not a separate finding, because REQ-002 mandates the field name.\n- `applyBandBudget` closes an open node as `exhausted` when its band's visits reach the share, using only records attributed to a node; pivot and blocked-stop iterations spend no node visit, so band spend can lag the loop's iteration count by design.\n- A `stuck` record is treated like `thought` by the visit filter but, unlike `thought`, the review doctrine has no explicit \"produces no evidence\" sentence; the finding rests on the `thought` case and names `stuck` only as the same filter gap.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The extension arithmetic and event/config ordering are correct against AC-004/AC-005: the event is appended before the config write, the config keeps `createdAt`, and a failed append leaves the run complete.\n- `reviewTraceabilityCovered` and `reviewOmitsTraceability` read the raw config, not the reduced stop config, so `crossReference.core` and `reviewDimensions` are present at the gate (`convergence.cjs:1601-1631`, `:1683-1710`).\n- The `frontier_drained` candidate is review-only and requires `frontierTotal >= 1` and `frontierAnswered >= 1`; a frontier that closed with nothing answered forms no candidate, as REQ-017 requires.\n- `upsert.cjs` folds leaf finding ids case-insensitively onto stored findings, skips an edge to an undeclared node with a stderr notice, and derives no edge from a ref without a line.\n- `verify-iteration.cjs` now prefers the projected route proof and falls back to the delta only when the state row fails it; the projected review row carries `target_agent`, `resolved_route` and `agent_definition_loaded` (read from this lineage's iteration 1 row).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Abstracting the two reducers' frontier visit, marker and ranking blocks: exactly two instances with contract-driven divergence, and `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4 says two is a coincidence, so extracting them now would buy a wrong abstraction. Named what would change the judgment: a third frontier consumer.\n- `maxIterations` extension lowering the ceiling after an early convergence: AC-004 defines the count-plus-N rule, and the schema check enforces the same identity; not a defect.\n- Research `all_questions_answered` after an exhausted node: REQ-005 deliberately marks the terminal node's question resolved so it leaves the open set; the code matches.\n- `thought` records in the global `buildDimensionCoverage`: the missing status filter predates the range; only the new frontier `answered` projection is reported.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness on F-1-007 (divergent pivot, continuity thread and coverage-graph signals).\n- Reason: the three dealt nodes now have F-1-003 and F-1-005 opened on correctness; F-1-007 is the only one with no dimension covered, and its pivot and graph signals feed the stop gates.\n- Required evidence: `divergent-pivot.ts` seat and quorum rules, `divergent-pivot.cjs` CLI, `continuity-thread.cjs` and the `coverage-graph` query/signal functions the stop gates read.\n- Rotation status: F-1-003 and F-1-005 each have correctness covered; F-1-007 has none.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\", \"content\": \"# Iteration 2 - F-1-005 correctness: reducers, convergence, verification and the ledger/projection layer\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-005, dimension correctness. Node scope: `reduce-state.cjs` (review and research), `upsert.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` and the five `runtime/lib` ledger, projection and reducer folders.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (extension payload and projection duplication judged against `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4), operator UX (`--extend` output, warning text and persisted `continuedFromRun` meaning), cross-CLI/OS parity (`dispatch-iteration.cjs` claude config-dir handling and locale-dependent frontier ordering).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- frontier store projection, visit attribution, node status derivation, band budget, lineage and extension bookkeeping, strategy and dashboard rendering.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- frontier store projection, visit records, focus ranking, band budget, question-resolution close rule.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` -- review and research stop facts, `frontier_drained` candidate, `frontierOpen` veto, traceability gate, counters.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` -- review finding-evidence derivation, finding-id folding, orphan-edge skip.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs` -- route-proof source preference and delta fallback.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs` -- `cli-claude-code` config-dir validation and env pass-through.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-schema.ts` and `deep-review-ledger-types.ts` -- `run_extended` payload shape and cross-field check.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-reducers/deep-review-reducer.ts`, `deep-research-reducers`, `legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts`, `legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts` -- extension projection to the run ceiling.\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` -- `step_extend_completed_run`, `step_reduce_review_state` and `step_graph_upsert` order.\\n- Traceability sources: `001-completed-run-extension` AC-004/AC-005, `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-017/REQ-018, and `deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md` section 4 (iteration status handling).\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **A `thought` iteration covers a frontier dimension and spends node depth** -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1971 -- `buildReviewFrontier` removes only `FAILED_VISIT_STATUSES` (`error`, `failed`, `failure`, `timeout`) from a node's records, then collects every surviving record's `dimensions` and projects the node `answered` once all four are present (`:1975-1984`). `thought` is a valid iteration status and the review contract states it produces no evidence: \\\"`thought`: Skipped entirely -- analytical iterations produce no evidence to measure\\\" (`deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:238`) and \\\"Skip if `status == \\\"thought\\\"` (no change)\\\" (`references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:369`). The research reducer already treats it that way for question coverage (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2614` excludes `stuck` and `thought`), but the shared visit filter at `frontier-admit.cjs:90` omits both, so the review frontier accepts a record the loop's own doctrine says proves nothing.\\nFinding class: class-of-bug\\nScope proof: `grep -n \\\"FAILED_VISIT_STATUSES\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` returns the import at `:21` and the single use at `:1971`; `frontier-admit.cjs:90` defines the set as `['error','failed','failure','timeout']`; no other status filter exists between the state rows and `buildReviewFrontier`.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"reduce-state.cjs buildReviewFrontier\\\", \\\"reduce-state.cjs reviewRecordsForNode\\\", \\\"frontier-admit.cjs FAILED_VISIT_STATUSES\\\", \\\"registry.frontier answered status\\\", \\\"frontier_drained stop candidate\\\"]\\nCase: a leaf dispatched to F-1-005 for security returns `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"thought\\\",\\\"dimensions\\\":[\\\"security\\\"],\\\"frontierNodeId\\\":\\\"F-1-005\\\"}`; the reducer counts the visit, marks security covered, and after four such records the node projects `answered`, releases the `frontierOpen` veto and lets `frontier_drained` form even though no review evidence was produced.\\n\\nClaim adjudication:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"contract-contradiction\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"A thought-status iteration is counted as a frontier visit and its dimensions as node coverage, so a node can answer without evidence.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1971\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1975\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:90\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:238\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:369\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2614\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Checked whether thought rows are filtered before the frontier projection (no status filter in main; iterationRecords carries every type:'iteration' row), whether the global dimension coverage applies a status filter (it does not, which predates this range), and whether the research reducer treats a thought visit the same way (it excludes thought from question coverage but still counts the visit for budget and ranking).\\\",\\n  \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"A thought visit may be intended to spend the node's budget because the iteration was dispatched, but the record's dimensions were not reviewed; the projection labels the node 'answered', which is the evidence claim the veto release reads.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"Downgrade to P2 if the state-record schema or the review workflow refuses a thought status on a frontier-dispatched iteration, or if the leaf contract forbids dimensions on a thought record.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n2. **Frontier steering and projection order by locale collation while the merge orders by code unit** -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2016 -- The active node is chosen with `left.nodeId.localeCompare(right.nodeId)` after depth, visits and iteration, and the projected node list sorts the same way (`:1924`); the research reducer mirrors both sorts (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2447`, `:2512`). The fan-out merge and its `compareText` helper order node ids by code unit (`fanout-merge.cjs:928`), so the same store can project a different active node and budget order on a host whose ICU collation orders the ids differently. This is the same root cause as R1-P2-002 on the reducer and steering surface.\\nFinding class: class-of-bug\\nScope proof: `grep -n \\\"localeCompare\\\" .../runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` returns `:1924` and `:2016` in the new frontier block; the research reducer returns `:2447` and `:2512`; every other node-id ordering in the merge uses `compareText`.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"reduce-state.cjs pickReviewFrontierFocus/activeNodeId\\\", \\\"reduce-state.cjs readReviewFrontierStore\\\", \\\"deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs pickFrontierFocus\\\", \\\"fanout-merge.cjs compareText\\\"]\\nCase: two nodes with equal visits and creation iteration are steered on a host whose collation orders `F-1-005` and `F-1-007` differently from the merge host, so the lineage reviews a different node order than the orchestration summary records.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | `001` AC-004/AC-005 rule `newMaxIterations = continuedFromRun + N` and `max(prior, elapsed) + M`; the step implements both (`deep-review.yaml:551-568`) and the schema enforces the iteration identity (`deep-review-ledger-schema.ts:951-956`). `010` REQ-005's terminal-status close resolves the inbox question (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2652-2662`). `011` REQ-017's review-only `frontier_drained` candidate and its cap/floor order match the code (`convergence.cjs:1169-1211`). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | AC-004's cap half is the fixture rule the step implements; AC-019's evidence-edge contract is implemented in `upsert.cjs:236-300` and guarded by the integration suite named in the phase; AC-018's candidate order and gate chain match `convergence.cjs:1164-1217`. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:514-620` (`step_extend_completed_run`) writes the `run_extended` event before the config, sets `status: \\\"initialized\\\"`, `lineageMode: \\\"completed-continue\\\"` and `continuedFromRun` to the distinct iteration count, and prints the re-stop warning.\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:2057-2098` runs `step_reduce_review_state` before `step_graph_upsert`, so the reducer's frontier projection is the one the graph and the next iteration read.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts` and `deep-review-state-contract.ts` project the extension to `type: \\\"event\\\", event: \\\"extended\\\"` with the budget payload; the research legacy upcast refuses a legacy `extended` row without the full budget (`legacy-compatibility.ts:655-672`).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:210-220` and `:350-447` now accept `--claude-config-dir` for either loop type and pass `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` through the executor guard env; `buildExecutorDispatchEnv` admits it through the `CLAUDE_` allowlist (`executor-audit.ts:1455`).\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `--extend=N` sets `continuedFromRun` to the number of distinct iteration rows, so extending a run that stopped at 7 of 10 by 3 produces a ceiling of 10 and exactly 3 more dispatches. That matches AC-004 but means the new ceiling can sit below the prior cap; I did not treat it as a defect because the flag reads as \\\"N more iterations\\\", not \\\"raise the cap by N\\\".\\n- The same `continuedFromRun` field is a lineage field elsewhere and an iteration count after an extension; the strategy renders it without a unit. Recorded as operator-facing ambiguity, not a separate finding, because REQ-002 mandates the field name.\\n- `applyBandBudget` closes an open node as `exhausted` when its band's visits reach the share, using only records attributed to a node; pivot and blocked-stop iterations spend no node visit, so band spend can lag the loop's iteration count by design.\\n- A `stuck` record is treated like `thought` by the visit filter but, unlike `thought`, the review doctrine has no explicit \\\"produces no evidence\\\" sentence; the finding rests on the `thought` case and names `stuck` only as the same filter gap.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The extension arithmetic and event/config ordering are correct against AC-004/AC-005: the event is appended before the config write, the config keeps `createdAt`, and a failed append leaves the run complete.\\n- `reviewTraceabilityCovered` and `reviewOmitsTraceability` read the raw config, not the reduced stop config, so `crossReference.core` and `reviewDimensions` are present at the gate (`convergence.cjs:1601-1631`, `:1683-1710`).\\n- The `frontier_drained` candidate is review-only and requires `frontierTotal >= 1` and `frontierAnswered >= 1`; a frontier that closed with nothing answered forms no candidate, as REQ-017 requires.\\n- `upsert.cjs` folds leaf finding ids case-insensitively onto stored findings, skips an edge to an undeclared node with a stderr notice, and derives no edge from a ref without a line.\\n- `verify-iteration.cjs` now prefers the projected route proof and falls back to the delta only when the state row fails it; the projected review row carries `target_agent`, `resolved_route` and `agent_definition_loaded` (read from this lineage's iteration 1 row).\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Abstracting the two reducers' frontier visit, marker and ranking blocks: exactly two instances with contract-driven divergence, and `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4 says two is a coincidence, so extracting them now would buy a wrong abstraction. Named what would change the judgment: a third frontier consumer.\\n- `maxIterations` extension lowering the ceiling after an early convergence: AC-004 defines the count-plus-N rule, and the schema check enforces the same identity; not a defect.\\n- Research `all_questions_answered` after an exhausted node: REQ-005 deliberately marks the terminal node's question resolved so it leaves the open set; the code matches.\\n- `thought` records in the global `buildDimensionCoverage`: the missing status filter predates the range; only the new frontier `answered` projection is reported.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness on F-1-007 (divergent pivot, continuity thread and coverage-graph signals).\\n- Reason: the three dealt nodes now have F-1-003 and F-1-005 opened on correctness; F-1-007 is the only one with no dimension covered, and its pivot and graph signals feed the stop gates.\\n- Required evidence: `divergent-pivot.ts` seat and quorum rules, `divergent-pivot.cjs` CLI, `continuity-thread.cjs` and the `coverage-graph` query/signal functions the stop gates read.\\n- Rotation status: F-1-003 and F-1-005 each have correctness covered; F-1-007 has none.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115513922,"end":1795115525829}}}}
