{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115531301,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53933a6001DTkmOc9bjqGYi3","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5392c7e0018qDaRIzwcuSZeC","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab19b3906d338bf6","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one."},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -77,9 +77,10 @@\n \n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\n+- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\", \"oldString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\", \"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115529126,"end":1795115531301}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115531310,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53937b5001G4w4F5oKaAofmB","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5392c7e0018qDaRIzwcuSZeC","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7d08fe6049c7126","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Iteration 1: treating the local review packet as an operator-owned directory left stale `*.jsonl` store files at the lineage root (audit and effect ledgers) with no reader; do not re-open generated bookkeeping there.\n- Iteration 2: the first read of the extension step looked like `maxIterations += N` was missing from a duration-symmetry rule; the checkpoint and AC-004 ruling showed the count-plus-N rule is deliberate, so the direction was dropped."},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -83,9 +83,10 @@\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Iteration 1: treating the local review packet as an operator-owned directory left stale `*.jsonl` store files at the lineage root (audit and effect ledgers) with no reader; do not re-open generated bookkeeping there.\n+- Iteration 2: the first read of the extension step looked like `maxIterations += N` was missing from a duration-symmetry rule; the checkpoint and AC-004 ruling showed the count-plus-N rule is deliberate, so the direction was dropped.\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\", \"oldString\": \"## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\", \"newString\": \"## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- Iteration 1: treating the local review packet as an operator-owned directory left stale `*.jsonl` store files at the lineage root (audit and effect ledgers) with no reader; do not re-open generated bookkeeping there.\\n- Iteration 2: the first read of the extension step looked like `maxIterations += N` was missing from a duration-symmetry rule; the checkpoint and AC-004 ruling showed the count-plus-N rule is deliberate, so the direction was dropped.\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115530165,"end":1795115531310}}}}
