{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115536472,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5394948001ZwO3BlaxGp36F3","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5393fd8001Z4cW3wd54WY4h9","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9aec04be9066df3a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Iteration 2: the first read of the extension step looked like `maxIterations += N` was missing a duration-symmetry rule; the AC-004 checkpoint showed the count-plus-N rule is deliberate, so the direction was dropped rather than reported.\n- Iteration 2: treating the duplicated frontier visit/marker code across the two reducers as an overengineering finding failed the two-instance test in `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4; recorded as a ruled-out direction instead.","oldString":"## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Iteration 1: treating the local review packet as an operator-owned directory left stale `*.jsonl` store files at the lineage root (audit and effect ledgers) with no reader; do not re-open generated bookkeeping there.\n- Iteration 2: the first read of the extension step looked like `maxIterations += N` was missing from a duration-symmetry rule; the checkpoint and AC-004 ruling showed the count-plus-N rule is deliberate, so the direction was dropped.","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n=