{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115636036,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53ad3ff00278LfkkODngYdW8","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53acd02001kHHBbi9OUp3QTl","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ed4a09ee96cc90","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"sourcesQueried\\|SOURCE\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml | sed -n '1,20p'; echo \"===upsert call research===\"; grep -n \"upsert.cjs\" -B6 -A4 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml | head -50"},"output":"1020:        command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n2243:        command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n===upsert call research===\n1908-      step_graph_upsert:\n1909-        action: \"Persist the latest iteration graph delta after the reducer refresh and after the iteration file exists\"\n1910-        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1911-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1912-        note: \"Skips with an informational line and exit 0 when this iteration carries no graph events.\"\n1913-        command: |\n1914:          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/iteration-graph-upsert.cjs --delta-dir \"{state_paths.delta_dir}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\"\n1915-\n1916-      step_frontier_graph_upsert:\n1917-        action: \"Mirror the frontier into the coverage graph so traversal does not depend on the leaf emitting graph events\"\n1918-        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1919-        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n1920-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1921-        note: \"Pruned nodes are never written. A node that closed exhausted, blocked or abstained is re-kinded from QUESTION to a CLAIM marked closed, so it stops lowering question coverage and source diversity. Open, active and answered nodes stay QUESTION nodes linked to their parent by DERIVED_FROM.\"\n1922-        command: |\n1923-          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs graph --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --output \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-graph-events.json\"\n1924:          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type research --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --events \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-graph-events.json\"\n1925-        skip_second_command_when: \"the first command prints nodes 0\"\n1926-        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1927-        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; the frontier store and registry stay authoritative.\"\n1928-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1020:        command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n2243:        command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n===upsert call research===\n1908-      step_graph_upsert:\n1909-        action: \"Persist the latest iteration graph delta after the reducer refresh and after the iteration file exists\"\n1910-        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1911-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1912-        note: \"Skips with an informational line and exit 0 when this iteration carries no graph events.\"\n1913-        command: |\n1914:          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/iteration-graph-upsert.cjs --delta-dir \"{state_paths.delta_dir}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\"\n1915-\n1916-      step_frontier_graph_upsert:\n1917-        action: \"Mirror the frontier into the coverage graph so traversal does not depend on the leaf emitting graph events\"\n1918-        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n1919-        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n1920-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1921-        note: \"Pruned nodes are never written. A node that closed exhausted, blocked or abstained is re-kinded from QUESTION to a CLAIM marked closed, so it stops lowering question coverage and source diversity. Open, active and answered nodes stay QUESTION nodes linked to their parent by DERIVED_FROM.\"\n1922-        command: |\n1923-          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs graph --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --output \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-graph-events.json\"\n1924:          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type research --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --events \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-graph-events.json\"\n1925-        skip_second_command_when: \"the first command prints nodes 0\"\n1926-        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1927-        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; the frontier store and registry stay authoritative.\"\n1928-\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"sourcesQueried\\\\|SOURCE\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml | sed -n '1,20p'; echo \\\"===upsert call research===\\\"; grep -n \\\"upsert.cjs\\\" -B6 -A4 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml | head -50\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115635711,"end":1795115636036}}}}
