{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115640224,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53ae32a002Qd2RuA326uY65Q","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53ad89c001GMoup8w9fDfk6Z","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-afb1ab6fecaac610","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"quality_class\\|metadata\\|path\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/spec.md | head -20; echo \"===tasks===\"; grep -n \"classif\\|path\\|metadata\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/tasks.md | head -10"},"output":"2:title: \"Feature Specification: Derive SOURCE quality_class at the graph upsert choke point\"\n3:description: \"The coverage-graph sourceDiversity signal counts distinct quality_class values on SOURCE nodes, but no runtime producer sets that value and upsert.cjs copies any leaf-supplied string verbatim. This phase derives quality_class at upsert from the node path, name or id, from a closed vocabulary kept beside SAFE_METADATA_KEYS, and strips leaf-supplied values.\"\n6:  - \"quality_class upsert derivation\"\n13:# Feature Specification: Derive SOURCE quality_class at the graph upsert choke point\n18:<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n31:<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n39:`computeResearchSourceDiversityFromData` counts distinct `metadata.quality_class` values on SOURCE nodes cited by each question's answering findings (`runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts:653-690`). No runtime producer sets `quality_class`; only test fixtures do. So on a contract-compliant research run the signal reads 0 and can never pass its 1.5 threshold, while `upsert.cjs:211-245` copies leaf `metadata` verbatim, so any invented string counts (defect D1, confirmed live in generation 1: 0.00 before, 2.0 after hand-set values).\n42:`quality_class` on every research SOURCE node comes from the upsert step itself, from a closed vocabulary, so citing sources of more distinct derived classes is the only way to raise source diversity. The signal counts distinct classes per question, not distinct sources, so a question answered only from one class of source (for example only `.cjs` files) still scores 1.0 and stays below the 1.5 threshold by design; a code-only question that cites code and its tests scores 2.0 and passes.\n48:$ rg -n \"quality_class\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime --glob \"!**/tests/**\" --glob \"!**/node_modules/**\" --glob \"*.{ts,cjs}\"\n49:.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts:131:  'quality_class',\n50:.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts:680:        const qualityClass = sourceMetadataById.get(sourceId)?.quality_class;\n61:- Add a frozen, exported constant of the allowed `quality_class` values beside `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS` in `coverage-graph-query.ts`: `repo-code`, `repo-test`, `repo-spec`, `skill-doc`, `ledger-state`, `external-doc`, `external-other`, `unclassified` (parent §18, \"D1 honest fix\").\n62:- Derive `quality_class` in `upsert.cjs` for research SOURCE nodes from the node's `path` first, then its `name` (the leaf's `label`), then its `id`: a URL maps by host, a repo-relative path maps by path segment and file type, anything else maps to `unclassified`. The pack already requires `\"path\"` on every SOURCE node that names a file (`deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:86`), and `iteration-graph-upsert.cjs:143` spreads the event into the upsert input, so `path` reaches the node loop at `upsert.cjs:211-245`, where it is dropped today.\n63:- Strip any leaf-supplied `quality_class` from SOURCE node metadata before the derived value is set.\n70:- Changing `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS`: it already lists `quality_class` (`coverage-graph-query.ts:131`), so the derived key survives a read with no change.\n71:- New prompt-pack wording: the pack already requires `path` on file SOURCE nodes (:86).\n77:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts` | Modify | Export the frozen `quality_class` vocabulary beside `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS` (:123-136) |\n78:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` | Modify | In the node loop (:211-245), for research SOURCE nodes, strip the leaf value and set the class derived from `path`, then `name`, then `id` |\n80:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts` | Modify | A leaf-supplied value does not survive the research upsert path |\n83:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/` | Modify | One scenario, written by `/create:manual-testing-playbook system-deep-loop update --path .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook` |\n===tasks===\n3:description: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\n26:**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n45:- [x] T003 Add the REQ-001 strip-and-path case and the REQ-002 derivation case before any code change (`RT/tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts`). Verify: `cd RT && npx vitest run tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts` reports the two new cases failing. Done: the two SOURCE cases failed on quality_class; the FINDING/review pass-through case passed.\n47:- [x] T005 Strip the leaf value and set the class derived from `path`, then `name`, then `id` for research SOURCE nodes (`RT/scripts/upsert.cjs`). Verify: the REQ-001 and REQ-002 cases pass and the REQ-005 pass-through case passes. Done: `classifySourceLocation` and `deriveSourceQualityClass` in `upsert.cjs`, wired in the node loop; upsert-script 13 passed.\n48:- [x] T006 Add the leaf-value-dropped case on the research upsert path (`RT/tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts`). Verify: `cd RT && npx vitest run tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts` exits 0 with the new case listed. Done: graph-upsert suite 3 passed, the new case stores `repo-code` over a leaf `primary`.\n49:- [x] T007 Move the upsert-seeded fixtures to source paths that derive distinct classes, and add the REQ-004 code-only fixture (a `.cjs` file plus its `.vitest.ts` test) (`RT/tests/integration/convergence-script.vitest.ts`, `RT/tests/unit/coverage-graph-signals.vitest.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"quality_class: '(primary|secondary|tertiary)'\" RT/tests` prints nothing, the REQ-004 cases report 2.0 and 1.0, and the code-only fixture reports 2.0 with no `source_diversity_guard` blocker. Done: fixtures moved to paths; REQ-004 cases report 2 and 1 (with `source_diversity_guard`), and the code-only `.cjs` plus `.vitest.ts` case reports 2 with no guard blocker. The rg still matches three strip-case inputs that send `primary` on purpose (REQ-001), so it holds for seeded fixtures only.\n60:- [x] T011 Write one playbook scenario for the derived classes through `/create:manual-testing-playbook system-deep-loop update --path RT/manual-testing-playbook` (category `coverage-graph/`). Verify: `rg -l \"quality_class\" RT/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph` lists the new scenario. Done 2026-11-17 through the update-mode steps of `create-manual-testing-playbook-auto.yaml` (`@markdown`): DLR-061 in `runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md`, listed in the root index. `rg -l quality_class` on the folder lists it. `validate-playbook-package.cjs` PASS (53 scenarios, 0 violations). The commands were not executed as a walk.\n61:- [x] T012 Write the changelog entry for the default-path signal change through `/create:changelog` under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/` (cross-phase handoff §3). Verify: the entry says source diversity now reads derived classes and that a single-class question still blocks. Done 2026-11-17 through the update-mode steps of `create-changelog-auto.yaml` (`@markdown`): `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v2.1.1.0.md` (patch). The entry says source diversity reads derived classes and that a code-only question still blocks. validate_document VALID, DQI 89. Step 6 moved the hub version carriers to 2.1.1.0; parent-skill-check PASS.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2:title: \"Feature Specification: Derive SOURCE quality_class at the graph upsert choke point\"\n3:description: \"The coverage-graph sourceDiversity signal counts distinct quality_class values on SOURCE nodes, but no runtime producer sets that value and upsert.cjs copies any leaf-supplied string verbatim. This phase derives quality_class at upsert from the node path, name or id, from a closed vocabulary kept beside SAFE_METADATA_KEYS, and strips leaf-supplied values.\"\n6:  - \"quality_class upsert derivation\"\n13:# Feature Specification: Derive SOURCE quality_class at the graph upsert choke point\n18:<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n31:<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n39:`computeResearchSourceDiversityFromData` counts distinct `metadata.quality_class` values on SOURCE nodes cited by each question's answering findings (`runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts:653-690`). No runtime producer sets `quality_class`; only test fixtures do. So on a contract-compliant research run the signal reads 0 and can never pass its 1.5 threshold, while `upsert.cjs:211-245` copies leaf `metadata` verbatim, so any invented string counts (defect D1, confirmed live in generation 1: 0.00 before, 2.0 after hand-set values).\n42:`quality_class` on every research SOURCE node comes from the upsert step itself, from a closed vocabulary, so citing sources of more distinct derived classes is the only way to raise source diversity. The signal counts distinct classes per question, not distinct sources, so a question answered only from one class of source (for example only `.cjs` files) still scores 1.0 and stays below the 1.5 threshold by design; a code-only question that cites code and its tests scores 2.0 and passes.\n48:$ rg -n \"quality_class\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime --glob \"!**/tests/**\" --glob \"!**/node_modules/**\" --glob \"*.{ts,cjs}\"\n49:.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts:131:  'quality_class',\n50:.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts:680:        const qualityClass = sourceMetadataById.get(sourceId)?.quality_class;\n61:- Add a frozen, exported constant of the allowed `quality_class` values beside `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS` in `coverage-graph-query.ts`: `repo-code`, `repo-test`, `repo-spec`, `skill-doc`, `ledger-state`, `external-doc`, `external-other`, `unclassified` (parent §18, \"D1 honest fix\").\n62:- Derive `quality_class` in `upsert.cjs` for research SOURCE nodes from the node's `path` first, then its `name` (the leaf's `label`), then its `id`: a URL maps by host, a repo-relative path maps by path segment and file type, anything else maps to `unclassified`. The pack already requires `\"path\"` on every SOURCE node that names a file (`deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:86`), and `iteration-graph-upsert.cjs:143` spreads the event into the upsert input, so `path` reaches the node loop at `upsert.cjs:211-245`, where it is dropped today.\n63:- Strip any leaf-supplied `quality_class` from SOURCE node metadata before the derived value is set.\n70:- Changing `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS`: it already lists `quality_class` (`coverage-graph-query.ts:131`), so the derived key survives a read with no change.\n71:- New prompt-pack wording: the pack already requires `path` on file SOURCE nodes (:86).\n77:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts` | Modify | Export the frozen `quality_class` vocabulary beside `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS` (:123-136) |\n78:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` | Modify | In the node loop (:211-245), for research SOURCE nodes, strip the leaf value and set the class derived from `path`, then `name`, then `id` |\n80:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts` | Modify | A leaf-supplied value does not survive the research upsert path |\n83:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/` | Modify | One scenario, written by `/create:manual-testing-playbook system-deep-loop update --path .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook` |\n===tasks===\n3:description: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\n26:**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n45:- [x] T003 Add the REQ-001 strip-and-path case and the REQ-002 derivation case before any code change (`RT/tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts`). Verify: `cd RT && npx vitest run tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts` reports the two new cases failing. Done: the two SOURCE cases failed on quality_class; the FINDING/review pass-through case passed.\n47:- [x] T005 Strip the leaf value and set the class derived from `path`, then `name`, then `id` for research SOURCE nodes (`RT/scripts/upsert.cjs`). Verify: the REQ-001 and REQ-002 cases pass and the REQ-005 pass-through case passes. Done: `classifySourceLocation` and `deriveSourceQualityClass` in `upsert.cjs`, wired in the node loop; upsert-script 13 passed.\n48:- [x] T006 Add the leaf-value-dropped case on the research upsert path (`RT/tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts`). Verify: `cd RT && npx vitest run tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts` exits 0 with the new case listed. Done: graph-upsert suite 3 passed, the new case stores `repo-code` over a leaf `primary`.\n49:- [x] T007 Move the upsert-seeded fixtures to source paths that derive distinct classes, and add the REQ-004 code-only fixture (a `.cjs` file plus its `.vitest.ts` test) (`RT/tests/integration/convergence-script.vitest.ts`, `RT/tests/unit/coverage-graph-signals.vitest.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"quality_class: '(primary|secondary|tertiary)'\" RT/tests` prints nothing, the REQ-004 cases report 2.0 and 1.0, and the code-only fixture reports 2.0 with no `source_diversity_guard` blocker. Done: fixtures moved to paths; REQ-004 cases report 2 and 1 (with `source_diversity_guard`), and the code-only `.cjs` plus `.vitest.ts` case reports 2 with no guard blocker. The rg still matches three strip-case inputs that send `primary` on purpose (REQ-001), so it holds for seeded fixtures only.\n60:- [x] T011 Write one playbook scenario for the derived classes through `/create:manual-testing-playbook system-deep-loop update --path RT/manual-testing-playbook` (category `coverage-graph/`). Verify: `rg -l \"quality_class\" RT/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph` lists the new scenario. Done 2026-11-17 through the update-mode steps of `create-manual-testing-playbook-auto.yaml` (`@markdown`): DLR-061 in `runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md`, listed in the root index. `rg -l quality_class` on the folder lists it. `validate-playbook-package.cjs` PASS (53 scenarios, 0 violations). The commands were not executed as a walk.\n61:- [x] T012 Write the changelog entry for the default-path signal change through `/create:changelog` under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/` (cross-phase handoff §3). Verify: the entry says source diversity now reads derived classes and that a single-class question still blocks. Done 2026-11-17 through the update-mode steps of `create-changelog-auto.yaml` (`@markdown`): `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v2.1.1.0.md` (patch). The entry says source diversity reads derived classes and that a code-only question still blocks. validate_document VALID, DQI 89. Step 6 moved the hub version carriers to 2.1.1.0; parent-skill-check PASS.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"quality_class\\\\|metadata\\\\|path\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/spec.md | head -20; echo \\\"===tasks===\\\"; grep -n \\\"classif\\\\|path\\\\|metadata\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/tasks.md | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115639594,"end":1795115640224}}}}
