{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115702320,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53bd72c001eKdn6psvPk3ROq","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53bcb7c001NpnbZ2u2ITIHTL","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-99023fbf0a6860ed","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"T0\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/012-pivot-hygiene/tasks.md | head -20"},"output":"36:- [x] T001 Get the operator's answer on the seat-cap scope and record it as ADR-001 `Accepted` (`decision-record.md`). Verify: `rg -n 'Accepted' decision-record.md` prints the ADR-001 status line. Done 2026-11-17: per pivot (OD-001), then 3 per council attempt with at most one retry per pivot (OD-002).\n37:- [x] T002 Capture the baseline of the REQ-006 and contract suites (`R/tests/`). Verify: `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run tests/integration/divergent-pivot.vitest.ts tests/council/multi-seat-dispatch.vitest.ts tests/unit/divergent-pivot-cli.vitest.ts tests/unit/check-contract-drift.vitest.ts tests/unit/compile-command-contracts.vitest.ts` exits 0 and the pass count is written in `goal.md` section 4. Done 2026-11-17: 5 files, 50 passed on integration tip `c898b3ad9a3`; typecheck exit 0. Recorded in `goal.md` §4.\n45:- [x] T003 [P] Drop the unreachable `minRemainingIterations` comparison while keeping the field accepted in config and persisted limits (`D`). Verify: the REQ-004 case passes and `rg -n \"remainingIterations < config\" R/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts` prints nothing. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch, `scratch/dispatch/T003.*`): the comparison is gone (`rg` exit 1); the minRemainingIterations row became the case \"keeps accepting a persisted minRemainingIterations limit without refusing on it\"; 14 passed.\n46:- [x] T004 Cap council seat outputs at 3 per council attempt: set the default to 3 (:286) and count only the current attempt in the seat-cap check (:736), and run that check only when an attempt is opened, not when `prepare` resumes an open attempt (:1244, :1284) (`D`). Verify: the REQ-005 cases pass in `tests/integration/divergent-pivot.vitest.ts`, including a resume of an attempt that holds 2 seat returns. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch): default 3, check runs only when the attempt holds no durable seat; cases \"allows a later pivot after an earlier pivot used six seat outputs\" and \"does not refuse a resumed attempt that already holds two seat returns\" pass (16 passed, typecheck 0). Deviation: a resumed prepare reuses the persisted `usageAtStart` (and, from T006, `limits`), because a caller-reported count that changed since the pivot opened made the `pivot_started` replay and `persistConfig` throw a conflict.\n47:- [x] T005 Scope the seat count to the current pivot id and attempt in both pivot scripts (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts:420`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts:405`). Verify: the REQ-008 two-pivot case passes. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch): both builders derive the current pivot id with `derivePivotId` and count only that pivot's seat events for its current attempt; new `R/tests/unit/divergent-pivot-seat-scope.vitest.ts` cases \"counts zero seat outputs for a second pivot after a completed first pivot (research)\" and \"(review)\" pass; the tsx loader the CLI uses still loads both scripts.\n48:- [x] T006 Give the attempt an identity: attempt-2 seat event ids (`seatEventId`, :600-601), seat output paths (`buildPivotCouncilPaths`, :807-830), attempt-scoped event lookups in place of `eventByName` (:596-598), and an `attempt` field with `invariants.rounds` of 1 or 2 in the persisted config (:1130-1165). Attempt 1 keeps today's ids and paths; seat ids stay `seat-001` to `seat-003` (`D`). Verify: the REQ-007 case passes, including a pre-change pivot fixture that still loads. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch): `seatEventId`/`deliberationEventId`/`buildPivotCouncilPaths` take an attempt; attempt 2 lives under `council/attempt-2/`; config carries `attempt` only for attempt 2 and `invariants.rounds` equals the attempt; cases \"gives attempt 2 its own seat and deliberation paths and keeps attempt 1 paths\" and \"keeps attempt-1 seat event ids and loads a config written before attempts existed\" pass (28 passed across the three suites, typecheck 0).\n49:- [x] T007 Mark a first-attempt quorum failure retryable in finalize, at most once per pivot, writing a distinct non-terminal per-attempt failure event instead of `pivot_failed` (:1295, :1441), with the matching `PivotEventName` (:146-153) and `PIVOT_LIFECYCLE_STATES` (:290-297) entries; reopen the same pivot as attempt 2 in prepare; record the real seat count (3 or 6) in usage (:1485-1486) (`D`). Verify: the REQ-002 and REQ-003 cases pass. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch, `scratch/dispatch/T007.*`): `pivot_attempt_failed` (lifecycle to `COUNCIL_RETRY_PENDING`) replaces `pivot_failed` for a first-attempt quorum miss; prepare reopens the pivot as attempt 2 and rewrites the config only after the attempt-1 record replays unchanged; usage records `3 * attempt`; `runDivergentPivot` loops at most twice. Cases \"retries a first-attempt quorum failure once and completes on the second attempt\", \"fails closed when the retry also misses quorum and opens no third attempt\" and \"does not retry an agreement failure\" pass.\n50:- [x] T008 Carry the retry signal and the attempt number through the `prepare` and `finalize` subcommands (`R/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs`). Verify: `npx vitest run tests/unit/divergent-pivot-cli.vitest.ts` passes with a case where `finalize` prints a retryable result and a second `prepare` returns attempt 2 with three missing seats. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch): no CLI code change was needed (prepare spreads `attempt`, finalize prints `retryable` and `attempt`); the module header documents the retry, and the case \"finalize prints a retryable quorum failure and a second prepare returns attempt 2 with three missing seats\" drives prepare, three record-seat calls, finalize and a second prepare through the real CLI (4 passed).\n51:- [x] T009 Re-enter `step_prepare_divergent_pivot` once when finalize returns retryable, passing the attempt number to the seat dispatch and record steps (`.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml`, pivot branch :1056-1112). Verify: `rg -n \"retryable\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml` prints the new branch, and a second failure still reaches the fail-closed log line. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch, `scratch/dispatch/T009.*`): `step_retry_divergent_pivot_once` re-enters `step_prepare_divergent_pivot` when `pivot_finalize_retryable` is true and `pivot_attempt` is 1; its `fail_closed` text names the existing if_failed log line for a second miss. Orchestrator corrected one sentence that claimed the seat prompts name attempt 2 (the renderers do not). The YAML suites pass (44 cases across 11 files).\n52:- [x] T010 Add the same one-time re-entry to the review pivot branch (`.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml`, :1158-1206). Verify: `rg -n \"retryable\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` prints the new branch. Done 2026-11-17 with T009: the same literal edit, identical diff hunks (checked by hashing both).\n53:- [x] T011 Regenerate both compiled contracts, last of the implementation tasks (`.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown`, `deep-review.contract.markdown`). Verify: `node R/scripts/compile-command-contracts.cjs --command deep/research --write` and `node R/scripts/compile-command-contracts.cjs --command deep/review --write` each print their contract path, and `npx vitest run tests/unit/check-contract-drift.vitest.ts tests/unit/compile-command-contracts.vitest.ts` exits 0. Regenerate again after each merge instead of resolving digest lines by hand. Done 2026-11-17 (orchestrator): both contracts regenerated after the last digested edit; `check-contract-drift.cjs` prints `OK commands=2`; `check-contract-drift.vitest.ts` and `compile-command-contracts.vitest.ts` pass.\n61:- [x] T012 Add the retry case: attempt 2 dispatches three seats under the same seat ids, and its event ids and seat files do not collide with attempt 1 (`R/tests/integration/divergent-pivot.vitest.ts`). Verify: the case passes. `tests/council/multi-seat-dispatch.vitest.ts` is not edited, because the workflow, not `dispatchCouncilSeats`, drives the pivot's seats. Done 2026-11-17 with T007: the retry case asserts six distinct seat event ids (attempt 2 prefixed `attempt-2:`), both attempts' seat files, `attempt: 2` in the config, and a replayed finalize; the step-API case \"reopens a quorum-failed pivot as attempt 2 through prepare, record and finalize\" also passes. 32 passed across the three suites, typecheck 0.\n62:- [x] T013 Typecheck the runtime (`R/tsconfig.json`). Verify: `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npm run typecheck` exits 0. Done 2026-11-17: `npm run typecheck` exit 0.\n63:- [x] T014 Write the changelog entry stating that `maxCouncilSeatOutputs` now means 3 per council attempt, that a quorum failure gets one retry, and that the worst-case run cost is 18 (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/`). Verify: `rg -l 'maxCouncilSeatOutputs' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog` lists the new entry. Done: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v2.1.4.0.md`.\n64:- [x] T015 Write the manual testing playbook scenario for a divergent run whose first council attempt fails quorum and whose retry completes, through `/create:manual-testing-playbook system-deep-loop update --path .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/council/`). Verify: `rg -l 'retry' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/council` lists the new scenario. Done: DLR-062 at `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/council/divergent-council-quorum-retry.md`.\n65:- [x] T016 Rerun the T002 suites and compare with the baseline (`R/tests/`). Verify: the same command exits 0 and the pass count rose only by the new cases. Done 2026-11-17: the T002 suites plus `divergent-pivot-seat-scope.vitest.ts` pass 6 files, 61 tests: 50 baseline + 9 new cases in the T002 files + 2 seat-scope cases, nothing else moved.\n66:- [x] T017 Update the two convergence references for the one-time retry (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md`), per `../scratch/cross-phase-handoff.md` §3 \"Every other phase\". Verify: `grep -n \"attempt 2\\|or six when\\|attempt-2 folder\"` prints the new lines in both files. Done 2026-11-17 (Go dispatch).\n67:- [x] T018 Update the two `divergent-convergence-mode.md` feature-catalog pages (`deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/`, `deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/`), which say \"exactly three native seats in one round\", through `/create:feature-catalog`. Verify: each page names the one-time quorum retry. Done: both pages, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/divergent-convergence-mode.md` and `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md`.\n77:- [x] The T016 rerun matches the baseline plus the new cases\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"36:- [x] T001 Get the operator's answer on the seat-cap scope and record it as ADR-001 `Accepted` (`decision-record.md`). Verify: `rg -n 'Accepted' decision-record.md` prints the ADR-001 status line. Done 2026-11-17: per pivot (O