{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115702328,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53bd66d002T254PkCpN98j4W","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53bcb7c001NpnbZ2u2ITIHTL","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b18b0a7d5c5ae5a5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"REQ-\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/012-pivot-hygiene/spec.md | head -15"},"output":"105:| REQ-001 | The operator's seat-cap choice is recorded before the cap changes. | `decision-record.md` ADR-001 shows `Accepted` and names 3 seat outputs per council attempt with at most one retry per pivot; OD-001 and OD-002 carry the decision. |\n106:| REQ-002 | A council quorum failure is retried once, and the retry attempt gets its own 3 seat outputs. | A `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` case: first attempt returns 2 of 3 seats, the retry attempt returns 3 valid seats; the pivot completes and records 6 seat outputs. A second consecutive quorum failure fails closed with the original reason, and no third attempt is opened. |\n107:| REQ-003 | `council_agreement_failed` is not retried. | A case where three valid seats disagree fails closed after one round with `council_agreement_failed` and records 3 seat outputs. |\n108:| REQ-004 | Persisted pivot limits that carry `minRemainingIterations` still load. | A case reading a persisted config with `minRemainingIterations: 1` parses without error, and no pivot is refused with `insufficient_remaining_iterations`. |\n114:| REQ-005 | The seat cap follows ADR-001: 3 seat outputs per council attempt, at most one retry per pivot. | A case where pivot 1 used 6 seats (with retry) still allows pivot 2, no pivot records more than 6 seat outputs, and resuming an open attempt that holds 2 seat returns is not refused by the cap. |\n115:| REQ-006 | Default runs are unaffected. | `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts`, `divergent-pivot-cli.vitest.ts` and `multi-seat-dispatch.vitest.ts` pass; the divergent path runs only under `--convergence-mode divergent`. |\n116:| REQ-007 | The retry attempt has its own identity. | A `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` case: after a retried pivot, the state log holds attempt-1 and attempt-2 seat events with distinct event ids, both attempts' seat files exist, the persisted config parses, and a pivot written before this change (attempt 1 ids, `invariants.rounds: 1`) still loads. A first-attempt quorum failure writes no terminal `pivot_failed`. |\n117:| REQ-008 | The seat count is scoped. | A case with two pivots in one artifact root: the usage that `divergent-research-pivot.ts` and `divergent-review-pivot.ts` pass for pivot 2 counts 0 seat outputs, not pivot 1's. |\n118:| REQ-009 | Generated and documented surfaces stay in step. | `check-contract-drift.vitest.ts` and `compile-command-contracts.vitest.ts` pass after both contracts are regenerated; a changelog entry and a council playbook retry scenario exist. |\n140:| Risk | Default-path risk is LOW: the pivot runs only in `divergent` convergence mode, which is opt-in (`.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:103`). | Low | REQ-006 suites |\n142:| Risk | Removing the field outright would break reads of persisted pivot limits, which list it as required (:1025). | Med | Keep the field accepted on read; only the check is dropped (REQ-004) |\n143:| Risk | `prepare` reruns the preflight cap check on a resume (`divergent-pivot.ts:1244`, :1284), so a per-attempt count would refuse a resumed attempt that already holds seat returns | High if missed | Run the seat-cap check only when an attempt is opened; a REQ-005 case resumes an attempt with 2 seat returns |\n144:| Risk | Attempt 2 reuses the fixed ids and paths: `${pivotId}:pivot_seat_returned:${seatId}`, `seats/seat-00N.md`, `${pivotId}:pivot_failed`, and `eventByName` returns the first match, so attempt 2 would read attempt 1's events | High if missed | Carry the attempt number in every id and path; keep attempt-1 ids unchanged so older pivots load (REQ-007) |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"105:| REQ-001 | The operator's seat-cap choice is recorded before the cap changes. | `decision-record.md` ADR-001 shows `Accepted` and names 3 seat outputs per council attempt with at most one retry per pivot; OD-001 and OD-002 carry the decision. |\n106:| REQ-002 | A council quorum failure is retried once, and the retry attempt gets its own 3 seat outputs. | A `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` case: first attempt returns 2 of 3 seats, the retry attempt returns 3 valid seats; the pivot completes and records 6 seat outputs. A second consecutive quorum failure fails closed with the original reason, and no third attempt is opened. |\n107:| REQ-003 | `council_agreement_failed` is not retried. | A case where three valid seats disagree fails closed after one round with `council_agreement_failed` and records 3 seat outputs. |\n108:| REQ-004 | Persisted pivot limits that carry `minRemainingIterations` still load. | A case reading a persisted config with `minRemainingIterations: 1` parses without error, and no pivot is refused with `insufficient_remaining_iterations`. |\n114:| REQ-005 | The seat cap follows ADR-001: 3 seat outputs per council attempt, at most one retry per pivot. | A case where pivot 1 used 6 seats (with retry) still allows pivot 2, no pivot records more than 6 seat outputs, and resuming an open attempt that holds 2 seat returns is not refused by the cap. |\n115:| REQ-006 | Default runs are unaffected. | `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts`, `divergent-pivot-cli.vitest.ts` and `multi-seat-dispatch.vitest.ts` pass; the divergent path runs only under `--convergence-mode divergent`. |\n116:| REQ-007 | The retry attempt has its own identity. | A `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` case: after a retried pivot, the state log holds attempt-1 and attempt-2 seat events with distinct event ids, both attempts' seat files exist, the persisted config parses, and a pivot written before this change (attempt 1 ids, `invariants.rounds: 1`) still loads. A first-attempt quorum failure writes no terminal `pivot_failed`. |\n117:| REQ-008 | The seat count is scoped. | A case with two pivots in one artifact root: the usage that `divergent-research-pivot.ts` and `divergent-review-pivot.ts` pass for pivot 2 counts 0 seat outputs, not pivot 1's. |\n118:| REQ-009 | Generated and documented surfaces stay in step. | `check-contract-drift.vitest.ts` and `compile-command-contracts.vitest.ts` pass after both contracts are regenerated; a changelog entry and a council playbook retry scenario exist. |\n140:| Risk | Default-path risk is LOW: the pivot runs only in `divergent` convergence mode, which is opt-in (`.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:103`). | Low | REQ-006 suites |\n142:| Risk | Removing the field outright would break reads of persisted pivot limits, which list it as required (:1025). | Med | Keep the field accepted on read; only the check is dropped (REQ-004) |\n143:| Risk | `prepare` reruns the preflight cap check on a resume (`divergent-pivot.ts:1244`, :1284), so a per-attempt count would refuse a resumed attempt that already holds seat returns | High if missed | Run the seat-cap check only when an attempt is opened; a REQ-005 case resumes an attempt with 2 seat returns |\n144:| Risk | Attempt 2 reuses the fixed ids and paths: `${pivotId}:pivot_seat_returned:${seatId}`, `seats/seat-00N.md`, `${pivotId}:pivot_failed`, and `eventByName` returns the first match, so attempt 2 would read attempt 1's events | High if missed | Carry the attempt number in every id and path; keep attempt-1 ids unchanged so older pivots load (REQ-007) |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"REQ-\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/012-pivot-hygiene/spec.md | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115701869,"end":1795115702328}}}}
