{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115706601,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53be802001wT1TMflorFXVca","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53bdb9a001FDuDeqal20uTI7","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d907eec4e55fa0c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"expansive\\|frontier\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts | head -20"},"output":"311:    'Candidate frontier:',\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"311:    'Candidate frontier:',\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"expansive\\\\|frontier\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115706370,"end":1795115706601}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115706609,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53be6f7002r7xM52AEiP3rNr","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53bdb9a001FDuDeqal20uTI7","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93d0272e51863266","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"sixth source\\|revisit direction\\|closed .*exhausted\\|exhausted.*blocked\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/spec.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md 2>/dev/null | head -15"},"output":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147:| REQ-007 | Under the flag, the review pivot is prepared only once every frontier node is terminal, may seed from nodes closed `exhausted` or `blocked`, and routes an accepted candidate through admission; the boundary regexes and the configured-target ban stay unchanged. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:155:| REQ-017 | Under the flag, a review run whose frontier holds at least one node and none open or active, and which forms neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite candidate, gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It never outranks the cap, failures, stuck recovery, `off`, `max-iterations` or the floor, every legal-stop gate and the graph decision still decide it, and a default run never forms it (plan ADR-006, decision-record Q003). A frontier that closed with no `answered` node, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:109:When the frontier holds at least one answered node and none is open or active, and neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite vote forms, an expansive run gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It ranks after the other two, so the floor, the legal-stop gates and the graph decision run on it as on any candidate: a failed gate gives `BLOCKED`, and a stop records `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained`. A fan-out lineage reads only its own partition, so one whose nodes are answered stops rather than running to its cap. A frontier that closed with nothing answered, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate, and a default run never forms it.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:115:Each eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. If that round misses quorum, because a seat fails to return or returns a report that does not parse, the pivot reopens once as attempt 2 with three fresh seat outputs. A second quorum miss, or three valid seats that do not agree, fails the pivot closed. `maxCouncilSeatOutputs` caps one council attempt at 3 seat outputs, so a pivot records at most 6. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147:| REQ-007 | Under the flag, the review pivot is prepared only once every frontier node is terminal, may seed from nodes closed `exhausted` or `blocked`, and routes an accepted candidate through admission; the boundary regexes and the configured-target ban stay unchanged. |\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:155:| REQ-017 | Under the flag, a review run whose frontier holds at least one node and none open or active, and which forms neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite candidate, gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It never outranks the cap, failures, stuck recovery, `off`, `max-iterations` or the floor, every legal-stop gate and the graph decision still decide it, and a default run never forms it (plan ADR-006, decision-record Q003). A frontier that closed with no `answered` node, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:109:When the frontier holds at least one answered node and none is open or active, and neither `all_dimensions_clean` nor the composite vote forms, an expansive run gets the hard candidate `frontier_drained`. It ranks after the other two, so the floor, the legal-stop gates and the graph decision run on it as on any candidate: a failed gate gives `BLOCKED`, and a stop records `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained`. A fan-out lineage reads only its own partition, so one whose nodes are answered stops rather than running to its cap. A frontier that closed with nothing answered, every node exhausted or pruned, forms no candidate, and a default run never forms it.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:115:Each eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. If that round misses quorum, because a seat fails to return or returns a report that does not parse, the pivot reopens once as attempt 2 with three fresh seat outputs. A second quorum miss, or three valid seats that do not agree, fails the pivot closed. `maxCouncilSeatOutputs` caps one council attempt at 3 seat outputs, so a pivot records at most 6. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"sixth source\\\\|revisit direction\\\\|closed .*exhausted\\\\|exhausted.*blocked\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/*/spec.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md 2>/dev/null | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115706103,"end":1795115706609}}}}
