{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795115738387,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f53c65130016EApVYUox6luyK","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53c5d7e001QnpWr6Ro4PWzrl","type":"step-start","snapshot":"4c9236f16bdc82eee22df161ae89de20b8fee7df"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115742312,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53c71e0001yhIzuzmPULUG1f","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53c5d7e001QnpWr6Ro4PWzrl","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a9c9bc5c9991ca3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"REQ-007\" -A 3 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md | head -10; echo \"===plan pivot admission===\"; grep -n \"pivot\" -A 4 -B 2 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md | grep -i \"admi\\|candidate\\|frontier\" | head -15"},"output":"147:| REQ-007 | Under the flag, the review pivot is prepared only once every frontier node is terminal, may seed from nodes closed `exhausted` or `blocked`, and routes an accepted candidate through admission; the boundary regexes and the configured-target ban stay unchanged. |\n148-| REQ-008 | With fan-out under the flag, the review `step_frontier_seed` writes the depth-1 nodes before `step_fanout_spawn`; `fanout-run.cjs` passes `config.depthMode: expansive` to every review lineage (nothing for `default`), partitions the nodes round-robin through a `frontier_scope:` binding that coexists with `review_focus`, records the partition as `frontier_partition` in `orchestration-summary.json` and writes each lineage's nodes into its store before it spawns; `mergeReviewRegistries` returns a merged `frontier`; and the merge guard fails when a partitioned depth-1 node is missing from every lineage. |\n149-| REQ-009 | Under expansive mode the review STUCK_RECOVERY handler closes the active node as `exhausted`, advances focus and still appends `deep_review.recovery_started`, which projects to the `stuckRecovery` event that resets `stuckCount`. |\n150-| REQ-010 | A pilot on example target 1 reviews `<pilot-sha>~100..<pilot-sha>` with the SHA recorded at start, prunes merges as `merge-no-own-diff` and index rebuilds as `generated-artifact` in the seed step, admits the seven subsystem nodes at depth 1, partitions them across fan-out lineages and ends with every node terminal and zero open and zero active nodes (amended 2026-11-18, decision-record Q008: the non-cap stop clause is dropped). |\n===plan pivot admission===\n2-title: \"Implementation Plan: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-review: admission into candidateCoverage and searchDebt\"\n3:description: \"Builds the review side of --depth-mode=expansive on top of the research frontier: review config and flag, golden review test, review proposal channel, admission into searchDebt and candidateCoverage, review Next Focus branch, veto on review stop candidates, pivot seed changes and the review fan-out partition, then the last-100-commits pilot.\"\n5-  - \"review frontier mode plan\"\n25-| **Storage** | JSONL deltas, the review findings registry (`candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, new `frontier`), the fan-out merged registry |\n29:The change reuses the research phase's flag semantics, admission helper, node-store row shape, seed step, depth budget and veto, and points them at the review coverage surfaces instead of an inbox. Every review branch is gated on `depthMode` being `expansive`. A golden review test, which also covers pivot seed output and the fan-out lineage prompt, lands before any behavior change.\n45:- [ ] From `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime`, `npm test` exits 0, including the golden review, review admit, close, steering, pivot and fan-out cases. Vitest run from any other directory finds no `.vitest.ts` file\n60:- **Review proposal channel**: the review pack and agent definition gain the `frontier_proposal` row. Without it a review leaf has no sanctioned way to name a sub-target; today every `frontier` hit in `deep-review.yaml` is the pivot's candidate frontier.\n61-- **Review node-status store (`review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`)**: the phase-010 row shape, written only by `frontier-admit.cjs` in review target mode. Review has no inbox, and `buildSearchLedgerState` (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1764`) rebuilds `candidateCoverage` and `searchDebt` from iteration records on every reduce, so an admitted node handed only to the reducer would vanish on the next reduce.\n63-- **Review admission step**: calls the phase-010 helper in a review target mode; an admitted node becomes a store row, an open `searchDebt` entry and a `registry.frontier` node.\n64-- **Review reducer frontier branch**: projects `registry.frontier` and the frontier debt from the store, tracks per-node dimension coverage, applies the close rule (clear debt, record a `candidateCoverage` bucket) and assigns the advisory Next Focus in the last-assignment-wins sequence.\n65-- **Dispatch steering**: review dispatch reads `next_dimension` (`deep-review.yaml:904`), which today comes from the init-only `dimension_queue`. Under the flag, `step_read_state` reads the active node from `registry.frontier`, sets `next_dimension` to that node's next uncovered dimension and fills `{frontier_block}` in the pack. The reducer's Next Focus text is read only by the agent, so it cannot steer on its own.\n66-- **Veto on review candidates**: the existing `frontierOpen` veto, now reading the review registry for `all_dimensions_clean` and composite candidates.\n67:- **Pivot seed change**: `divergent-review-pivot.ts` waits for a terminal frontier, may seed from `exhausted` or `blocked` nodes and hands an accepted candidate to admission.\n68-- **Review fan-out path**: `config.depthMode` passthrough, `frontier_scope:` beside `review_focus`, the partition recorded in `orchestration-summary.json`, per-lineage stores written before spawn, a merged `frontier` in `mergeReviewRegistries` (`fanout-merge.cjs:981-996` returns none today), and a merge guard over the recorded partition and the phase-009 merged coverage.\n71:The seed step writes depth-1 nodes to the store before iteration 1 (and, under fan-out, `fanout-run.cjs` splits them across lineage stores). Review leaf writes `frontier_proposal` rows in its delta. The review admission step prunes or admits and records each outcome in the store; the reducer reads the store and writes `searchDebt`, `registry.frontier` and Next Focus. `step_read_state` then turns the active node into `next_dimension` and `{frontier_block}` for the next dispatch. `convergence.cjs` applies the veto right after the `minIterations` floor and before the gates and guards, as the parent research places it. The order matters on review: `candidateCoverageGate` fails while `searchDebt` is non-empty, so a gate evaluated first would turn every stop with open frontier debt into BLOCKED, and blocked-stop text outranks the frontier focus. On a terminal status the reducer clears the node's debt and records its bucket. At a STOP candidate with a terminal frontier the pivot may run and propose more nodes through admission.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"147:| REQ-007 | Under the flag, the review pivot is prepared only once every frontier node is terminal, may seed from nodes closed `exhausted` or `blocked`, and routes an accepted candidate through admission; the boundary regexes and the configured-target ban stay unchanged. |\n148-| REQ-008 | With fan-out under the flag, the review `step_frontier_seed` writes the depth-1 nodes before `step_fanout_spawn`; `fanout-run.cjs` passes `config.depthMode: expansive` to every review lineage (nothing for `default`), partitions the nodes round-robin through a `frontier_scope:` binding that coexists with `review_focus`, records the partition as `frontier_partition` in `orchestration-summary.json` and writes each lineage's nodes into its store before it spawns; `mergeReviewRegistries` returns a merged `frontier`; and the merge guard fails when a partitioned depth-1 node is missing from every lineage. |\n149-| REQ-009 | Under expansive mode the review STUCK_RECOVERY handler closes the active node as `exhausted`, advances focus and still appends `deep_review.recovery_started`, which projects to the `stuckRecovery` event that resets `stuckCount`. |\n150-| REQ-010 | A pilot on example target 1 reviews `<pilot-sha>~100..<pilot-sha>` with the SHA recorded at start, prunes merges as `merge-no-own-diff` and index rebuilds as `generated-artifact` in the seed step, admits the seven subsystem nodes at depth 1, partitions them across fan-out lineages and ends with every node terminal and zero open and zero active nodes (amended 2026-11-18, decision-record Q008: the non-cap stop clause is dropped). |\n===plan pivot admission===\n2-title: \"Implementation Plan: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-review: admission into candidateCoverage and searchDebt\"\n3:description: \"Builds the review side of --depth-mode=expansive on top of the research frontier: review config and flag, golden review test, review proposal channel, admission into searchDebt and candidateCoverage, review Next Focus branch, veto on review stop candidates, pivot seed changes and the review fan-out partition, then the last-100-commits pilot.\"\n5-  - \"review frontier mode plan\"\n25-| **Storage** | JSONL deltas, the review findings registry (`candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, new `frontier`), the fan-out merged registry |\n29:The change reuses the research phase's flag semantics, admission helper, node-store row shape, seed step, depth budget and veto, and points them at the review coverage surfaces instead of an inbox. Every review branch is gated on `depthMode` being `expansive`. A golden review test, which also covers pivot seed output and the fan-out lineage prompt, lands before any behavior change.\n45:- [ ] From `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime`, `npm test` exits 0, including the golden review, review admit, close, steering, pivot and fan-out cases. Vitest run from any other directory finds no `.vitest.ts` file\n60:- **Review proposal channel**: the review pack and agent definition gain the `frontier_proposal` row. Without it a review leaf has no sanctioned way to name a sub-target; today every `frontier` hit in `deep-review.yaml` is the pivot's candidate frontier.\n61-- **Review node-status store (`review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`)**: the phase-010 row shape, written only by `frontier-admit.cjs` in review target mode. Review has no inbox, and `buildSearchLedgerState` (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1764`) rebuilds `candidateCoverage` and `searchDebt` from iteration records on every reduce, so an admitted node handed only to the reducer would vanish on the next reduce.\n63-- **Review admission step**: calls the phase-010 helper in a review target mode; an admitted node becomes a store row, an open `searchDebt` entry and a `registry.frontier` node.\n64-- **Review reducer frontier branch**: projects `registry.frontier` and the frontier debt from the store, tracks per-node dimension coverage, applies the close rule (clear debt, record a `candidateCoverage` bucket) and assigns the advisory Next Focus in the last-assignment-wins sequence.\n65-- **Dispatch steering**: review dispatch reads `next_dimension` (`deep-review.yaml:904`), which today comes from the init-only `dimension_queue`. Under the flag, `step_read_state` reads the active node from `registry.frontier`, sets `next_dimension` to that node's next uncovered dimension and fills `{frontier_block}` in the pack. The reducer's Next Focus text is read only by the agent, so it cannot steer on its own.\n66-- **Veto on review candidates**: the existing `frontierOpen` veto, now reading the review registry for `all_dimensions_clean` and composite candidates.\n67:- **Pivot seed change**: `divergent-review-pivot.ts` waits for a terminal frontier, may seed from `exhausted` or `blocked` nodes and hands an accepted candidate to admission.\n68-- **Review fan-out path**: `config.depthMode` passthrough, `frontier_scope:` beside `review_focus`, the partition recorded in `orchestration-summary.json`, per-lineage stores written before spawn, a merged `frontier` in `mergeReviewRegistries` (`fanout-merge.cjs:981-996` returns none today), and a merge guard over the recorded partition and the phase-009 merged coverage.\n71:The seed step writes depth-1 nodes to the store before iteration 1 (and, under fan-out, `fanout-run.cjs` splits them across lineage stores). Review leaf writes `frontier_proposal` rows in its delta. The review admission step prunes or admits and records each outcome in the store; the reducer reads the store and writes `searchDebt`, `registry.frontier` and Next Focus. `step_read_state` then turns the active node into `next_dimension` and `{frontier_block}` for the next dispatch. `convergence.cjs` applies the veto right after the `minIterations` floor and before the gates and guards, as the parent research places it. The order matters on review: `candidateCoverageGate` fails while `searchDebt` is non-empty, so a gate evaluated first would turn every stop with open frontier debt into BLOCKED, and blocked-stop text outranks the frontier focus. On a terminal status the reducer clears the node's debt and records its bucket. At a STOP candidate with a terminal frontier the pivot may run and propose more nodes through admission.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"REQ-007\\\" -A 3 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md | head -10; echo \\\"===plan pivot admission===\\\"; grep -n \\\"pivot\\\" -A 4 -B 2 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md | grep -i \\\"admi\\\\|candidate\\\\|frontier\\\" | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115741664,"end":1795115742312}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115742318,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53c72e2001NPVorF5BP2Odog","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53c5d7e001QnpWr6Ro4PWzrl","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9312a2c24377606b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"admission\\|admit\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts | head -10; echo \"===011 tasks T0 pivot===\"; grep -n \"pivot\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md | head -10"},"output":"===011 tasks T0 pivot===\n64:- [x] T001 Confirm phases 003, 004, 008, 009, 010 and 012 are merged on the working branch (`../003-review-min-iterations-floor/`, `../004-focus-hijack-fix/`, `../008-review-dimension-coverage/`, `../009-fanout-review-coverage-merge/`, `../010-research-frontier-mode/`, `../012-pivot-hygiene/`). Verify: each phase's `implementation-summary.md` names a merged commit and `git branch --contains <sha>` lists the working branch for all six. All six merge commits are on branch 469 (goal.md log, T001 row).\n66:- [x] T003 Capture the golden review baseline: registry, dashboard, Next Focus, rendered pack, pivot seed output and a fan-out lineage prompt with `depthMode` absent (`$U/fixtures/`, path settled at build). Verify: the six baseline files exist and `shasum -a 256` prints one stable hash per file across two runs. Seven baselines in runtime/tests/fixtures/golden-review-default/, stable sha256 across two runs.\n86:- [x] T016 Add the review Next Focus frontier assignment in the last-assignment-wins sequence of the strategy focus block and its dashboard twin, naming the node and its next uncovered dimension (`$D/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`, today `:2173-2187` and `:2271-2274`). Verify: a precedence case shows blocked-stop, then pivot, then frontier, then leaf `nextFocus`, then first uncovered dimension, in both the strategy and dashboard text. Pi dispatch: pickReviewFrontierFocus assigned after the leaf/uncovered base and before the pivot and blocked-stop overrides in the strategy, and between pivot and base in the dashboard twin; precedence case passes in deep-review-state-reducer (45 passed with golden).\n90:- [x] T020 Gate the review pivot on a terminal frontier, seed from `exhausted` and `blocked` nodes and route accepted candidates through admission, on the pivot code and branch as 012 left them (`$D/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `Y` divergent branch). Verify: `$R tests/integration/divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` exits 0 with a gating case, and default seed output matches the T003 baseline byte for byte. Pi dispatch: under the expansive mode buildCandidateSeeds adds a 'frontier-unanswered' seed per exhausted or blocked node and buildReviewPivotPreparationInput refuses an open frontier; the YAML eligibility contract carries frontier_gate and routes an accepted candidate through admission; divergent-pivot + golden review 40 passed (gating, seed and default cases), default pivot seeds byte-identical; typecheck exit 0.\n171:- [x] CHK-011 [P0] No new branch is reachable when `depthMode` is absent or `default` Every new branch is gated on depthMode === 'expansive' (reducer, convergence, fan-out, pivot, YAML enabled_when); review-depth-mode-golden 14 of 14 for absent and default.\n182:- [x] CHK-021 [P0] Golden review test passes for absent key and `--depth-mode=default`, pivot seeds and lineage prompt included review-depth-mode-golden: 14 of 14, pivot seeds and lineage prompt included (lineage prompt with the one stripped paragraph, ADR-005).\n192:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Not a fix packet; every shared-file edit is classed `cross-consumer` and covered by the golden test. Every shared-file edit (reduce-state.cjs, convergence.cjs, fanout-run.cjs, fanout-merge.cjs, frontier-admit.cjs, divergent-review-pivot.ts, deep-review.yaml, the template and the agent) is cross-consumer and gated on the expansive mode; the golden review test covers the default path of each.\n194:- [x] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for `searchDebt`, `candidateCoverage`, `frontier_scope` and `depthMode`. Consumers: searchDebt read by convergence.cjs, review-verdict.cjs, fanout-merge.cjs, divergent-review-pivot.ts and deep-review.yaml; candidateCoverage by convergence.cjs, fanout-merge.cjs and deep-review.yaml; frontier_scope only by fanout-run.cjs prompts; depthMode by deep-review.yaml, reduce-state.cjs, convergence.cjs, fanout-run.cjs and divergent-review-pivot.ts. Open frontier debt makes the verdict CONDITIONAL while nodes are open, which the veto already holds at CONTINUE.\n196:- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes from plan.md listed with their row count before completion is claimed. plan.md matrix: depthMode (absent, default, expansive) x convergenceMode (default, divergent) x executor (single, fan-out) = 12 rows. Absent/default rows: golden review plus the unchanged existing suites; expansive single: reducer, veto, yaml-contract; expansive divergent: divergent-pivot gating; expansive fan-out: fanout-run and fanout-merge. Expansive x divergent x fan-out has no dedicated end-to-end case; the pilot exercises fan-out live.\n208:- [x] CHK-032 [P1] Proposal scope must intersect the configured review target, so neither a leaf nor the pivot can expand it scopeInsideReviewTarget prunes a proposal scoped outside a file-list review target as relevance (frontier-admit-review case); the pivot's boundary regexes and target ban are unchanged.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"===011 tasks T0 pivot===\n64:- [x] T001 Confirm phases 003, 004, 008, 009, 010 and 012 are merged on the working branch (`../003-review-min-iterations-floor/`, `../004-focus-hijack-fix/`, `../008-review-dimension-coverage/`, `../009-fanout-review-coverage-merge/`, `../010-research-frontier-mode/`, `../012-pivot-hygiene/`). Verify: each phase's `implementation-summary.md` names a merged commit and `git branch --contains <sha>` lists the working branch for all six. All six merge commits are on branch 469 (goal.md log, T001 row).\n66:- [x] T003 Capture the golden review baseline: registry, dashboard, Next Focus, rendered pack, pivot seed output and a fan-out lineage prompt with `depthMode` absent (`$U/fixtures/`, path settled at build). Verify: the six baseline files exist and `shasum -a 256` prints one stable hash per file across two runs. Seven baselines in runtime/tests/fixtures/golden-review-default/, stable sha256 across two runs.\n86:- [x] T016 Add the review Next Focus frontier assignment in the last-assignment-wins sequence of the strategy focus block and its dashboard twin, naming the node and its next uncovered dimension (`$D/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs`, today `:2173-2187` and `:2271-2274`). Verify: a precedence case shows blocked-stop, then pivot, then frontier, then leaf `nextFocus`, then first uncovered dimension, in both the strategy and dashboard text. Pi dispatch: pickReviewFrontierFocus assigned after the leaf/uncovered base and before the pivot and blocked-stop overrides in the strategy, and between pivot and base in the dashboard twin; precedence case passes in deep-review-state-reducer (45 passed with golden).\n90:- [x] T020 Gate the review pivot on a terminal frontier, seed from `exhausted` and `blocked` nodes and route accepted candidates through admission, on the pivot code and branch as 012 left them (`$D/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `Y` divergent branch). Verify: `$R tests/integration/divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` exits 0 with a gating case, and default seed output matches the T003 baseline byte for byte. Pi dispatch: under the expansive mode buildCandidateSeeds adds a 'frontier-unanswered' seed per exhausted or blocked node and buildReviewPivotPreparationInput refuses an open frontier; the YAML eligibility contract carries frontier_gate and routes an accepted candidate through admission; divergent-pivot + golden review 40 passed (gating, seed and default cases), default pivot seeds byte-identical; typecheck exit 0.\n171:- [x] CHK-011 [P0] No new branch is reachable when `depthMode` is absent or `default` Every new branch is gated on depthMode === 'expansive' (reducer, convergence, fan-out, pivot, YAML enabled_when); review-depth-mode-golden 14 of 14 for absent and default.\n182:- [x] CHK-021 [P0] Golden review test passes for absent key and `--depth-mode=default`, pivot seeds and lineage prompt included review-depth-mode-golden: 14 of 14, pivot seeds and lineage prompt included (lineage prompt with the one stripped paragraph, ADR-005).\n192:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Not a fix packet; every shared-file edit is classed `cross-consumer` and covered by the golden test. Every shared-file edit (reduce-state.cjs, convergence.cjs, fanout-run.cjs, fanout-merge.cjs, frontier-admit.cjs, divergent-review-pivot.ts, deep-review.yaml, the template and the agent) is cross-consumer and gated on the expansive mode; the golden review test covers the default path of each.\n194:- [x] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for `searchDebt`, `candidateCoverage`, `frontier_scope` and `depthMode`. Consumers: searchDebt read by convergence.cjs, review-verdict.cjs, fanout-merge.cjs, divergent-review-pivot.ts and deep-review.yaml; candidateCoverage by convergence.cjs, fanout-merge.cjs and deep-review.yaml; frontier_scope only by fanout-run.cjs prompts; depthMode by deep-review.yaml, reduce-state.cjs, convergence.cjs, fanout-run.cjs and divergent-review-pivot.ts. Open frontier debt makes the verdict CONDITIONAL while nodes are open, which the veto already holds at CONTINUE.\n196:- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes from plan.md listed with their row count before completion is claimed. plan.md matrix: depthMode (absent, default, expansive) x convergenceMode (default, divergent) x executor (single, fan-out) = 12 rows. Absent/default rows: golden review plus the unchanged existing suites; expansive single: reducer, veto, yaml-contract; expansive divergent: divergent-pivot gating; expansive fan-out: fanout-run and fanout-merge. Expansive x divergent x fan-out has no dedicated end-to-end case; the pilot exercises fan-out live.\n208:- [x] CHK-032 [P1] Proposal scope must intersect the configured review target, so neither a leaf nor the pivot can expand it scopeInsideReviewTarget prunes a proposal scoped outside a file-list review target as relevance (frontier-admit-review case); the pivot's boundary regexes and target ban are unchanged.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"admission\\\\|admit\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts | head -10; echo \\\"===011 tasks T0 pivot===\\\"; grep -n \\\"pivot\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/tasks.md | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115741922,"end":1795115742318}}}}
