{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115746704,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53c84a4001iVb7y1hMhUpzj0","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53c77d1001TYEWtNk9OmptUv","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de4d47a2c75dafb","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"frontier-admit\\|admit\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | sed -n '1,20p'"},"output":"65:  depth_mode: \"[default|expansive] - Opt-in frontier growth. expansive seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes, admits leaf frontier_proposal rows and vetoes a review stop candidate while nodes stay open. Default: default.\"\n352:      command. frontier-admit.cjs writes the node store, and fanout-run.cjs\n355:      file by hand, and never queue or hand-expand the admitted nodes\n357:    command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n360:      - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n906:          # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n942:          run the command. frontier-admit.cjs writes the node store, and\n946:          the admitted nodes yourself.\n947:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n950:          - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n967:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n1613:            command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --node-id \"{active_frontier_node}\" --status exhausted --reason stuck --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n1719:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --node-id \"{active_frontier_node}\" --status active --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n1761:              frontier_block: \"Empty string unless depth_mode == 'expansive' and active_frontier_node is non-empty. Under expansive, the exact stdout of: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs block --target review --artifact-dir \\\"{artifact_dir}\\\" --node-id \\\"{active_frontier_node}\\\" --dimension \\\"{next_dimension}\\\". Pass it verbatim; an empty stdout means the leaf gets no frontier block and proposes nothing.\"\n2039:      step_frontier_admit:\n2051:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs admit --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --input \"{state_paths.delta_pattern with NNN = current_iteration}\" --known-texts \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json\"'\n2054:          - frontier_admit_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"65:  depth_mode: \"[default|expansive] - Opt-in frontier growth. expansive seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes, admits leaf frontier_proposal rows and vetoes a review stop candidate while nodes stay open. Default: default.\"\n352:      command. frontier-admit.cjs writes the node store, and fanout-run.cjs\n355:      file by hand, and never queue or hand-expand the admitted nodes\n357:    command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n360:      - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n906:          # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n942:          run the command. frontier-admit.cjs writes the node store, and\n946:          the admitted nodes yourself.\n947:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n950:          - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n967:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n1613:            command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --node-id \"{active_frontier_node}\" --status exhausted --reason stuck --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n1719:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --node-id \"{active_frontier_node}\" --status active --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n1761:              frontier_block: \"Empty string unless depth_mode == 'expansive' and active_frontier_node is non-empty. Under expansive, the exact stdout of: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs block --target review --artifact-dir \\\"{artifact_dir}\\\" --node-id \\\"{active_frontier_node}\\\" --dimension \\\"{next_dimension}\\\". Pass it verbatim; an empty stdout means the leaf gets no frontier block and proposes nothing.\"\n2039:      step_frontier_admit:\n2051:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs admit --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --input \"{state_paths.delta_pattern with NNN = current_iteration}\" --known-texts \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json\"'\n2054:          - frontier_admit_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"frontier-admit\\\\|admit\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | sed -n '1,20p'\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115746468,"end":1795115746704}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115746711,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53c8390002er0XnoOAYixbS7","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53c77d1001TYEWtNk9OmptUv","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-be081c0f5655ce87","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"REQ-007\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md; echo \"===plan admission detail===\"; grep -n \"accepted candidate\\|through admission\\|pivot\" -B2 -A4 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md | sed -n '1,60p'"},"output":"63:| AC-008 | REQ-007 | Given `--convergence-mode=divergent` and an open review node, When a STOP candidate appears, Then no pivot is prepared; once all nodes are terminal, a pivot may seed from an `exhausted` node and its accepted candidate goes through admission | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npm test -- tests/integration/divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` exits 0 with the gating case. Observed 2026-11-17: `npx vitest run divergent-pivot.vitest` gating case: an open node makes buildReviewPivotPreparationInput refuse; with all nodes terminal one 'frontier-unanswered' seed names the exhausted node; the YAML frontier_gate routes an accepted candidate through step_frontier_admit | Met | - |\n===plan admission detail===\n1----\n2-title: \"Implementation Plan: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-review: admission into candidateCoverage and searchDebt\"\n3:description: \"Builds the review side of --depth-mode=expansive on top of the research frontier: review config and flag, golden review test, review proposal channel, admission into searchDebt and candidateCoverage, review Next Focus branch, veto on review stop candidates, pivot seed changes and the review fan-out partition, then the last-100-commits pilot.\"\n4-trigger_phrases:\n5-  - \"review frontier mode plan\"\n6-importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7-contextType: \"implementation\"\n--\n21-| Aspect | Value |\n22-|--------|-------|\n23:| **Language/Stack** | Node.js CommonJS scripts (`.cjs`), TypeScript runtime and pivot modules, YAML workflow assets |\n24-| **Framework** | `system-deep-loop` deep-review workflow (`/deep:review`) |\n25-| **Storage** | JSONL deltas, the review findings registry (`candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, new `frontier`), the fan-out merged registry |\n26-| **Testing** | vitest suites under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/` |\n27-\n28-### Overview\n29:The change reuses the research phase's flag semantics, admission helper, node-store row shape, seed step, depth budget and veto, and points them at the review coverage surfaces instead of an inbox. Every review branch is gated on `depthMode` being `expansive`. A golden review test, which also covers pivot seed output and the fan-out lineage prompt, lands before any behavior change.\n30-<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31-\n32----\n33-\n--\n43-### Definition of Done\n44-- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n45:- [ ] From `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime`, `npm test` exits 0, including the golden review, review admit, close, steering, pivot and fan-out cases. Vitest run from any other directory finds no `.vitest.ts` file\n46-- [ ] The review compiled contract is regenerated and `check-contract-drift.vitest.ts` passes\n47-- [ ] Reference docs, playbook scenarios, changelog and agent mirrors updated (REQ-015)\n48-- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n49-<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n--\n58-\n59-### Key Components\n60:- **Review proposal channel**: the review pack and agent definition gain the `frontier_proposal` row. Without it a review leaf has no sanctioned way to name a sub-target; today every `frontier` hit in `deep-review.yaml` is the pivot's candidate frontier.\n61-- **Review node-status store (`review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`)**: the phase-010 row shape, written only by `frontier-admit.cjs` in review target mode. Review has no inbox, and `buildSearchLedgerState` (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1764`) rebuilds `candidateCoverage` and `searchDebt` from iteration records on every reduce, so an admitted node handed only to the reducer would vanish on the next reduce.\n62-- **Review seed step**: decomposes the review target into depth-1 nodes before the first iteration, before `step_fanout_spawn` on the fan-out path. The target-1 pruning of merges and index rebuilds happens here.\n63-- **Review admission step**: calls the phase-010 helper in a review target mode; an admitted node becomes a store row, an open `searchDebt` entry and a `registry.frontier` node.\n64-- **Review reducer frontier branch**: projects `registry.frontier` and the frontier debt from the store, tracks per-node dimension coverage, applies the close rule (clear debt, record a `candidateCoverage` bucket) and assigns the advisory Next Focus in the last-assignment-wins sequence.\n65-- **Dispatch steering**: review dispatch reads `next_dimension` (`deep-review.yaml:904`), which today comes from the init-only `dimension_queue`. Under the flag, `step_read_state` reads the active node from `registry.frontier`, sets `next_dimension` to that node's next uncovered dimension and fills `{frontier_block}` in the pack. The reducer's Next Focus text is read only by the agent, so it cannot steer on its own.\n66-- **Veto on review candidates**: the existing `frontierOpen` veto, now reading the review registry for `all_dimensions_clean` and composite candidates.\n67:- **Pivot seed change**: `divergent-review-pivot.ts` waits for a terminal frontier, may seed from `exhausted` or `blocked` nodes and hands an accepted candidate to admission.\n68-- **Review fan-out path**: `config.depthMode` passthrough, `frontier_scope:` beside `review_focus`, the partition recorded in `orchestration-summary.json`, per-lineage stores written before spawn, a merged `frontier` in `mergeReviewRegistries` (`fanout-merge.cjs:981-996` returns none today), and a merge guard over the recorded partition and the phase-009 merged coverage.\n69-\n70-### Data Flow\n71:The seed step writes depth-1 nodes to the store before iteration 1 (and, under fan-out, `fanout-run.cjs` splits them across lineage stores). Review leaf writes `frontier_proposal` rows in its delta. The review admission step prunes or admits and records each outcome in the store; the reducer reads the store and writes `searchDebt`, `registry.frontier` and Next Focus. `step_read_state` then turns the active node into `next_dimension` and `{frontier_block}` for the next dispatch. `convergence.cjs` applies the veto right after the `minIterations` floor and before the gates and guards, as the parent research places it. The order matters on review: `candidateCoverageGate` fails while `searchDebt` is non-empty, so a gate evaluated first would turn every stop with open frontier debt into BLOCKED, and blocked-stop text outranks the frontier focus. On a terminal status the reducer clears the node's debt and records its bucket. At a STOP candidate with a terminal frontier the pivot may run and propose more nodes through admission.\n72-<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n73-\n74----\n75-\n--\n83-| `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` (review block) | Owns review coverage, debt and Next Focus | update, flag-gated | Golden review test with the key absent |\n84-| `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | Owns the review stop order and `candidateCoverageGate` | update, veto unreachable when off | `review-depth-convergence` and `stop-decision*` suites |\n85:| `deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` | Builds review pivot seeds | update, seeds unchanged when off | `divergent-pivot*` suites plus a byte-compare of seed output |\n86-| `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` | Build review lineage prompts with `review_focus`, merge registries | update, binding absent when off | `fanout-review-focus`, `fanout-merge*` suites |\n87-| Phase 010 admission helper | Research admission | update, review target mode added | Research admission suite stays green |\n88-| `step_read_state` `next_dimension` rule and `render_prompt_pack.variables` | Pick the dispatched dimension and fill the pack | update, flag-gated case | `stop-decision-yaml-contract` wording case; golden pack with the flag off |\n89-| Review template and every caller that renders it (`deep-review.yaml`, `prompt-pack.vitest.ts`, `deep-review-marker-scan.vitest.ts`, `tests/fanout-review-focus.vitest.ts`) | Renders every review prompt | update, one empty-by-default `{frontier_block}` token | Golden pack; each caller passes the variable |\n--\n106-## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n107-\n108:Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup records the operator's ADR acceptance, confirms phases 003, 004, 008, 009, 010 and 012 are merged, including 008's custom dimension support, and captures the golden review baseline. Implementation adds config, flag and binding surfaces, the golden assertion, the store and seed step, the proposal channel, admission into the coverage surfaces, the reducer close and focus branch with per-node dimension coverage, dispatch steering, the veto on review candidates, the stuck sub-branch, the pivot seed changes and the fan-out path. Documentation closes the phase. Verification runs the full suite and the target-1 pilot.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"63:| AC-008 | REQ-007 | Given `--convergence-mode=divergent` and an open review node, When a STOP candidate appears, Then no pivot is prepared; once all nodes are terminal, a pivot may seed from an `exhausted` node and its accepted candidate goes through admission | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npm test -- tests/integration/divergent-pivot.vitest.ts` exits 0 with the gating case. Observed 2026-11-17: `npx vitest run divergent-pivot.vitest` gating case: an open node makes buildReviewPivotPreparationInput refuse; with all nodes terminal one 'frontier-unanswered' seed names the exhausted node; the YAML frontier_gate routes an accepted candidate through step_frontier_admit | Met | - |\n===plan admission detail===\n1----\n2-title: \"Implementation Plan: Opt-in expansive depth mode for deep-review: admission into candidateCoverage and searchDebt\"\n3:description: \"Builds the review side of --depth-mode=expansive on top of the research frontier: review config and flag, golden review test, review proposal channel, admission into searchDebt and candidateCoverage, review Next Focus branch, veto on review stop candidates, pivot seed changes and the review fan-out partition, then the last-100-commits pilot.\"\n4-trigger_phrases:\n5-  - \"review frontier mode plan\"\n6-importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7-contextType: \"implementation\"\n--\n21-| Aspect | Value |\n22-|--------|-------|\n23:| **Language/Stack** | Node.js CommonJS scripts (`.cjs`), TypeScript runtime and pivot modules, YAML workflow assets |\n24-| **Framework** | `system-deep-loop` deep-review workflow (`/deep:review`) |\n25-| **Storage** | JSONL deltas, the review findings registry (`candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, new `frontier`), the fan-out merged registry |\n26-| **Testing** | vitest suites under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/` |\n27-\n28-### Overview\n29:The change reuses the research phase's flag semantics, admission helper, node-store row shape, seed step, depth budget and veto, and points them at the review coverage surfaces instead of an inbox. Every review branch is gated on `depthMode` being `expansive`. A golden review test, which also covers pivot seed output and the fan-out lineage prompt, lands before any behavior change.\n30-<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31-\n32----\n33-\n--\n43-### Definition of Done\n44-- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n45:- [ ] From `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime`, `npm test` exits 0, including the golden review, review admit, close, steering, pivot and fan-out cases. Vitest run from any other directory finds no `.vitest.ts` file\n46-- [ ] The review compiled contract is regenerated and `check-contract-drift.vitest.ts` passes\n47-- [ ] Reference docs, playbook scenarios, changelog and agent mirrors updated (REQ-015)\n48-- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n49-<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n--\n58-\n59-### Key Components\n60:- **Review proposal channel**: the review pack and agent definition gain the `frontier_proposal` row. Without it a review leaf has no sanctioned way to name a sub-target; today every `frontier` hit in `deep-review.yaml` is the pivot's candidate frontier.\n61-- **Review node-status store (`review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`)**: the phase-010 row shape, written only by `frontier-admit.cjs` in review target mode. Review has no inbox, and `buildSearchLedgerState` (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1764`) rebuilds `candidateCoverage` and `searchDebt` from iteration records on every reduce, so an admitted node handed only to the reducer would vanish on the next reduce.\n62-- **Review seed step**: decomposes the review target into depth-1 nodes before the first iteration, before `step_fanout_spawn` on the fan-out path. The target-1 pruning of merges and index rebuilds happens here.\n63-- **Review admission step**: calls the phase-010 helper in a review target mode; an admitted node becomes a store row, an open `searchDebt` entry and a `registry.frontier` node.\n64-- **Review reducer frontier branch**: projects `registry.frontier` and the frontier debt from the store, tracks per-node dimension coverage, applies the close rule (clear debt, record a `candidateCoverage` bucket) and assigns the advisory Next Focus in the last-assignment-wins sequence.\n65-- **Dispatch steering**: review dispatch reads `next_dimension` (`deep-review.yaml:904`), which today comes from the init-only `dimension_queue`. Under the flag, `step_read_state` reads the active node from `registry.frontier`, sets `next_dimension` to that node's next uncovered dimension and fills `{frontier_block}` in the pack. The reducer's Next Focus text is read only by the agent, so it cannot steer on its own.\n66-- **Veto on review candidates**: the existing `frontierOpen` veto, now reading the review registry for `all_dimensions_clean` and composite candidates.\n67:- **Pivot seed change**: `divergent-review-pivot.ts` waits for a terminal frontier, may seed from `exhausted` or `blocked` nodes and hands an accepted candidate to admission.\n68-- **Review fan-out path**: `config.depthMode` passthrough, `frontier_scope:` beside `review_focus`, the partition recorded in `orchestration-summary.json`, per-lineage stores written before spawn, a merged `frontier` in `mergeReviewRegistries` (`fanout-merge.cjs:981-996` returns none today), and a merge guard over the recorded partition and the phase-009 merged coverage.\n69-\n70-### Data Flow\n71:The seed step writes depth-1 nodes to the store before iteration 1 (and, under fan-out, `fanout-run.cjs` splits them across lineage stores). Review leaf writes `frontier_proposal` rows in its delta. The review admission step prunes or admits and records each outcome in the store; the reducer reads the store and writes `searchDebt`, `registry.frontier` and Next Focus. `step_read_state` then turns the active node into `next_dimension` and `{frontier_block}` for the next dispatch. `convergence.cjs` applies the veto right after the `minIterations` floor and before the gates and guards, as the parent research places it. The order matters on review: `candidateCoverageGate` fails while `searchDebt` is non-empty, so a gate evaluated first would turn every stop with open frontier debt into BLOCKED, and blocked-stop text outranks the frontier focus. On a terminal status the reducer clears the node's debt and records its bucket. At a STOP candidate with a terminal frontier the pivot may run and propose more nodes through admission.\n72-<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n73-\n74----\n75-\n--\n83-| `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` (review block) | Owns review coverage, debt and Next Focus | update, flag-gated | Golden review test with the key absent |\n84-| `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | Owns the review stop order and `candidateCoverageGate` | update, veto unreachable when off | `review-depth-convergence` and `stop-decision*` suites |\n85:| `deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` | Builds review pivot seeds | update, seeds unchanged when off | `divergent-pivot*` suites plus a byte-compare of seed output |\n86-| `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` | Build review lineage prompts with `review_focus`, merge registries | update, binding absent when off | `fanout-review-focus`, `fanout-merge*` suites |\n87-| Phase 010 admission helper | Research admission | update, review target mode added | Research admission suite stays green |\n88-| `step_read_state` `next_dimension` rule and `render_prompt_pack.variables` | Pick the dispatched dimension and fill the pack | update, flag-gated case | `stop-decision-yaml-contract` wording case; golden pack with the flag off |\n89-| Review template and every caller that renders it (`deep-review.yaml`, `prompt-pack.vitest.ts`, `deep-review-marker-scan.vitest.ts`, `tests/fanout-review-focus.vitest.ts`) | Renders every review prompt | update, one empty-by-default `{frontier_block}` token | Golden pack; each caller passes the variable |\n--\n106-## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n107-\n108:Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup records the operator's ADR acceptance, confirms phases 003, 004, 008, 009, 010 and 012 are merged, including 008's custom dimension support, and captures the golden review baseline. Implementation adds config, flag and binding surfaces, the golden assertion, the store and seed step, the proposal channel, admission into the coverage surfaces, the reducer close and focus branch with per-node dimension coverage, dispatch steering, the veto on review candidates, the stuck sub-branch, the pivot seed changes and the fan-out path. Documentation closes the phase. Verification runs the full suite and the target-1 pilot.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"REQ-007\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md; echo \\\"===plan admission detail===\\\"; grep -n \\\"accepted candidate\\\\|through admission\\\\|pivot\\\" -B2 -A4 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md | sed -n '1,60p'\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115746192,"end":1795115746711}}}}
