{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795115763617,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f53cc7a0001aBRfRnQvjGcPls","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53cbf6e0010VXb7oagcV92nz","type":"step-start","snapshot":"4c9236f16bdc82eee22df161ae89de20b8fee7df"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115770833,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53cc7a6001AO7h0UYl4FIst6","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53cbf6e0010VXb7oagcV92nz","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83823da00512de35","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 3 - F-1-007 correctness: divergent pivot, continuity thread and coverage-graph signals\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension correctness. Node scope: `divergent-pivot.ts`, `divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `divergent-research-pivot.ts`, `divergent-pivot.cjs`, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (two retry control paths and the double config write judged against the current requirement), operator UX (pivot failure reasons, the terminal-frontier gate text, and the accepted-direction handoff), cross-CLI/OS parity (pivot paths remain repo-relative and the retry step exists in both YAMLs).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts` -- attempt identity, preflight, seat-cap per attempt, council paths, pending/finalize, retry loop, lifecycle events.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` -- read-only guard, path-shaped scope stripping, frontier-unanswered seeds, open-frontier gate, identity and seat-usage scoping.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts` -- identity derivation, attempt-aware seat usage.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs` -- prepare/record-seat/finalize surface and retry documentation.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/continuity-thread.cjs` -- carried-forward question filter, leaf-focus step, next-focus precedence.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts` -- `SOURCE_QUALITY_CLASS` vocabulary.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts` -- unclassified sources no longer raise diversity.\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1422-1547` and `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1316-1400` -- divergent branch eligibility, retry re-entry and result application.\n- Traceability sources: `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-007, AC-008 and plan lines 67/71; `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-002/REQ-005/REQ-007/REQ-008; `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **REQ-007 and AC-008 promise pivot-candidate admission the pivot branch never performs** -- .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1429 -- `011` REQ-007 requires that an accepted pivot candidate be \"routed through admission\" (`011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147`), AC-008 repeats it and records the evidence as \"the YAML frontier_gate routes an accepted candidate through step_frontier_admit\" (`011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:63`), and the plan says the pivot \"hands an accepted candidate to admission\" and \"may run and propose more nodes through admission\" (`plan.md:67`, `:71`). The implemented branch says the opposite: \"with the frontier terminal the leaf gets no FRONTIER block, so the pivot adds no frontier node\" (`deep-review.yaml:1429`), and its completed path only sets `next_dimension: \"{pivot_result.restoredFocus}\"` and re-reduces (`:1541-1547`). `step_frontier_admit` reads `frontier_proposal` rows from the iteration delta (`:2051`); the pivot result writes no such row, so no accepted candidate ever reaches the node store.\nFinding class: class-of-bug\nScope proof: `rg -n \"frontier-admit|admit\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` lists the seed, the budget step, the STUCK close, the activation close and `step_frontier_admit`; none sits in the `if_completed` pivot branch at `:1504-1547`. `rg -n \"frontier_proposal\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` prints nothing, so the pivot emits no proposal row for its selected candidate.\nAffected surface hints: [\"deep-review.yaml divergent pivot frontier_gate\", \"deep-review.yaml step_apply_divergent_pivot_result\", \"step_frontier_admit\", \"divergent-review-pivot.ts accepted candidate\", \"011 AC-008 evidence\"]\nCase: a review run closes all frontier nodes, the frontier_drained stop makes the pivot eligible, the Council accepts a read-only direction for a subsystem the frontier closed as exhausted, and the direction becomes only focus text; the frontier store stays terminal, `registry.frontier` gains no node for it, and the next stop can form `frontier_drained` again without the accepted direction ever becoming tracked frontier depth.\n\nClaim adjudication:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"spec-contradiction\",\n  \"claim\": \"The pivot branch adopts an accepted direction as next_dimension and never routes it through frontier admission, contrary to REQ-007 and AC-008.\",\n  \"evidenceRefs\": [\n    \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147\",\n    \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:63\",\n    \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:67\",\n    \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1429\",\n    \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1541\",\n    \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:2051\"\n  ],\n  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Searched the whole review YAML for an admission call in the pivot branch and found only the post-dispatch step that reads iteration deltas; checked the review pivot script for a frontier_proposal writer (none); considered whether 'admission' could mean the pivot's own candidate dedupe, but AC-008 names step_frontier_admit explicitly.\",\n  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The YAML clause reads as a deliberate later decision that a pivot direction should be focus text rather than frontier depth, because a new frontier node would reopen the veto the pivot just passed; if that is the ruling, REQ-007, AC-008 and the plan are the stale surfaces.\",\n  \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade to P2 if 'admission' in REQ-007 is ruled to mean the pivot candidate dedupe rather than step_frontier_admit, or if a later step writes the selected candidate as a frontier proposal.\"\n}\n```\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-002/REQ-005/REQ-007/REQ-008 and `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 match the code (attempt-scoped ids and paths, per-attempt seat cap checked only on open, 3 or 6 recorded outputs, legacy config load, scoped usage). `011` REQ-007's admission clause does not: the pivot completed path adopts focus text only (`deep-review.yaml:1541-1547`). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-008's gating and seed halves are met (`divergent-review-pivot.ts:311-330`, `:398-410`); its admission evidence claim is not met by the branch it cites. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1422-1496` runs prepare, one seat at a time, record-seat, finalize and the one-time retry through the real CLI subcommands; `step_retry_divergent_pivot_once` re-enters prepare once and stops when `pivot_attempt == 2`.\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1316-1400` carries the same retry wiring for the research pivot, so the retry is not review-only.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs:1-25` documents the prepare-only mode ownership and the retry contract the YAML implements.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts:679-690` consumes the `SOURCE_QUALITY_CLASS` vocabulary exported from `coverage-graph-query.ts:138-150`, and `upsert.cjs:236-300` derives the class before the signal reads it.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Attempt 2 lives under `council/attempt-2/` while `config.json`, `state.jsonl` and `report.md` stay shared (`divergent-pivot.ts:844-861`); a resumed attempt 2 therefore reads the shared config, and the config rewrite compares against the attempt-1 record before overwriting. A crash between the two writes leaves attempt 1 persisted with the attempt-failed event durable, which re-enters the same branch on the next prepare.\n- `maxCouncilSeatOutputs` is now per council attempt, so a pivot may record 6 seat returns while the field reads 3 (`divergent-pivot.ts:292`, `:1589`); REQ-002 and REQ-005 require exactly that, so the count is not a lifetime cap.\n- `minRemainingIterations` is still parsed, persisted and accepted but no longer refuses a pivot (`divergent-pivot.ts:749-760`; test at `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts:574-584`); REQ-004 retires the guard deliberately.\n- The research pivot does not seed frontier revisits because the sixth source is specified only in the deep-review convergence reference; the research convergence reference does not carry it.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Attempt identity is complete: seat events, deliberation, seat paths and config `attempt`/`invariants.rounds` are attempt-scoped, attempt-1 ids and paths stay unchanged, and `buildPivotCouncilPaths` rejects any attempt other than 1 or 2.\n- The seat cap is evaluated only when an attempt opens (`durableSeatEvents.size === 0`), so resuming an attempt that already holds two seat returns is not refused.\n- A second quorum miss and an agreement failure both fail closed without a third attempt; `pivot_attempt_failed` is written only for a first-attempt quorum miss.\n- The review pivot refuses an open or active frontier before preparing, seeds only `exhausted` or `blocked` nodes, and strips path-shaped scope entries before the read-only mutation scan.\n- `buildCarriedForwardOpenQuestions` drops resolved and non-question-shaped items only when they are not registry questions, and `deriveNextFocusFromContinuity` places the leaf recommendation ahead of the carried-forward step but behind the terminal sentinel, as REQ-001/REQ-002/REQ-005 require.\n- `computeResearchSourceDiversityFromData` no longer counts `unclassified` as a distinct source kind, and the class vocabulary is derived at the upsert choke point rather than trusted from a leaf.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Retrying the library `runDivergentPivot` loop and the YAML step in two places: the library is the packaged transaction API and the YAML must orchestrate native seat dispatch across steps, so neither can own the other's retry; two instances do not justify a shared abstraction.\n- Recording six seat outputs for an attempt-1 quorum miss that returned only two: REQ-002 explicitly defines the recorded total as `3 * attempt`.\n- Overwriting the pivot config twice when attempt 2 opens: the first write replays the attempt-1 record and the second adopts attempt 2; a crash between them is recoverable and leaves no contradictory state.\n- A research frontier revisit source: missing by design; the sixth source is a deep-review-only sentence.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security on F-1-003 (fan-out runner and merge trust boundaries).\n- Reason: all three dealt nodes now have correctness covered; security is the next uncovered dimension on the first node and the fan-out path handles executor commands, env allowlists and cross-lineage input.\n- Required evidence: `fanout-run.cjs` command construction and env pass-through, `fanout-merge.cjs` input validation, and the executor guard helpers they call.\n- Rotation status: F-1-003, F-1-005 and F-1-007 each have correctness covered; security is uncovered on all three.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 3 - F-1-007 correctness: divergent pivot, continuity thread and coverage-graph signals\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension correctness. Node scope: `divergent-pivot.ts`, `divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `divergent-research-pivot.ts`, `divergent-pivot.cjs`, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (two retry control paths and the double config write judged against the current requirement), operator UX (pivot failure reasons, the terminal-frontier gate text, and the accepted-direction handoff), cross-CLI/OS parity (pivot paths remain repo-relative and the retry step exists in both YAMLs).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts` -- attempt identity, preflight, seat-cap per attempt, council paths, pending/finalize, retry loop, lifecycle events.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` -- read-only guard, path-shaped scope stripping, frontier-unanswered seeds, open-frontier gate, identity and seat-usage scoping.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts` -- identity derivation, attempt-aware seat usage.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs` -- prepare/record-seat/finalize surface and retry documentation.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/continuity-thread.cjs` -- carried-forward question filter, leaf-focus step, next-focus precedence.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts` -- `SOURCE_QUALITY_CLASS` vocabulary.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts` -- unclassified sources no longer raise diversity.\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1422-1547` and `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1316-1400` -- divergent branch eligibility, retry re-entry and result application.\\n- Traceability sources: `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-007, AC-008 and plan lines 67/71; `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-002/REQ-005/REQ-007/REQ-008; `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **REQ-007 and AC-008 promise pivot-candidate admission the pivot branch never performs** -- .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1429 -- `011` REQ-007 requires that an accepted pivot candidate be \\\"routed through admission\\\" (`011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147`), AC-008 repeats it and records the evidence as \\\"the YAML frontier_gate routes an accepted candidate through step_frontier_admit\\\" (`011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:63`), and the plan says the pivot \\\"hands an accepted candidate to admission\\\" and \\\"may run and propose more nodes through admission\\\" (`plan.md:67`, `:71`). The implemented branch says the opposite: \\\"with the frontier terminal the leaf gets no FRONTIER block, so the pivot adds no frontier node\\\" (`deep-review.yaml:1429`), and its completed path only sets `next_dimension: \\\"{pivot_result.restoredFocus}\\\"` and re-reduces (`:1541-1547`). `step_frontier_admit` reads `frontier_proposal` rows from the iteration delta (`:2051`); the pivot result writes no such row, so no accepted candidate ever reaches the node store.\\nFinding class: class-of-bug\\nScope proof: `rg -n \\\"frontier-admit|admit\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` lists the seed, the budget step, the STUCK close, the activation close and `step_frontier_admit`; none sits in the `if_completed` pivot branch at `:1504-1547`. `rg -n \\\"frontier_proposal\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` prints nothing, so the pivot emits no proposal row for its selected candidate.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"deep-review.yaml divergent pivot frontier_gate\\\", \\\"deep-review.yaml step_apply_divergent_pivot_result\\\", \\\"step_frontier_admit\\\", \\\"divergent-review-pivot.ts accepted candidate\\\", \\\"011 AC-008 evidence\\\"]\\nCase: a review run closes all frontier nodes, the frontier_drained stop makes the pivot eligible, the Council accepts a read-only direction for a subsystem the frontier closed as exhausted, and the direction becomes only focus text; the frontier store stays terminal, `registry.frontier` gains no node for it, and the next stop can form `frontier_drained` again without the accepted direction ever becoming tracked frontier depth.\\n\\nClaim adjudication:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"spec-contradiction\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The pivot branch adopts an accepted direction as next_dimension and never routes it through frontier admission, contrary to REQ-007 and AC-008.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\n    \\\"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147\\\",\\n    \\\"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/acceptance-criteria.md:63\\\",\\n    \\\"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/plan.md:67\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1429\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1541\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:2051\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Searched the whole review YAML for an admission call in the pivot branch and found only the post-dispatch step that reads iteration deltas; checked the review pivot script for a frontier_proposal writer (none); considered whether 'admission' could mean the pivot's own candidate dedupe, but AC-008 names step_frontier_admit explicitly.\\\",\\n  \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"The YAML clause reads as a deliberate later decision that a pivot direction should be focus text rather than frontier depth, because a new frontier node would reopen the veto the pivot just passed; if that is the ruling, REQ-007, AC-008 and the plan are the stale surfaces.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"Downgrade to P2 if 'admission' in REQ-007 is ruled to mean the pivot candidate dedupe rather than step_frontier_admit, or if a later step writes the selected candidate as a frontier proposal.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-002/REQ-005/REQ-007/REQ-008 and `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 match the code (attempt-scoped ids and paths, per-attempt seat cap checked only on open, 3 or 6 recorded outputs, legacy config load, scoped usage). `011` REQ-007's admission clause does not: the pivot completed path adopts focus text only (`deep-review.yaml:1541-1547`). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-008's gating and seed halves are met (`divergent-review-pivot.ts:311-330`, `:398-410`); its admission evidence claim is not met by the branch it cites. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1422-1496` runs prepare, one seat at a time, record-seat, finalize and the one-time retry through the real CLI subcommands; `step_retry_divergent_pivot_once` re-enters prepare once and stops when `pivot_attempt == 2`.\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1316-1400` carries the same retry wiring for the research pivot, so the retry is not review-only.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs:1-25` documents the prepare-only mode ownership and the retry contract the YAML implements.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts:679-690` consumes the `SOURCE_QUALITY_CLASS` vocabulary exported from `coverage-graph-query.ts:138-150`, and `upsert.cjs:236-300` derives the class before the signal reads it.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Attempt 2 lives under `council/attempt-2/` while `config.json`, `state.jsonl` and `report.md` stay shared (`divergent-pivot.ts:844-861`); a resumed attempt 2 therefore reads the shared config, and the config rewrite compares against the attempt-1 record before overwriting. A crash between the two writes leaves attempt 1 persisted with the attempt-failed event durable, which re-enters the same branch on the next prepare.\\n- `maxCouncilSeatOutputs` is now per council attempt, so a pivot may record 6 seat returns while the field reads 3 (`divergent-pivot.ts:292`, `:1589`); REQ-002 and REQ-005 require exactly that, so the count is not a lifetime cap.\\n- `minRemainingIterations` is still parsed, persisted and accepted but no longer refuses a pivot (`divergent-pivot.ts:749-760`; test at `divergent-pivot.vitest.ts:574-584`); REQ-004 retires the guard deliberately.\\n- The research pivot does not seed frontier revisits because the sixth source is specified only in the deep-review convergence reference; the research convergence reference does not carry it.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Attempt identity is complete: seat events, deliberation, seat paths and config `attempt`/`invariants.rounds` are attempt-scoped, attempt-1 ids and paths stay unchanged, and `buildPivotCouncilPaths` rejects any attempt other than 1 or 2.\\n- The seat cap is evaluated only when an attempt opens (`durableSeatEvents.size === 0`), so resuming an attempt that already holds two seat returns is not refused.\\n- A second quorum miss and an agreement failure both fail closed without a third attempt; `pivot_attempt_failed` is written only for a first-attempt quorum miss.\\n- The review pivot refuses an open or active frontier before preparing, seeds only `exhausted` or `blocked` nodes, and strips path-shaped scope entries before the read-only mutation scan.\\n- `buildCarriedForwardOpenQuestions` drops resolved and non-question-shaped items only when they are not registry questions, and `deriveNextFocusFromContinuity` places the leaf recommendation ahead of the carried-forward step but behind the terminal sentinel, as REQ-001/REQ-002/REQ-005 require.\\n- `computeResearchSourceDiversityFromData` no longer counts `unclassified` as a distinct source kind, and the class vocabulary is derived at the upsert choke point rather than trusted from a leaf.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Retrying the library `runDivergentPivot` loop and the YAML step in two places: the library is the packaged transaction API and the YAML must orchestrate native seat dispatch across steps, so neither can own the other's retry; two instances do not justify a shared abstraction.\\n- Recording six seat outputs for an attempt-1 quorum miss that returned only two: REQ-002 explicitly defines the recorded total as `3 * attempt`.\\n- Overwriting the pivot config twice when attempt 2 opens: the first write replays the attempt-1 record and the second adopts attempt 2; a crash between them is recoverable and leaves no contradictory state.\\n- A research frontier revisit source: missing by design; the sixth source is a deep-review-only sentence.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security on F-1-003 (fan-out runner and merge trust boundaries).\\n- Reason: all three dealt nodes now have correctness covered; security is the next uncovered dimension on the first node and the fan-out path handles executor commands, env allowlists and cross-lineage input.\\n- Required evidence: `fanout-run.cjs` command construction and env pass-through, `fanout-merge.cjs` input validation, and the executor guard helpers they call.\\n- Rotation status: F-1-003, F-1-005 and F-1-007 each have correctness covered; security is uncovered on all three.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115763622,"end":1795115770833}}}}
