{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115774901,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53cefd4002bqq506Yq22AHid","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53ce7930012qbrgfyx7fwjPY","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-beca96e7e8749e9c","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\n- Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -77,10 +77,10 @@\n \n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n-- Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\n - Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\n+- Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\\n- Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.\", \"oldString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115773908,"end":1795115774901}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115774910,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53cf1ee0012MhemCSntMUs8J","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53ce7930012qbrgfyx7fwjPY","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-90bb08dd2322ee9b","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Iteration 2: treating the duplicated frontier visit/marker code across the two reducers as an overengineering finding failed the two-instance test in `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4; recorded as a ruled-out direction instead.\n- Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \"pivot adds no frontier node\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.","oldString":"- Iteration 2: treating the duplicated frontier visit/marker code across the two reducers as an overengineering finding failed the two-instance test in `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4; recorded as a ruled-out direction instead.","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -85,8 +85,9 @@\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n - Iteration 2: the first read of the extension step looked like `maxIterations += N` was missing a duration-symmetry rule; the AC-004 checkpoint showed the count-plus-N rule is deliberate, so the direction was dropped rather than reported.\n - Iteration 2: treating the duplicated frontier visit/marker code across the two reducers as an overengineering finding failed the two-instance test in `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4; recorded as a ruled-out direction instead.\n+- Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \"pivot adds no frontier node\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Iteration 2: treating the duplicated frontier visit/marker code across the two reducers as an overengineering finding failed the two-instance test in `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4; recorded as a ruled-out direction instead.\\n- Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \\\"pivot adds no frontier node\\\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.\", \"oldString\": \"- Iteration 2: treating the duplicated frontier visit/marker code across the two reducers as an overengineering finding failed the two-instance test in `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4; recorded as a ruled-out direction instead.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115774446,"end":1795115774910}}}}
