{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115782027,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53d0a6f002y9ip3XXmXhn3Ky","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53cf75f001x6n4xQ2tRNcxz7","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a83e014c7f1f1afb","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\n- Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\n- Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/r