irectory and session id below as the detached state boundary.`,\n1699-        ``,\n1700-      ]\n1701-    : lineage.kind === 'native'\n1702-      ? [\n1703-          `This is an explicit native fan-out adapter running through the command host's OpenCode CLI surface.`,\n1704-          `Use the separate lineage directory and session id below as the detached state boundary.`,\n1705-          ``,\n1706-        ]\n1707-      : [];\n1708-  // A CLI lineage subprocess IS the executor for its own iterations. Left unsaid, a leaf reads\n1709-  // the workflow YAML's per-iteration executor-dispatch step literally and spawns a nested CLI\n1710-  // from inside its own sandbox, where nested dispatch is denied — the lineage then burns every\n1711-  // iteration on dispatch failures and produces zero findings. Native lineages run through the\n1712-  // command host and already have their executor bound, so the directive is CLI-only.\n1713-  // A state row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot rebuild,\n1714-  // so the gateway refuses every later projection and the lineage records nothing.\n1715-  const stateLogName = lineageStateLogName(loopType);\n1716-  // The workflow keeps its reducer on the lineage directory during fan-out, and the\n1717-  // merge reads the reducer's dashboard stamp as proof the lineage registry was\n--\n4059:      const prompt = buildLoopPrompt(loopType, specFolder, promptLineageDir, sessionId, lineage, researchTopic, {\n4060-        convergenceThreshold,\n4061-        convergenceMode,\n4062-        depthMode,\n4063-        frontierScope,\n4064-        stopPolicy,\n4065-        reviewFocus,\n4066-        reviewTarget: reviewTargetBinding.target,\n4067-        reviewTargetType: reviewTargetBinding.type,\n4068-      });\n4069-\n4070-      // Sandbox resolution stays write-capable by default even for review lineages:\n4071-      // the review subprocess writes its own iteration artifacts (iterations/iteration-NNN.md,\n4072-      // deep-review-state.jsonl, review-report.md, resource-map.md) INTO lineageDir, so a\n4073-      // blanket read-only default would break those writes. The lineageDir-only write boundary\n4074-      // is enforced by the lineage prompt's explicit write-scope instruction (which also names the\n4075-      // repo tooling a weaker model must not run) rather than by a narrower sandbox; a path-scoped\n4076-      // workspace-write would be the stronger fix if the CLIs exposed one. Callers can still pass an\n4077-      // explicit sandboxMode to override.\n4078-      //\n4079-      // cli-opencode has no OS-level sandbox flag at all, so the generic workspace-write\n4080-      // default would silently ask it to honor a mode it can never enforce. An UNSPECIFIED\n4081-      // sandboxMode for this kind resolves to danger-full-access instead -- the only mode it\n4082-      // can honestly report as effective -- so ordinary dispatch proceeds normally. A caller\n4083-      // that EXPLICITLY asks for read-only/workspace-write still reaches finalizeLineageCommand\n4084-      // unmodified, where that genuine confinement request is rejected.\n4085-      const resolvedSandbox = lineage.kind === 'cli-opencode'\n4086-        && (lineage.sandboxMode === null || lineage.sandboxMode === undefined)\n4087-        ? 'danger-full-access'\n4088-        : resolveSandboxMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n4089-      const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n4090-\n4091-      const effectiveSandbox = resolvedSandbox;\n4092-      const effectivePermission = resolvedPermission;\n4093-\n4094-      const {\n4095-        command,\n4096-        args: cmdArgs,\n4097-        input,\n4098-        cwd: commandCwd,\n4099-        env: commandEnv,\n--\n4865:  buildLoopPrompt,\n4866-  buildNativeCommandInput,\n4867-  normalizeReviewFocus,\n4868-  normalizeDepthMode,\n4869-  partitionFrontierNodes,\n4870-  resolveFrontierPartition,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"co