{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115885799,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53e92ad001BnrqZOKgJnNVue","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53e8a6f001sVOC4F1nxGf4C4","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-818bad62bc1b877c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 4 - F-1-003 security: fan-out runner command construction, env and merge trust boundaries\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-003, dimension security. Node scope: `fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` and their unit suites.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (native and CLI PRE-BOUND blocks compared, two instances ruled out as a pattern), operator UX (review-focus control stripping and length bound, partition and merge warning text), cross-CLI/OS parity (all nine executor adapters, per-kind env filtering, Windows-safe spawn and path handling).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` -- `normalizeReviewFocus`, native command input, detached lineage prompt, spawn wrapper and timeout/stderr caps, all nine executor adapters, per-lineage env assembly.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` -- real-file/containment readers, lineage directory enumeration, frontier merge and partition guard, review finding/traceability merge.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` -- lineage label grammar and config validation (context for path safety).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts` -- per-kind env allowlist applied before the lineage env overlay (context).\n- Traceability sources: `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-008 and `009-fanout-review-coverage-merge` REQ-001..REQ-006.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `011` REQ-008's depth-1 seed before spawn, `depthMode` passthrough, round-robin partition, `frontier_scope:` binding, `frontier_partition` record, per-lineage stores and the merge guard are implemented as written. The only outstanding partial remains iteration 3's REQ-007 admission gap; this iteration found no new contradiction. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `009` REQ-001..REQ-006 merge rules and `011` AC-010/AC-011 fan-out criteria match the code; AC-008's admission claim remains the outstanding partial. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4193-4206` builds each child env as `buildExecutorDispatchEnv(lineage, process.env)` and overlays only the named `SPECKIT_*`, gate-off, graph-store and adapter env keys after the allowlist filter.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4171-4186` re-injects `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED`, `DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR` and the per-kind state dir because the allowlist drops them; these are the values the detached contract depends on.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:1592-1617` enumerates lineage directories from disk and rejects symlinked entries; every read goes through `resolveOptionalRealFile`/`assertSafeOutputPath` with realpath containment.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:778-805` qualifies every merged node id with its lineage label, sorts by label then id, and compares the dealt depth-1 ids against reported local ids so a missing lineage is named.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3492-3515` maps all nine `EXECUTOR_KINDS` to an adapter and throws on an unknown kind.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `cli-opencode` defaults to `danger-full-access` because the CLI exposes no enforceable sandbox flag (`fanout-run.cjs:4079-4088`); the lineage-only write boundary is carried by the prompt and the post-hoc containment guard, a tradeoff the range records in its own comment rather than hiding.\n- A multi-line or control-bearing review focus is collapsed to one bounded line before it reaches the `review_focus:` binding (`fanout-run.cjs:232-247`), so it cannot end the binding early; the focus is also embedded twice for CLI lineages, once as a flag and once as a binding.\n- `spawnSync('/bin/sh', ['-c', 'command -v codex ...'])` is used only for binary detection in `isCodexBinaryAvailable` and the sibling checks; the command string is static, so no lineage/config value reaches a shell.\n- The merge throws on the first unreadable or invalid lineage registry/state log rather than degrading that lineage; this reader predates the range, so it is recorded as context and not as a range finding.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- No executor adapter uses `shell: true`; every argument is built as an argv array, with prompts passed on stdin or as a single argv element.\n- Lineage labels are validated to `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` before they become directory names (`executor-config.ts:889`), and the merge enumerates real directories rather than trusting a label from the summary.\n- The merge rejects symlinked artifact and lineage directories and confirms every read path resolves inside the artifact root.\n- The review-focus and review-target normalizers strip control characters, collapse whitespace and cap length, closing the setup-binding injection path the code documents.\n- Per-kind env allowlists are applied before the fan-out overlay, so credentials for one executor kind do not reach another kind's child by default.\n- The recursion guard requires both an inherited fan-out lineage id and the same kind on the dispatch stack, so a seat cannot silently re-fan-out its own executor.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Shell injection through model, focus, target or node text: no adapter shells out, and the two static `/bin/sh -c command -v` probes carry no input.\n- Prompt injection from an admitted frontier node into a sibling lineage: post-spawn admissions stay in the lineage's own store and prompt; the shared seed questions come from the orchestrator.\n- Treating the whole-merge abort on one corrupt lineage log as a security finding: the throwing readers predate the range and the behavior is fail-closed rather than silently merging a corrupt registry.\n- Extracting the duplicated PRE-BOUND block from `buildNativeCommandInput` and `buildLoopPrompt`: two instances with different delivery surfaces, and `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4 keeps them separate until a third caller appears.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security on F-1-005 (reducers, convergence, upsert and dispatch).\n- Reason: F-1-003 security is clear; the reducer and gateway path handles lineage state, extension events and finding evidence, so it carries the next security risk.\n- Required evidence: `append-mode-event.cjs` authorization/fencing surface, `reduce-state.cjs` path echo and file writes, `upsert.cjs` JSON parsing and graph namespace isolation, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` env propagation.\n- Rotation status: correctness covered on all three nodes; security covered on F-1-003 only.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 4 - F-1-003 security: fan-out runner command construction, env and merge trust boundaries\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-003, dimension security. Node scope: `fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` and their unit suites.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (native and CLI PRE-BOUND blocks compared, two instances ruled out as a pattern), operator UX (review-focus control stripping and length bound, partition and merge warning text), cross-CLI/OS parity (all nine executor adapters, per-kind env filtering, Windows-safe spawn and path handling).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` -- `normalizeReviewFocus`, native command input, detached lineage prompt, spawn wrapper and timeout/stderr caps, all nine executor adapters, per-lineage env assembly.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` -- real-file/containment readers, lineage directory enumeration, frontier merge and partition guard, review finding/traceability merge.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` -- lineage label grammar and config validation (context for path safety).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts` -- per-kind env allowlist applied before the lineage env overlay (context).\\n- Traceability sources: `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-008 and `009-fanout-review-coverage-merge` REQ-001..REQ-006.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `011` REQ-008's depth-1 seed before spawn, `depthMode` passthrough, round-robin partition, `frontier_scope:` binding, `frontier_partition` record, per-lineage stores and the merge guard are implemented as written. The only outstanding partial remains iteration 3's REQ-007 admission gap; this iteration found no new contradiction. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `009` REQ-001..REQ-006 merge rules and `011` AC-010/AC-011 fan-out criteria match the code; AC-008's admission claim remains the outstanding partial. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4193-4206` builds each child env as `buildExecutorDispatchEnv(lineage, process.env)` and overlays only the named `SPECKIT_*`, gate-off, graph-store and adapter env keys after the allowlist filter.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4171-4186` re-injects `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED`, `DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR` and the per-kind state dir because the allowlist drops them; these are the values the detached contract depends on.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:1592-1617` enumerates lineage directories from disk and rejects symlinked entries; every read goes through `resolveOptionalRealFile`/`assertSafeOutputPath` with realpath containment.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:778-805` qualifies every merged node id with its lineage label, sorts by label then id, and compares the dealt depth-1 ids against reported local ids so a missing lineage is named.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3492-3515` maps all nine `EXECUTOR_KINDS` to an adapter and throws on an unknown kind.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `cli-opencode` defaults to `danger-full-access` because the CLI exposes no enforceable sandbox flag (`fanout-run.cjs:4079-4088`); the lineage-only write boundary is carried by the prompt and the post-hoc containment guard, a tradeoff the range records in its own comment rather than hiding.\\n- A multi-line or control-bearing review focus is collapsed to one bounded line before it reaches the `review_focus:` binding (`fanout-run.cjs:232-247`), so it cannot end the binding early; the focus is also embedded twice for CLI lineages, once as a flag and once as a binding.\\n- `spawnSync('/bin/sh', ['-c', 'command -v codex ...'])` is used only for binary detection in `isCodexBinaryAvailable` and the sibling checks; the command string is static, so no lineage/config value reaches a shell.\\n- The merge throws on the first unreadable or invalid lineage registry/state log rather than degrading that lineage; this reader predates the range, so it is recorded as context and not as a range finding.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- No executor adapter uses `shell: true`; every argument is built as an argv array, with prompts passed on stdin or as a single argv element.\\n- Lineage labels are validated to `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` before they become directory names (`executor-config.ts:889`), and the merge enumerates real directories rather than trusting a label from the summary.\\n- The merge rejects symlinked artifact and lineage directories and confirms every read path resolves inside the artifact root.\\n- The review-focus and review-target normalizers strip control characters, collapse whitespace and cap length, closing the setup-binding injection path the code documents.\\n- Per-kind env allowlists are applied before the fan-out overlay, so credentials for one executor kind do not reach another kind's child by default.\\n- The recursion guard requires both an inherited fan-out lineage id and the same kind on the dispatch stack, so a seat cannot silently re-fan-out its own executor.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Shell injection through model, focus, target or node text: no adapter shells out, and the two static `/bin/sh -c command -v` probes carry no input.\\n- Prompt injection from an admitted frontier node into a sibling lineage: post-spawn admissions stay in the lineage's own store and prompt; the shared seed questions come from the orchestrator.\\n- Treating the whole-merge abort on one corrupt lineage log as a security finding: the throwing readers predate the range and the behavior is fail-closed rather than silently merging a corrupt registry.\\n- Extracting the duplicated PRE-BOUND block from `buildNativeCommandInput` and `buildLoopPrompt`: two instances with different delivery surfaces, and `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4 keeps them separate until a third caller appears.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security on F-1-005 (reducers, convergence, upsert and dispatch).\\n- Reason: F-1-003 security is clear; the reducer and gateway path handles lineage state, extension events and finding evidence, so it carries the next security risk.\\n- Required evidence: `append-mode-event.cjs` authorization/fencing surface, `reduce-state.cjs` path echo and file writes, `upsert.cjs` JSON parsing and graph namespace isolation, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` env propagation.\\n- Rotation status: correctness covered on all three nodes; security covered on F-1-003 only.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115881133,"end":1795115885799}}}}
