ges/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -80,8 +80,9 @@\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n - Iteration 1: reading the fan-out partition and merge paths together exposed the prompt and coverage mismatches quickly; the plan section 3 merge rules mapped one-to-one to the code.\n - Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\n - Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.\n+- Iteration 4: following the focus from argv to the setup binding showed the control-strip and length bound close the injection path; walking env assembly from the allowlist to the overlay confirmed per-kind credential filtering.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.\\n- Iteration 4: following the focus from argv to the setup binding showed the control-strip and length bound close the injection path; walking env assembly from the allowlist to the overlay confirmed per-kind credential filtering.\", \"oldString\": \"- Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115889675,"end":1795115890463}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115890472,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53eb57d001Bp32GPkkWAlUfg","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53eaa6a001Q8oVCUHSiwafcz","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6a5d9c44d1ea7f9","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \"pivot adds no frontier node\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.\n- Iteration 4: reading the merge's throwing readers as a security issue failed the range test (they predate the range) and the fail-closed rationale; recorded as context instead.","oldString":"- Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \"pivot adds no frontier node\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -88,8 +88,9 @@\n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n - Iteration 2: the first read of the extension step looked like `maxIterations += N` was missing a duration-symmetry rule; the AC-004 checkpoint showed the count-plus-N rule is deliberate, so the direction was dropped rather than reported.\n - Iteration 2: treating the duplicated frontier visit/marker code across the two reducers as an overengineering finding failed the two-instance test in `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4; recorded as a ruled-out direction instead.\n - Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \"pivot adds no frontier node\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.\n+- Iteration 4: reading the merge's throwing readers as a security issue failed the range test (they predate the range) and the fail-closed rationale; recorded as context instead.\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \\\"pivot adds no frontier node\\\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.\\n- Iteration 4: reading the merge's throwing readers as a security issue failed the range test (they predate the range) and the fail-closed rationale; recorded as context instead.\", \"oldString\": \"- Iteration 3: the first read of the review pivot treated the YAML's \\\"pivot adds no frontier node\\\" clause as the settled design; the acceptance criterion says the opposite, so the mismatch became the finding rather than a pass.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115890045,"end":1795115890472}}}}
