{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795115940501,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f53f7884002Qv7KASHb5Sb4O3","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f53f57fc001Jbjvg7LFye4y0D","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8135a62cceac936f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"REQ-00\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/spec.md | head -12"},"output":"99:| REQ-001 | A leaf-supplied `quality_class` never reaches the stored node, and `path` outranks the label | An `upsert-script` case upserts a research SOURCE node with `path: \".skilled/agents/deep-research.md\"`, a free-text label and `metadata.quality_class: \"primary\"`; the stored metadata holds the class derived from the path, not `primary` and not `unclassified` |\n100:| REQ-002 | Every stored research SOURCE `quality_class` is in the closed vocabulary | An `upsert-script` case upserts SOURCE nodes identified by a repo code path, a test path, a spec path, a skill doc, a state ledger file, an external doc URL, another URL and free text, and gets `repo-code`, `repo-test`, `repo-spec`, `skill-doc`, `ledger-state`, `external-doc`, `external-other` and `unclassified` |\n101:| REQ-003 | The vocabulary is one frozen constant beside `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS` | `rg -n \"Object.freeze\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts` prints the constant within 20 lines of `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS`, and `upsert.cjs` reads it instead of repeating the values |\n102:| REQ-004 | Source diversity rises only with distinct derived classes | A `convergence-script` case with two findings citing two sources of different derived classes reports `sourceDiversity` 2.0; the same case with both sources in one class reports 1.0. A code-only fixture whose question is answered from a `.cjs` file and its `.vitest.ts` test reports 2.0 and raises no `source_diversity_guard` blocker (`convergence.cjs:448`) |\n108:| REQ-005 | Non-SOURCE nodes and review nodes keep their metadata unchanged | An `upsert-script` case upserts a FINDING with `metadata.confidence` and a review node, and both store their metadata as given |\n109:| REQ-006 | The four named suites pass after the fixture move | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run tests/unit/coverage-graph-signals.vitest.ts tests/integration/convergence-script.vitest.ts tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts` exits 0 |\n110:| REQ-007 | The signal change has a playbook scenario | `/create:manual-testing-playbook system-deep-loop update --path .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook` has written one scenario, and `rg -l \"quality_class\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph` lists it |\n129:| Risk | Default-path behavior changes: the graph `sourceDiversity` signal now carries values on normal research runs, where it read 0 before, so graph-based stop decisions can change (parent §20, \"LOW-MEDIUM, signal tightens\") | Low-Medium | REQ-004 pins the arithmetic; state the change in the phase changelog note |\n131:| Risk | A question answered from a single derived class, such as only `.cjs` files, scores 1.0 and stays blocked by `source_diversity_guard` (threshold 1.5, `convergence.cjs:437`, blocker at :448). Code-only runs that cite code and tests pass | Medium | Intended: the signal measures class diversity. The REQ-004 code-only fixture pins the passing case; a lower threshold or a source-count rule would amend goal decision D3 |\n146:- **Exact path rules per class** (for example, whether `.skilled/skills/**/SKILL.md` is `skill-doc` and `.skilled/skills/**/*.cjs` is `repo-code`) are fixed in the REQ-002 case; the implementer writes the table there and keeps it the only copy.\n147:- **Does a code-only run pass?** When its questions cite at least two derived classes, such as code and tests, yes (REQ-004 fixture). A single-class question blocks by design.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"99:| REQ-001 | A leaf-supplied `quality_class` never reaches the stored node, and `path` outranks the label | An `upsert-script` case upserts a research SOURCE node with `path: \".skilled/agents/deep-research.md\"`, a free-text label and `metadata.quality_class: \"primary\"`; the stored metadata holds the class derived from the path, not `primary` and not `unclassified` |\n100:| REQ-002 | Every stored research SOURCE `quality_class` is in the closed vocabulary | An `upsert-script` case upserts SOURCE nodes identified by a repo code path, a test path, a spec path, a skill doc, a state ledger file, an external doc URL, another URL and free text, and gets `repo-code`, `repo-test`, `repo-spec`, `skill-doc`, `ledger-state`, `external-doc`, `external-other` and `unclassified` |\n101:| REQ-003 | The vocabulary is one frozen constant beside `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS` | `rg -n \"Object.freeze\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts` prints the constant within 20 lines of `SAFE_METADATA_KEYS`, and `upsert.cjs` reads it instead of repeating the values |\n102:| REQ-004 | Source diversity rises only with distinct derived classes | A `convergence-script` case with two findings citing two sources of different derived classes reports `sourceDiversity` 2.0; the same case with both sources in one class reports 1.0. A code-only fixture whose question is answered from a `.cjs` file and its `.vitest.ts` test reports 2.0 and raises no `source_diversity_guard` blocker (`convergence.cjs:448`) |\n108:| REQ-005 | Non-SOURCE nodes and review nodes keep their metadata unchanged | An `upsert-script` case upserts a FINDING with `metadata.confidence` and a review node, and both store their metadata as given |\n109:| REQ-006 | The four named suites pass after the fixture move | `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run tests/unit/coverage-graph-signals.vitest.ts tests/integration/convergence-script.vitest.ts tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts tests/unit/deep-research-graph-upsert.vitest.ts` exits 0 |\n110:| REQ-007 | The signal change has a playbook scenario | `/create:manual-testing-playbook system-deep-loop update --path .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook` has written one scenario, and `rg -l \"quality_class\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph` lists it |\n129:| Risk | Default-path behavior changes: the graph `sourceDiversity` signal now carries values on normal research runs, where it read 0 before, so graph-based stop decisions can change (parent §20, \"LOW-MEDIUM, signal tightens\") | Low-Medium | REQ-004 pins the arithmetic; state the change in the phase changelog note |\n131:| Risk | A question answered from a single derived class, such as only `.cjs` files, scores 1.0 and stays blocked by `source_diversity_guard` (threshold 1.5, `convergence.cjs:437`, blocker at :448). Code-only runs that cite code and tests pass | Medium | Intended: the signal measures class diversity. The REQ-004 code-only fixture pins the passing case; a lower threshold or a source-count rule would amend goal decision D3 |\n146:- **Exact path rules per class** (for example, whether `.skilled/skills/**/SKILL.md` is `skill-doc` and `.skilled/skills/**/*.cjs` is `repo-code`) are fixed in the REQ-002 case; the implementer writes the table there and keeps it the only copy.\n147:- **Does a code-only run pass?** When its questions cite at least two derived classes, such as code and tests, yes (REQ-004 fixture). A single-class question blocks by design.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"REQ-00\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/007-source-diversity-quality-class/spec.md | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1795115939972,"end":1795115940501}}}}
