{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795115998400,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f5405cc0001n9l651SPu8ExpQ","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54052c3001xgNSm8H06Ne0Zk","type":"step-start","snapshot":"0bf40c34b68d56d16e4b90a04eaf22db5095b034"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116007033,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5406a20002nUqaZo7UPtAfxB","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54052c3001xgNSm8H06Ne0Zk","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-abe13d0494ff8a1c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 6 - F-1-007 security: pivot persisted input, council paths and frontier graph projection\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension security. Node scope: `divergent-pivot.ts` and its mode scripts and CLI, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (attempt-scoped ids vs a parallel path builder), operator UX (failure reasons and the terminal-frontier refusal), cross-CLI/OS parity (path containment uses `realpath`, and council artifact names stay portable).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts` -- persisted config parsing, council path construction, artifact root and ai-council guards, event store, seat report parsing.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs` -- argv parsing for prepare/record-seat/finalize.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` -- candidate seeds and the read-only boundary scan.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs` -- `buildFrontierGraphEvents` node/edge shape and metadata.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts`, `coverage-graph-query.ts` -- relation vocabulary, metadata sanitization and parameterized queries.\n- Traceability sources: `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008, `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-001..REQ-009.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-001..REQ-009 match the pivot code; `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 match the frontier graph projection. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission gap remains the only outstanding partial. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `012` AC rows for retry, agreement failure and seat scope match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:839-842` rejects an artifact root that canonicalizes inside an ai-council tree, and `:844-861` builds every council path under the pivot root.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1201-1211` parses a persisted pivot config through a strict field-by-field validator before any seat or event write.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs:35-70` parses each subcommand's argv into a typed call and never interpolates a value into a shell.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:995-1042` emits `DERIVED_FROM` edges, which `coverage-graph-db.ts:226` admits for the research loop the research frontier step runs under.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts:123-142` allowlists metadata keys and `:250-270` sanitizes every value to a scalar, so leaf metadata cannot reach the graph as a nested payload.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `finalize` accepts the caller's `--paths-json` and writes through it rather than re-deriving the council paths; the workflow binds that JSON from its own `prepare` result, so a leaf cannot reach it, but the CLI itself would honor a hand-written path set.\n- A resumed attempt reuses the persisted `usageAtStart` and `limits`, so a tampered pivot config could raise its own caps; the leaf already holds write access to its lineage, and the coverage of that write is containment, so this is recorded as a trust-model note rather than a finding.\n- `buildFrontierGraphEvents` writes the node question into the graph `name`; admission bounds the stored text, and the graph read path sanitizes only metadata, so a long question stays a long display name rather than an executable payload.\n- PRAGMA and schema-migration statements are fixed strings; every row value in the new path is bound as a parameter, including namespace fields.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The pivot config parser rejects an unknown attempt, a rounds value that disagrees with the attempt, a missing limit and a non-integer usage before any write.\n- The artifact-root guard resolves the prospective real path and refuses an ai-council tree, so a symlinked or nested artifact root cannot redirect council artifacts into a reserved directory.\n- Seat outputs are parsed as JSON objects with an exact seat id and candidate ids; a partial or malformed report is rejected rather than coerced.\n- The read-only boundary scan inspects title and focus after path-shaped scope entries are removed, so a path name cannot smuggle a mutation verb.\n- Coverage-graph reads expose only allowlisted scalar metadata, and all relation and node-kind values are validated against per-loop vocabularies before storage.\n- The research frontier's `DERIVED_FROM` edge is in the research relation vocabulary and is never emitted for a review run.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A review-run `DERIVED_FROM` write: the research frontier graph step is the only caller, and the review relation vocabulary excludes it.\n- SQL injection through node names, metadata or namespace values: every value is bound, and the only interpolated SQL fragments are fixed column/table names.\n- Treating the caller-provided `--paths-json` as a boundary bypass: only the orchestrator calls `finalize`, and it passes its own prepare output.\n- Treating the reused persisted pivot limits as a range security defect: the reuse is a documented deviation that keeps a resumed prepare from conflicting with its own recorded state, and the leaf already owns its lineage writes.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability on F-1-003 (fan-out runner and merge against the review packet requirements).\n- Reason: security is covered on all three nodes; traceability is the next dimension in the rotation and the fan-out merge carries the cross-lineage evidence the final report cites.\n- Required evidence: `011` REQ-008 and `009` REQ-001..REQ-006 against `fanout-run.cjs`/`fanout-merge.cjs`, plus the merged report's provenance fields.\n- Rotation status: correctness and security covered on all nodes; traceability uncovered on all three.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 6 - F-1-007 security: pivot persisted input, council paths and frontier graph projection\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension security. Node scope: `divergent-pivot.ts` and its mode scripts and CLI, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (attempt-scoped ids vs a parallel path builder), operator UX (failure reasons and the terminal-frontier refusal), cross-CLI/OS parity (path containment uses `realpath`, and council artifact names stay portable).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts` -- persisted config parsing, council path construction, artifact root and ai-council guards, event store, seat report parsing.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs` -- argv parsing for prepare/record-seat/finalize.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts` -- candidate seeds and the read-only boundary scan.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs` -- `buildFrontierGraphEvents` node/edge shape and metadata.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts`, `coverage-graph-query.ts` -- relation vocabulary, metadata sanitization and parameterized queries.\\n- Traceability sources: `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008, `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-001..REQ-009.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-001..REQ-009 match the pivot code; `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 match the frontier graph projection. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission gap remains the only outstanding partial. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `012` AC rows for retry, agreement failure and seat scope match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:839-842` rejects an artifact root that canonicalizes inside an ai-council tree, and `:844-861` builds every council path under the pivot root.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1201-1211` parses a persisted pivot config through a strict field-by-field validator before any seat or event write.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs:35-70` parses each subcommand's argv into a typed call and never interpolates a value into a shell.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:995-1042` emits `DERIVED_FROM` edges, which `coverage-graph-db.ts:226` admits for the research loop the research frontier step runs under.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-query.ts:123-142` allowlists metadata keys and `:250-270` sanitizes every value to a scalar, so leaf metadata cannot reach the graph as a nested payload.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `finalize` accepts the caller's `--paths-json` and writes through it rather than re-deriving the council paths; the workflow binds that JSON from its own `prepare` result, so a leaf cannot reach it, but the CLI itself would honor a hand-written path set.\\n- A resumed attempt reuses the persisted `usageAtStart` and `limits`, so a tampered pivot config could raise its own caps; the leaf already holds write access to its lineage, and the coverage of that write is containment, so this is recorded as a trust-model note rather than a finding.\\n- `buildFrontierGraphEvents` writes the node question into the graph `name`; admission bounds the stored text, and the graph read path sanitizes only metadata, so a long question stays a long display name rather than an executable payload.\\n- PRAGMA and schema-migration statements are fixed strings; every row value in the new path is bound as a parameter, including namespace fields.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The pivot config parser rejects an unknown attempt, a rounds value that disagrees with the attempt, a missing limit and a non-integer usage before any write.\\n- The artifact-root guard resolves the prospective real path and refuses an ai-council tree, so a symlinked or nested artifact root cannot redirect council artifacts into a reserved directory.\\n- Seat outputs are parsed as JSON objects with an exact seat id and candidate ids; a partial or malformed report is rejected rather than coerced.\\n- The read-only boundary scan inspects title and focus after path-shaped scope entries are removed, so a path name cannot smuggle a mutation verb.\\n- Coverage-graph reads expose only allowlisted scalar metadata, and all relation and node-kind values are validated against per-loop vocabularies before storage.\\n- The research frontier's `DERIVED_FROM` edge is in the research relation vocabulary and is never emitted for a review run.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A review-run `DERIVED_FROM` write: the research frontier graph step is the only caller, and the review relation vocabulary excludes it.\\n- SQL injection through node names, metadata or namespace values: every value is bound, and the only interpolated SQL fragments are fixed column/table names.\\n- Treating the caller-provided `--paths-json` as a boundary bypass: only the orchestrator calls `finalize`, and it passes its own prepare output.\\n- Treating the reused persisted pivot limits as a range security defect: the reuse is a documented deviation that keeps a resumed prepare from conflicting with its own recorded state, and the leaf already owns its lineage writes.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability on F-1-003 (fan-out runner and merge against the review packet requirements).\\n- Reason: security is covered on all three nodes; traceability is the next dimension in the rotation and the fan-out merge carries the cross-lineage evidence the final report cites.\\n- Required evidence: `011` REQ-008 and `009` REQ-001..REQ-006 against `fanout-run.cjs`/`fanout-merge.cjs`, plus the merged report's provenance fields.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security covered on all nodes; traceability uncovered on all three.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116001824,"end":1795116007033}}}}
