{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116011352,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5408c49002IE1xpa5VTp75S0","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f540839a0017NEa31Ufp39AzT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a0e2ce33b07404","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Iteration 5: tracing path shapes through the new source-quality classifier found the POSIX-only split; the rest of the reducer and upsert path handled every state input without a shell or an out-of-packet write.\n- Iteration 6: reading the pivot config parser beside its writer confirmed the persistence contract is strict; the graph query path's allowlist and parameter binding closed the metadata and SQL surfaces.","oldString":"- Iteration 5: tracing path shapes through the new source-quality classifier found the POSIX-only split; the rest of the reducer and upsert path handled every state input without a shell or an out-of-packet write.","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -82,8 +82,9 @@\n - Iteration 2: governing the reducer against the review doctrine caught the `thought`-visit gap in the new frontier projection; reading the extension step beside its ledger schema confirmed the count-plus-N arithmetic is intentional (AC-004), not an off-by-one.\n - Iteration 3: reading the pivot acceptance criterion beside the YAML branch exposed the admission promise the branch does not keep; the attempt-scoped ids and paths held up under a resume and crash-window read.\n - Iteration 4: following the focus from argv to the setup binding showed the control-strip and length bound close the injection path; walking env assembly from the allowlist to the overlay confirmed per-kind credential filtering.\n - Iteration 5: tracing path shapes through the new source-quality classifier found the POSIX-only split; the rest of the reducer and upsert path handled every state input without a shell or an out-of-packet write.\n+- Iteration 6: reading the pivot config parser beside its writer confirmed the persistence contract is strict; the graph query path's allowlist and parameter binding closed the metadata and SQL surfaces.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Iteration 5: tracing path shapes through the new source-quality classifier found the POSIX-only split; the rest of the reducer and upsert path handled every state input without a shell or an out-of-packet write.\\n- Iteration 6: reading the pivot config parser beside its writer confirmed the persistence contract is strict; the graph query path's allowlist and parameter binding closed the metadata and SQL surfaces.\", \"oldStrin