{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116037301,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f540f1a8002y4snhEnRfwrFLa","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f540e329001YlYdWIOSQQb3Z6","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b823527448bf3f97","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rln \"frontier_proposal\\|depth-mode=expansive\\|expansive\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -15; echo \"===pivot admission claims===\"; grep -rn \"admission\\|admit\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -15"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/state-management/config-management.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/expansive-depth-mode.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/divergent-convergence-mode.md\n===pivot admission claims===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22:The workflow admits only the exact reason `all_dimensions_clean`, after all nine legal-stop gates have run. Candidate sources include unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer paths, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects missing-evidence and mutation-shaped directions. The shared adapter runs three native seats in one round. A first-attempt quorum miss gets a one-time quorum retry of the same three seats, so one pivot uses at most six seat outputs. The adapter persists the transaction under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, and continues with the selected read-only direction.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:16:`--depth-mode` takes `default` or `expansive`. A review without the flag is unchanged. `expansive` seeds depth-one sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows under the research caps with two differences, a root-children cap of at least 8 against research's 6 and a relevance check that prunes a proposal scoped outside a file-list review target, keeps node status in `review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`, and holds open nodes as `searchDebt`. This page describes the shipped code and its tests.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:24:The expansive run seeds depth-one sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1. Leaf `frontier_proposal` rows are admitted under relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order. On a commit-range target, the seed prunes a merge commit with no diff of its own as `merge-no-own-diff` and a generated index rebuild as `generated-artifact`.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:59:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs` | Script | Admits review proposals as node-store rows; the reducer files the nodes it leaves open as `searchDebt`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:70:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/frontier-admit-review.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Review admission into the node store. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:74:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/frontier-admission-prunes-with-reasons.md` | Manual playbook | DRV-078: admission prunes a proposal with its reason. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/state-management/config-management.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/expansive-depth-mode.md\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/convergence/divergent-convergence-mode.md\n===pivot admission claims===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22:The workflow admits only the exact reason `all_dimensions_clean`, after all nine legal-stop gates have run. Candidate sources include unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer paths, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects missing-evidence and mutation-shaped directions. The shared adapter runs three native seats in one round. A first-attempt quorum miss gets a one-time quorum retry of the same three seats, so one pivot uses at most six seat outputs. The adapter persists the transaction under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, and continues with the selected read-only direction.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:16:`--depth-mode` takes `default` or `expansive`. A review without the flag is unchanged. `expansive` seeds depth-one sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows under the research caps with two differences, a root-children cap of at least 8 against research's 6 and a relevance check that prunes a proposal scoped outside a file-list review target, keeps node status in `review/frontier-nodes.jsonl`, and holds open nodes as `searchDebt`. This page describes the shipped code and its tests.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:24:The expansive run seeds depth-one sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1. Leaf `frontier_proposal` rows are admitted under relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order. On a commit-range target, the seed prunes a merge commit with no diff of its own as `merge-no-own-diff` and a generated index rebuild as `generated-artifact`.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:59:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs` | Script | Admits review proposals as node-store rows; the reducer files the nodes it leaves open as `searchDebt`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:70:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/frontier-admit-review.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Review admission into the node store. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:74:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/frontier-admission-prunes-with-reasons.md` | Manual playbook | DRV-078: admission prunes a proposal with its reason. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rln \\\"frontier_proposal\\\\|depth-mode=expansive\\\\|expansive\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -15; echo \\\"===pivot admission claims===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"admission\\\\|admit\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116036520,"end":1795116037301}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116037313,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f540f2ea001rPORlE3rc96QC2","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f540e329001YlYdWIOSQQb3Z6","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b216437475f90077","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"frontier_drained\\|frontierOpen\\|pivot.*admit\\|revisit\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/quality-gates.md:35:| `hotspotSaturationGate` | Review hotspots revisited enough to satisfy saturation |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22:The workflow admits only the exact reason `all_dimensions_clean`, after all nine legal-stop gates have run. Candidate sources include unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer paths, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects missing-evidence and mutation-shaped directions. The shared adapter runs three native seats in one round. A first-attempt quorum miss gets a one-time quorum retry of the same three seats, so one pivot uses at most six seat outputs. The adapter persists the transaction under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, and continues with the selected read-only direction.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:34:A review stop candidate becomes another iteration while nodes stay open. The `frontierOpen` veto applies to the review stop candidates, including `all_dimensions_clean` and the composite stop, after the minIterations floor. Once every node is closed and at least one was answered, a run that forms no other stop candidate gets `frontier_drained`, which the legal-stop gates still decide.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:38:An expansive run adds a `## 10B. FRONTIER` section to its review dashboard, and a default run renders no such section. The section reports the frontier size by status, the pruned count, the revisits that covered no new dimension, each budget band's spent and allotted iterations, and the active node with its next dimension.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:79:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md` | Manual playbook | DRV-083: a drained frontier forms the `frontier_drained` stop. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates that under the expansive mode a review whose frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node forms the frontier_drained hard stop candidate, and that the legal-stop gates and every earlier stop rule still decide it, for `DRV-083`.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:15:This scenario validates the `frontier_drained` stop candidate in the review stop decision for `DRV-083`. The objective is to confirm that a drained frontier forms a stop candidate when neither the clean stop nor the composite vote does, that the legal-stop gates still decide it, and that it never forms on a default run or on a frontier that closed with nothing answered.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:27:- Objective: Confirm that `frontier_drained` forms only under the expansive mode, once the frontier holds at least one node, none open or active, and at least one answered, that the legal-stop gates and the graph decision still decide it, that the cap, the floor, stuck recovery, consecutive failures, convergence off and the max-iterations policy keep their own decisions, and that the clean stop ranks first.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:29:- Prompt: `Check that under expansive depth mode a review whose frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node forms the frontier_drained stop candidate, that the legal-stop gates still decide it, and that a default run or a frontier closed with nothing answered forms no candidate. Return a PASS or FAIL verdict with the reason.`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:31:- Expected signals: All 21 drained-frontier cases pass. The headline case returns `STOP` with stop reason `converged`, `frontier_drained` and no blocking gate. A failed hotspot gate, an active P0 and unsettled traceability each block the stop, with the named gate as the reason. An open node, an empty partition, a missing node count, a frontier with no answered node, a missing answered count and a default run each return `CONTINUE` with `noStopCandidate`. The earlier stop rules keep their own decisions. The clean stop outranks the drained candidate. The workflow prose lists `frontier_drained` after `composite_converged` and before the floor and the gates, and the research stop order does not name it.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:46:- Prompt: `Check that under expansive depth mode a review whose frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node forms the frontier_drained stop candidate, that the legal-stop gates still decide it, and that a default run or a frontier closed with nothing answered forms no candidate. Return a PASS or FAIL verdict with the reason.`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:50:1. `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run stop-decision.vitest -t \"review frontier_drained candidate\" --reporter=verbose`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:52:3. `rg -n -F \"reasonDetail: 'frontier_drained'\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:56:Command 1 prints `Tests  21 passed` (the rest of the file skipped). The fixture case `the fixture forms no other candidate` returns `CONTINUE` with `noStopCandidate` once the expansive flag is removed, which shows that only the drained frontier forms the stop. The case `stops a drained lineage whose gates all pass` returns `STOP` with stop reason `converged`, `frontier_drained`, graph decision `STOP_ALLOWED` and an empty `blockedBy`. The table rows name each gate, guard and earlier rule, and the row `an open node keeps the lineage running` returns `CONTINUE` with `noStopCandidate`, since the candidate does not form while a node is open. The case `ranks after the clean candidate` returns `all_dimensions_clean`. The case `counts every frontier node as the partition size` asserts that the stop input counts answered, pruned and exhausted nodes toward the node total, with one answered and none open.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:58:Command 2 prints `Tests  2 passed` (the rest of the file skipped). One case asserts that the review stop-order prose lists `frontier_drained` after `composite_converged` and before `minIterationsNotReached` and the legal-stop gates. The other asserts that the research stop order does not contain it.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:96:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | The `frontier_drained` branch after the clean and composite candidates, and the node counts in the review stop input |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:97:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` | The review stop-order prose that lists `frontier_drained` with the candidates |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates that under the expansive mode the review divergent pivot refuses to run while a frontier node stays open, seeds one revisit direction per closed sub-target the frontier left uncovered and leaves a default run untouched, for `DRV-081`.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md:15:This scenario validates the review divergent pivot gate for `DRV-081`. It focuses on the refusal while a frontier node is open, on the revisit directions the pivot seeds from sub-targets the frontier closed without covering every dimension, and on the default run, which keeps the pivot exactly as before.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md:25:Operators run the commands below and confirm that the pivot waits for a terminal frontier, seeds a revisit for each closed sub-target it left uncovered, and leaves the default run alone.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/quality-gates.md:35:| `hotspotSaturationGate` | Review hotspots revisited enough to satisfy saturation |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22:The workflow admits only the exact reason `all_dimensions_clean`, after all nine legal-stop gates have run. Candidate sources include unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer paths, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Under `--depth-mode=expansive`, a sixth source seeds one revisit direction for each frontier node the run closed `exhausted` or `blocked`. Candidate generation rejects missing-evidence and mutation-shaped directions. The shared adapter runs three native seats in one round. A first-attempt quorum miss gets a one-time quorum retry of the same three seats, so one pivot uses at most six seat outputs. The adapter persists the transaction under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, and continues with the selected read-only direction.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:34:A review stop candidate becomes another iteration while nodes stay open. The `frontierOpen` veto applies to the review stop candidates, including `all_dimensions_clean` and the composite stop, after the minIterations floor. Once every node is closed and at least one was answered, a run that forms no other stop candidate gets `frontier_drained`, which the legal-stop gates still decide.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:38:An expansive run adds a `## 10B. FRONTIER` section to its review dashboard, and a default run renders no such section. The section reports the frontier size by status, the pruned count, the revisits that covered no new dimension, each budget band's spent and allotted iterations, and the active node with its next dimension.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:79:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md` | Manual playbook | DRV-083: a drained frontier forms the `frontier_drained` stop. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates that under the expansive mode a review whose frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node forms the frontier_drained hard stop candidate, and that the legal-stop gates and every earlier stop rule still decide it, for `DRV-083`.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:15:This scenario validates the `frontier_drained` stop candidate in the review stop decision for `DRV-083`. The objective is to confirm that a drained frontier forms a stop candidate when neither the clean stop nor the composite vote does, that the legal-stop gates still decide it, and that it never forms on a default run or on a frontier that closed with nothing answered.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:27:- Objective: Confirm that `frontier_drained` forms only under the expansive mode, once the frontier holds at least one node, none open or active, and at least one answered, that the legal-stop gates and the graph decision still decide it, that the cap, the floor, stuck recovery, consecutive failures, convergence off and the max-iterations policy keep their own decisions, and that the clean stop ranks first.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:29:- Prompt: `Check that under expansive depth mode a review whose frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node forms the frontier_drained stop candidate, that the legal-stop gates still decide it, and that a default run or a frontier closed with nothing answered forms no candidate. Return a PASS or FAIL verdict with the reason.`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:31:- Expected signals: All 21 drained-frontier cases pass. The headline case returns `STOP` with stop reason `converged`, `frontier_drained` and no blocking gate. A failed hotspot gate, an active P0 and unsettled traceability each block the stop, with the named gate as the reason. An open node, an empty partition, a missing node count, a frontier with no answered node, a missing answered count and a default run each return `CONTINUE` with `noStopCandidate`. The earlier stop rules keep their own decisions. The clean stop outranks the drained candidate. The workflow prose lists `frontier_drained` after `composite_converged` and before the floor and the gates, and the research stop order does not name it.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:46:- Prompt: `Check that under expansive depth mode a review whose frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node forms the frontier_drained stop candidate, that the legal-stop gates still decide it, and that a default run or a frontier closed with nothing answered forms no candidate. Return a PASS or FAIL verdict with the reason.`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:50:1. `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run stop-decision.vitest -t \"review frontier_drained candidate\" --reporter=verbose`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:52:3. `rg -n -F \"reasonDetail: 'frontier_drained'\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:56:Command 1 prints `Tests  21 passed` (the rest of the file skipped). The fixture case `the fixture forms no other candidate` returns `CONTINUE` with `noStopCandidate` once the expansive flag is removed, which shows that only the drained frontier forms the stop. The case `stops a drained lineage whose gates all pass` returns `STOP` with stop reason `converged`, `frontier_drained`, graph decision `STOP_ALLOWED` and an empty `blockedBy`. The table rows name each gate, guard and earlier rule, and the row `an open node keeps the lineage running` returns `CONTINUE` with `noStopCandidate`, since the candidate does not form while a node is open. The case `ranks after the clean candidate` returns `all_dimensions_clean`. The case `counts every frontier node as the partition size` asserts that the stop input counts answered, pruned and exhausted nodes toward the node total, with one answered and none open.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:58:Command 2 prints `Tests  2 passed` (the rest of the file skipped). One case asserts that the review stop-order prose lists `frontier_drained` after `composite_converged` and before `minIterationsNotReached` and the legal-stop gates. The other asserts that the research stop order does not contain it.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:96:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | The `frontier_drained` branch after the clean and composite candidates, and the node counts in the review stop input |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:97:| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` | The review stop-order prose that lists `frontier_drained` with the candidates |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates that under the expansive mode the review divergent pivot refuses to run while a frontier node stays open, seeds one revisit direction per closed sub-target the frontier left uncovered and leaves a default run untouched, for `DRV-081`.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md:15:This scenario validates the review divergent pivot gate for `DRV-081`. It focuses on the refusal while a frontier node is open, on the revisit directions the pivot seeds from sub-targets the frontier closed without covering every dimension, and on the default run, which keeps the pivot exactly as before.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md:25:Operators run the commands below and confirm that the pivot waits for a terminal frontier, seeds a revisit for each closed sub-target it left uncovered, and leaves the default run alone.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"frontier_drained\\\\|frontierOpen\\\\|pivot.*admit\\\\|revisit\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116036842,"end":1795116037313}}}}
