{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116054623,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f541235a001cGGOWEaCdh3Fa5","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5410d89001p73vYV9CsfxMOs","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9509aaebfa755252","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 7 - F-1-003 traceability: fan-out runner and merge against the review packet\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-003, dimension traceability. Node scope: `fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` and their unit suites, with the packet docs, feature catalogs and playbooks as traceability evidence.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (catalog and playbook prose checked against one code rule), operator UX (the dashboard/report text the merge produces), cross-CLI/OS parity (all runtime mirrors checked for the new agent contract).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` -- partition, per-lineage prompt, budget derivation and lineage store.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` -- merged coverage, frontier and provenance.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md` -- the shipped-behavior claims for depth coverage, stop behavior and pivot.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md` -- the pivot candidate and retry claims.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md` and `review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md` -- the DRV-083 and DRV-081 commands and expectations.\n- `.skilled/agents/deep-review.md` and `.skilled/agents/deep-research.md` against `.claude/agents`, `.codex/agents`, `.pi/agents`, `.dsh/agents` and `.vibe/agents` -- the new frontier/proposal contract in every mirror.\n- Traceability sources: `009-fanout-review-coverage-merge` REQ-001..REQ-006, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-008/REQ-017, `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-002/REQ-005/REQ-007.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `011` REQ-008's seed, partition, `frontier_scope`, store and merge guard match the code; REQ-017's candidate order and gate chain match `convergence.cjs`. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission gap remains the only partial. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-010/AC-011 fan-out rows match; AC-008 remains the outstanding row. |\n| `skill_agent` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md` expands the depth mode, the veto and the frontier row contract the agent definition carries (`.skilled/agents/deep-review.md`, `frontier_proposal` section). |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The three new agent-contract additions (frontier proposal rows, frontierNodeId, the CLI output contract) appear in `.skilled/agents`, `.claude/agents`, `.codex/agents`, `.pi/agents`, `.dsh/agents` and `.vibe/agents`; the diffs differ only in runtime frontmatter and the path-convention line. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | The expansive-depth catalog matches seeding, band budget, stop order and dashboard. Its dimension-coverage sentence says \"only an attempt that produced evidence counts\" but lists only `error`/`failed`/`failure`/`timeout`; the code also counts `thought` and `stuck`, which is the code side of R2-P1-001. |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | DRV-081 names the pivot gate, the `frontier-unanswered` seed and the default-path case; DRV-083 names the 21 drained-frontier cases and the exact test and rg commands. Both match the code's steps and messages. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22` says the adapter \"continues with the selected read-only direction\" and does not claim frontier admission; the feature catalog therefore agrees with the implemented branch and disagrees with AC-008, which narrows the fix for R3-P1-001 to the acceptance criterion and plan text.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:34` matches the `frontier_drained` ordering and the gate chain in `convergence.cjs:1164-1217`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:50-58` cites the stop-decision suite name and the `rg` command the code actually exposes.\n- `.skilled/agents/deep-review.md` and all five mirrors carry the same `frontier_proposal` contract; the `.claude`/`.pi` diffs are the runtime frontmatter and path-convention lines only.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The catalog's \"produced evidence\" sentence and its status list disagree with each other; I recorded the conflict against the existing R2-P1-001 rather than opening a second finding for the same rule.\n- The `.vibe` mirror is generated from the canonical agent by `sync-agents-vibe.cjs`; its instruction string carries the full contract, so a hash comparison against the markdown canonical would be misleading.\n- The packet's `Met` rows for AC-008 are the traceability defect surface; the code and catalog agree with each other, so the resolution is a packet amendment unless the operator wants the admission behavior.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The fan-out review partition, per-lineage budget and merge guard are documented in REQ-008 and implemented line-for-line.\n- The feature catalog's band-budget, derived-budget and ledger-store claims match `frontier-admit.cjs` and `reduce-state.cjs`.\n- Both new playbooks cite commands and test names that exist and match the current code.\n- Every runtime mirror carries the new agent contract; no mirror is stale for this range.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A new finding for the catalog's \"produced evidence\" sentence: the same rule is already R2-P1-001, and splitting it would double-count one defect across code and docs.\n- A stale-mirror finding: all six agent surfaces carry the new contract, so the differences are runtime packaging only.\n- A playbook/code mismatch: the DRV-081 and DRV-083 commands and named cases exist as written.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability on F-1-005 (reducers, extension and graph evidence against the packet).\n- Reason: F-1-003 is traceable and its only gap is the shared REQ-007 claim; F-1-005 carries the extension, ledger-projection and evidence-edge requirements that the report cites.\n- Required evidence: `001` REQ-002/REQ-004, `006` REQ-001..REQ-004 and `011` REQ-018/AС-019 against `reduce-state.cjs`, `upsert.cjs`, the ledger schema and the projections.\n- Rotation status: correctness and security covered on all nodes; traceability covered on F-1-003.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 7 - F-1-003 traceability: fan-out runner and merge against the review packet\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-003, dimension traceability. Node scope: `fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` and their unit suites, with the packet docs, feature catalogs and playbooks as traceability evidence.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (catalog and playbook prose checked against one code rule), operator UX (the dashboard/report text the merge produces), cross-CLI/OS parity (all runtime mirrors checked for the new agent contract).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` -- partition, per-lineage prompt, budget derivation and lineage store.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` -- merged coverage, frontier and provenance.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md` -- the shipped-behavior claims for depth coverage, stop behavior and pivot.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md` -- the pivot candidate and retry claims.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md` and `review-pivot-gates-on-terminal-frontier.md` -- the DRV-083 and DRV-081 commands and expectations.\\n- `.skilled/agents/deep-review.md` and `.skilled/agents/deep-research.md` against `.claude/agents`, `.codex/agents`, `.pi/agents`, `.dsh/agents` and `.vibe/agents` -- the new frontier/proposal contract in every mirror.\\n- Traceability sources: `009-fanout-review-coverage-merge` REQ-001..REQ-006, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-008/REQ-017, `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-002/REQ-005/REQ-007.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `011` REQ-008's seed, partition, `frontier_scope`, store and merge guard match the code; REQ-017's candidate order and gate chain match `convergence.cjs`. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission gap remains the only partial. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-010/AC-011 fan-out rows match; AC-008 remains the outstanding row. |\\n| `skill_agent` | pass | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md` expands the depth mode, the veto and the frontier row contract the agent definition carries (`.skilled/agents/deep-review.md`, `frontier_proposal` section). |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The three new agent-contract additions (frontier proposal rows, frontierNodeId, the CLI output contract) appear in `.skilled/agents`, `.claude/agents`, `.codex/agents`, `.pi/agents`, `.dsh/agents` and `.vibe/agents`; the diffs differ only in runtime frontmatter and the path-convention line. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | The expansive-depth catalog matches seeding, band budget, stop order and dashboard. Its dimension-coverage sentence says \\\"only an attempt that produced evidence counts\\\" but lists only `error`/`failed`/`failure`/`timeout`; the code also counts `thought` and `stuck`, which is the code side of R2-P1-001. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | DRV-081 names the pivot gate, the `frontier-unanswered` seed and the default-path case; DRV-083 names the 21 drained-frontier cases and the exact test and rg commands. Both match the code's steps and messages. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22` says the adapter \\\"continues with the selected read-only direction\\\" and does not claim frontier admission; the feature catalog therefore agrees with the implemented branch and disagrees with AC-008, which narrows the fix for R3-P1-001 to the acceptance criterion and plan text.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:34` matches the `frontier_drained` ordering and the gate chain in `convergence.cjs:1164-1217`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-recovery/frontier-drained-stops-review.md:50-58` cites the stop-decision suite name and the `rg` command the code actually exposes.\\n- `.skilled/agents/deep-review.md` and all five mirrors carry the same `frontier_proposal` contract; the `.claude`/`.pi` diffs are the runtime frontmatter and path-convention lines only.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The catalog's \\\"produced evidence\\\" sentence and its status list disagree with each other; I recorded the conflict against the existing R2-P1-001 rather than opening a second finding for the same rule.\\n- The `.vibe` mirror is generated from the canonical agent by `sync-agents-vibe.cjs`; its instruction string carries the full contract, so a hash comparison against the markdown canonical would be misleading.\\n- The packet's `Met` rows for AC-008 are the traceability defect surface; the code and catalog agree with each other, so the resolution is a packet amendment unless the operator wants the admission behavior.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The fan-out review partition, per-lineage budget and merge guard are documented in REQ-008 and implemented line-for-line.\\n- The feature catalog's band-budget, derived-budget and ledger-store claims match `frontier-admit.cjs` and `reduce-state.cjs`.\\n- Both new playbooks cite commands and test names that exist and match the current code.\\n- Every runtime mirror carries the new agent contract; no mirror is stale for this range.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A new finding for the catalog's \\\"produced evidence\\\" sentence: the same rule is already R2-P1-001, and splitting it would double-count one defect across code and docs.\\n- A stale-mirror finding: all six agent surfaces carry the new contract, so the differences are runtime packaging only.\\n- A playbook/code mismatch: the DRV-081 and DRV-083 commands and named cases exist as written.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability on F-1-005 (reducers, extension and graph evidence against the packet).\\n- Reason: F-1-003 is traceable and its only gap is the shared REQ-007 claim; F-1-005 carries the extension, ledger-projection and evidence-edge requirements that the report cites.\\n- Required evidence: `001` REQ-002/REQ-004, `006` REQ-001..REQ-004 and `011` REQ-018/AС-019 against `reduce-state.cjs`, `upsert.cjs`, the ledger schema and the projections.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security covered on all nodes; traceability covered on F-1-003.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116049242,"end":1795116054623}}}}
