{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116077988,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f541907e001jAcM5p0E8jktTf","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54183f4001F8gAGHCKUcXR06","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9727defc81d562d6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && ls .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/ .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"===extend claims===\"; grep -rn \"maxIterations\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/*.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/*.md 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"extend\\|continued\" | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/:\ncompleted-run-extension.md\nconvergence-check.md\nfanout-dispatch.md\ninitialization.md\niteration-dispatch.md\nloop-wide-dry-run.md\nmemory-save.md\nper-iteration-memory-upsert.md\nresource-map-emission.md\nrun-now-control.md\nsynthesis.md\n\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/:\ncompleted-run-extension.md\nconvergence-check.md\nexecutor-selection-contract.md\nexpansive-depth-mode.md\nfanout-dispatch.md\ninitialization.md\niteration-dispatch.md\nmemory-save.md\nmin-iterations-floor.md\nresource-map-coverage-gate.md\nresource-map-emission.md\nsynthesis.md\n===extend claims===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/initialization.md:27:Lineage handling is narrower than some older drafts. The runtime supports `new`, `resume`, `restart`, and `completed-continue`. Resume keeps the same session identifier and appends a typed `resumed` event. Restart archives the old research tree, mints a fresh session identifier, increments generation, and appends a typed `restarted` event. `completed-continue` is live through `--extend=N` on a completed run: it keeps the session identifier and generation, sets `maxIterations` to the iterations run so far plus N, appends a typed `run_extended` event, and copies the prior synthesis to a versioned snapshot before the first new iteration.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/:\ncompleted-run-extension.md\nconvergence-check.md\nfanout-dispatch.md\ninitialization.md\niteration-dispatch.md\nloop-wide-dry-run.md\nmemory-save.md\nper-iteration-memory-upsert.md\nresource-map-emission.md\nrun-now-control.md\nsynthesis.md\n\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/:\ncompleted-run-extension.md\nconvergence-check.md\nexecutor-selection-contract.md\nexpansive-depth-mode.md\nfanout-dispatch.md\ninitialization.md\niteration-dispatch.md\nmemory-save.md\nmin-iterations-floor.md\nresource-map-coverage-gate.md\nresource-map-emission.md\nsynthesis.md\n===extend claims===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/initialization.md:27:Lineage handling is narrower than some older drafts. The runtime supports `new`, `resume`, `restart`, and `completed-continue`. Resume keeps the same session identifier and appends a typed `resumed` event. Restart archives the old research tree, mints a fresh session identifier, increments generation, and appends a typed `restarted` event. `completed-continue` is live through `--extend=N` on a completed run: it keeps the session identifier and generation, sets `maxIterations` to the iterations run so far plus N, appends a typed `run_extended` event, and copies the prior synthesis to a versioned snapshot before the first new iteration.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && ls .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/ .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/ 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"===extend claims===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"maxIterations\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/*.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/*.md 2>/dev/null | grep -i \\\"extend\\\\|continued\\\" | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116077182,"end":1795116077988}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116077999,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f54191ca001dVz4S5acwNbFY7","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54183f4001F8gAGHCKUcXR06","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3bbddbf6adb515d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"continuedFromRun\\|count plus\\|prior max\\|+ N\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -10; echo \"===evidence edge catalog===\"; grep -rn \"EVIDENCE_FOR\\|evidence density\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:17:`--extend=N` reopens a completed review run in the same session and generation and adds `N` iterations. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event, and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. `--extend-minutes=M` sets the same extension's duration budget to the later of the prior budget and the minutes already elapsed since `createdAt`, plus M.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:37:The `run_extended` stem is part of the deep-review ledger schema, and the deep-review reducer routes it. The schema refuses an event whose `newMaxIterations` is not `continuedFromRun` plus `addedIterations`, the ceiling the extend step derives, since the reducer adopts it as the run's cap. `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` reads the extension through its live lineage modes.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:51:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts` | Shared | Projects `deep_review.run_extended` into the `extended` state-log row with `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun` and `extension`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:17:`--extend=N` reopens a completed research run in the same session and generation and adds `N` iterations. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event, and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. `--extend-minutes=M` sets the same extension's duration budget to the later of the prior budget and the minutes already elapsed since `createdAt`, plus M.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:37:The `run_extended` stem is part of the deep-research ledger schema, and the deep-research reducer routes it. The schema refuses an event whose `newMaxIterations` is not `continuedFromRun` plus `addedIterations`, the ceiling the extend step derives, since the reducer adopts it as the run's cap. The lifecycle event filters in `deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` read the same event.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:51:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts` | Shared | Projects `deep_research.run_extended` into the `extended` state-log row with `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun` and `extension`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:58:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts` | Vitest | `run_extended` payload: the new ceiling must equal `continuedFromRun` plus `addedIterations`; the legacy extended row upcast refuses one without a full budget. |\n===evidence edge catalog===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:524:The legal-stop bundle combines evidence, scope, coverage, P0 resolution, evidence density, hotspot saturation, and claim adjudication checks. When a stop vote fails those checks, the loop persists a `blocked_stop` event and continues with a recovery hint instead of silently stopping.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:17:`--extend=N` reopens a completed review run in the same session and generation and adds `N` iterations. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event, and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md` before re-synthesis. `--extend-minutes=M` sets the same extension's duration budget to the later of the prior budget and the minutes already elapsed since `createdAt`, plus M.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:37:The `run_extended` stem is part of the deep-review ledger schema, and the deep-review reducer routes it. The schema refuses an event whose `newMaxIterations` is not `continuedFromRun` plus `addedIterations`, the ceiling the extend step derives, since the reducer adopts it as the run's cap. `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` reads the extension through its live lineage modes.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:51:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-review-state-contract.ts` | Shared | Projects `deep_review.run_extended` into the `extended` state-log row with `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun` and `extension`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:17:`--extend=N` reopens a completed research run in the same session and generation and adds `N` iterations. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event, and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. `--extend-minutes=M` sets the same extension's duration budget to the later of the prior budget and the minutes already elapsed since `createdAt`, plus M.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:37:The `run_extended` stem is part of the deep-research ledger schema, and the deep-research reducer routes it. The schema refuses an event whose `newMaxIterations` is not `continuedFromRun` plus `addedIterations`, the ceiling the extend step derives, since the reducer adopts it as the run's cap. The lifecycle event filters in `deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` read the same event.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:51:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/legacy-projections/deep-research-contract.ts` | Shared | Projects `deep_research.run_extended` into the `extended` state-log row with `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun` and `extension`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:58:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts` | Vitest | `run_extended` payload: the new ceiling must equal `continuedFromRun` plus `addedIterations`; the legacy extended row upcast refuses one without a full budget. |\n===evidence edge catalog===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:524:The legal-stop bundle combines evidence, scope, coverage, P0 resolution, evidence density, hotspot saturation, and claim adjudication checks. When a stop vote fails those checks, the loop persists a `blocked_stop` event and continues with a recovery hint instead of silently stopping.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"continuedFromRun\\\\|count plus\\\\|prior max\\\\|+ N\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -10; echo \\\"===evidence edge catalog===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"EVIDENCE_FOR\\\\|evidence density\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog 2>/dev/null | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116077514,"end":1795116077999}}}}
