{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116097648,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f541ccbc002SJXynsD3CVVUab","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f541bb660011Ck0HCijPAzzdi","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc63ef60d9fe6edd","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 8 - F-1-005 traceability: extension, state-log fields and evidence edges against the packet\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-005, dimension traceability. Node scope: the two reducers, `upsert.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` and the five `runtime/lib` folders, with packet docs and catalogs as evidence.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (the extension and evidence rules restated across schema, catalog and playbook), operator UX (the `--extend` catalog wording and the warning text), cross-CLI/OS parity (the projection's leaf fields on both loops).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`, `reduce-state.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` -- the requirement surfaces for this node.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema`, `deep-review-reducers`, `legacy-projections` -- extension and leaf-field projections.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md` and the deep-research twin -- the shipped-behavior claims for `--extend`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts` and `tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts` -- the cases the acceptance rows name.\n- Traceability sources: `001-completed-run-extension` REQ-002/REQ-004 and AC-004/AC-005, `006-state-log-leaf-fields` REQ-001..REQ-004, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-018 and AC-019.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `001` REQ-002/REQ-004 match `deep-review.yaml:528-611`, the ledger schema and the projection; `006` REQ-001..REQ-004 match the gateway projection and `verify-iteration.cjs:497-570`; `011` REQ-018/AC-019 match `upsert.cjs:236-300` and the six integration cases. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-004/AC-005 are pinned by `workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:812` and `:1057`; AC-019 by `upsert-script.vitest.ts:377-642`; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | The completed-run-extension pages say the ceiling is `continuedFromRun + N` and the duration is the later of prior budget and elapsed time, which matches the code and AC-004/AC-005. The expansive-depth page's produced-evidence sentence remains the earlier R2-P1-001 doc side. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:812` and `:1057` assert the count-plus-N ceiling and the elapsed-time duration rule for research and review.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts:377-642` covers the evidence edge, the delta-sourced ref, the id fold, the reused id, the ref without a line and the trailing column.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts:455-461` asserts the review graph step passes `--state-log`, `--delta-dir` and `--iteration`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:17-37` matches the code's `continuedFromRun + addedIterations` schema check and the `extended` projection.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The AC-019 row cites a commit and a full-suite count rather than a local run; I verified the cases exist by name and read the code they exercise, but I did not execute the suite in this detached lineage (the workflow forbids writing the graph DB outside the lineage).\n- The extension catalog says the flag \"adds N iterations\" and later defines the ceiling as count-plus-N; both statements are true for the flag's meaning, so the shorter phrasing is not a contradiction.\n- The `feature_catalog_code` result stays partial because the earlier catalog sentence is still in the shipped page; a per-iteration pass cannot clear it.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Every extension requirement has a named test that exists and asserts the same arithmetic the code performs.\n- Every evidence-edge requirement has an integration case, including the reused-id and no-line cases.\n- The review and research catalogs agree on the extension semantics and the projection fields.\n- The YAML contract case proves the graph step passes the three new flags the upsert requires.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Re-reporting the extension arithmetic as a defect: the catalog, tests and code agree on count-plus-N.\n- Re-reporting the evidence-edge code as untested: six integration cases cover the stated shapes.\n- A projection-parity finding between research and review: both project `extended` rows with lineage mode, `continuedFromRun` and the budget, and the review row carries the leaf fields this lineage's state log shows.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability on F-1-007 (pivot and continuity against the packet).\n- Reason: F-1-005 is traceable; F-1-007 is the last node without traceability, and its requirements carry the retry and quality-class rules the catalogs cite.\n- Required evidence: `012` REQ-001..REQ-009, `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 and `007` REQ-001..REQ-007 against the pivot, continuity and graph code and their catalog/playbook pages.\n- Rotation status: correctness and security covered on all nodes; traceability covered on F-1-003 and F-1-005.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 8 - F-1-005 traceability: extension, state-log fields and evidence edges against the packet\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-005, dimension traceability. Node scope: the two reducers, `upsert.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` and the five `runtime/lib` folders, with packet docs and catalogs as evidence.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (the extension and evidence rules restated across schema, catalog and playbook), operator UX (the `--extend` catalog wording and the warning text), cross-CLI/OS parity (the projection's leaf fields on both loops).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`, `reduce-state.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` -- the requirement surfaces for this node.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema`, `deep-review-reducers`, `legacy-projections` -- extension and leaf-field projections.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md` and the deep-research twin -- the shipped-behavior claims for `--extend`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts` and `tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts` -- the cases the acceptance rows name.\\n- Traceability sources: `001-completed-run-extension` REQ-002/REQ-004 and AC-004/AC-005, `006-state-log-leaf-fields` REQ-001..REQ-004, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-018 and AC-019.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `001` REQ-002/REQ-004 match `deep-review.yaml:528-611`, the ledger schema and the projection; `006` REQ-001..REQ-004 match the gateway projection and `verify-iteration.cjs:497-570`; `011` REQ-018/AC-019 match `upsert.cjs:236-300` and the six integration cases. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-004/AC-005 are pinned by `workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:812` and `:1057`; AC-019 by `upsert-script.vitest.ts:377-642`; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | The completed-run-extension pages say the ceiling is `continuedFromRun + N` and the duration is the later of prior budget and elapsed time, which matches the code and AC-004/AC-005. The expansive-depth page's produced-evidence sentence remains the earlier R2-P1-001 doc side. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-restart-lifecycle.vitest.ts:812` and `:1057` assert the count-plus-N ceiling and the elapsed-time duration rule for research and review.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/upsert-script.vitest.ts:377-642` covers the evidence edge, the delta-sourced ref, the id fold, the reused id, the ref without a line and the trailing column.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/stop-decision-yaml-contract.vitest.ts:455-461` asserts the review graph step passes `--state-log`, `--delta-dir` and `--iteration`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/completed-run-extension.md:17-37` matches the code's `continuedFromRun + addedIterations` schema check and the `extended` projection.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The AC-019 row cites a commit and a full-suite count rather than a local run; I verified the cases exist by name and read the code they exercise, but I did not execute the suite in this detached lineage (the workflow forbids writing the graph DB outside the lineage).\\n- The extension catalog says the flag \\\"adds N iterations\\\" and later defines the ceiling as count-plus-N; both statements are true for the flag's meaning, so the shorter phrasing is not a contradiction.\\n- The `feature_catalog_code` result stays partial because the earlier catalog sentence is still in the shipped page; a per-iteration pass cannot clear it.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Every extension requirement has a named test that exists and asserts the same arithmetic the code performs.\\n- Every evidence-edge requirement has an integration case, including the reused-id and no-line cases.\\n- The review and research catalogs agree on the extension semantics and the projection fields.\\n- The YAML contract case proves the graph step passes the three new flags the upsert requires.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Re-reporting the extension arithmetic as a defect: the catalog, tests and code agree on count-plus-N.\\n- Re-reporting the evidence-edge code as untested: six integration cases cover the stated shapes.\\n- A projection-parity finding between research and review: both project `extended` rows with lineage mode, `continuedFromRun` and the budget, and the review row carries the leaf fields this lineage's state log shows.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability on F-1-007 (pivot and continuity against the packet).\\n- Reason: F-1-005 is traceable; F-1-007 is the last node without traceability, and its requirements carry the retry and quality-class rules the catalogs cite.\\n- Required evidence: `012` REQ-001..REQ-009, `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 and `007` REQ-001..REQ-007 against the pivot, continuity and graph code and their catalog/playbook pages.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security covered on all nodes; traceability covered on F-1-003 and F-1-005.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116092604,"end":1795116097648}}}}
