vidence-edge rows resolve to named tests and matching projections; only the REQ-007 admission claim and the catalog sentence already inside R2-P1-001 remain partial.', iteration: 8 },\\n  { type: 'ruled_out', direction: 'The extension arithmetic as a traceability defect', reason: 'Catalog, code and the two named tests all state continuedFromRun plus N.', iteration: 8 },\\n  { type: 'ruled_out', direction: 'The evidence-edge code as untested', reason: 'Six integration cases cover the stated shapes including reused id and no-line.', iteration: 8 },\\n  { type: 'ruled_out', direction: 'Research/review extension projection parity drift', reason: 'Both project extended rows with lineage mode, continuedFromRun and the budget; the review projection carries the leaf fields observed in this lineage.', iteration: 8 }\\n];\\nfs.writeFileSync(dir + '/deltas/iter-008.jsonl', [rec, ...rows.map((row) => JSON.stringify(row))].join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n');\\nNODE\\nnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek --event-json specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/logs/iter-008-event.json; echo \\\"GATEWAY_EXIT:$?\\\"; node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode --artifact-dir specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek --create-missing-anchors; echo \\\"REDUCER_EXIT:$?\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116110628,"end":1795116112664}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1795116113595,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f5421ebb0012f771cRyje8FFi","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5420ab20014f56vYESV2qs4G","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"a2ffa1628a805068fa4cd1b2ead97b57deecd6eb","cost":0.002299976,"tokens":{"input":1197,"output":585,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":398144,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795116116351,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f542297f001YBKRFmQdWbxSCi","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5421ec1001Iquz5Tc6XNHqlP","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a2ffa1628a805068fa4cd1b2ead97b57deecd6eb"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116117202,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5422b37002OzFoVOK1dzRZUZ","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5421ec1001Iquz5Tc6XNHqlP","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a017d369083bda63","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && sed -n '40,52p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md"},"output":"### Pivot\n\nThe divergent review pivot runs only once the frontier is terminal. It seeds only from nodes closed `exhausted` or `blocked`; an `abstained` node is terminal but never seeds it, and an accepted candidate becomes the next review direction through `restoredFocus`. The pivot writes no frontier node.\n\n### Fan-Out\n\nFan-out lineages receive a share of the seeded nodes. `runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` returns the merged review frontier and runs the review fan-in guard over the recorded partition. A recorded partition with at least one dealt node builds the merged frontier even when no review lineage reports one, so a lost node still surfaces. Each fan-out CLI lineage keeps its coverage graph in `graph-db/` inside its own directory: `fanout-run.cjs` exports `DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR` to it, so the graph steps stay inside the lineage write surface instead of the shared runtime database.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Pivot\n\nThe divergent review pivot runs only once the frontier is terminal. It seeds only from nodes closed `exhausted` or `blocked`; an `abstained` node is terminal but never seeds it, and an accepted candidate becomes the next review direction through `restoredFocus`. The pivot writes no frontier node.\n\n### Fan-Out\n\nFan-out lineages receive a share of the seeded nodes. `runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` returns the merged review frontier and runs the review fan-in guard over the recorded partition. A recorded partition with at least one dealt node builds the merged frontier even when no review lineage reports one, so a lost node still surfaces. Each fan-out CLI lineage keeps its coverage graph in `graph-db/` inside its own directory: `fanout-run.cjs` exports `DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR` to it, so the graph steps stay inside the lineage write surface instead of the shared runtime database.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && sed -n '40,52p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116116791,"end":1795116117202}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116117213,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5422bc70015XzJmlBl1Ns4le","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5421ec1001Iquz5Tc6XNHqlP","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8178c5b5334abea5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \"quality_class\\|unclassified\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph 2>/dev/null | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates the derived quality_class on research SOURCE nodes for `DLR-061`. It focuses on the path-first classification at upsert and on the source-diversity signal that reads it.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:15:This scenario validates the derived `quality_class` for `DLR-061`. It focuses on two points: `upsert.cjs` sets `quality_class` on every research SOURCE node it stores, derived from the first of its path, name, label and id that names a real location, and the `sourceDiversity` signal reads those derived classes on normal runs rather than only on fixtures that typed one in.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:19:If no producer sets `quality_class`, the source-diversity guard has nothing real to read. If the derivation runs on the wrong field, a free-text label can hide a repo path, and a leaf-supplied value can override the classification the runtime owns. Either failure lets a code-only research question pass the diversity guard it should block.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:30:- Prompt: `Upsert a research source with a repo test path and a leaf-supplied quality_class that disagrees, then confirm the stored class follows the path and that a question answered only from code files still blocks at the source diversity guard.`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:31:- Expected signals: The stored `quality_class` is `repo-test` for the test path, the leaf-supplied value is gone, a question answered only from code files scores 1.0 and blocks, and code plus its tests scores 2.0 and passes. The ledger boundary holds too: a `.jsonl` path and a ledger-named `.json` are `ledger-state`, while a `.ts` or `.cjs` named for a ledger is `repo-code`.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:52:Command 1 prints the frozen vocabulary constant, the classifier and the derivation helper. Command 2 prints one vocabulary literal, `coverage-graph-query.ts:142`, so no second copy of the class names exists. Command 3 exits 0 with all cases passing, including the path-first case, the eight-class derivation case, the three source-diversity cases and the unclassified-source parity pin. Command 4 exits 0 with no output.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:65:If the classification is wrong, check the order in `deriveSourceQualityClass` first: it tries the path, then the name, then the label, then the id, and the first field that `classifySourceLocation` does not mark `unclassified` decides. A free-text field with spaces is `unclassified` and falls through. If the diversity score is wrong, check that the seeded fixtures carry paths, or a path-shaped name or label, since a fixture whose fields are all free text cannot produce a derived class, and an `unclassified` source adds no source kind to the count.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:87:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` | Derives `quality_class` on each SOURCE node in the node loop |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:90:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/convergence-script.vitest.ts` | Source-diversity cases: 2.0, 1.0 with guard, code plus tests 2.0, an unclassified source not counted |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates the derived quality_class on research SOURCE nodes for `DLR-061`. It focuses on the path-first classification at upsert and on the source-diversity signal that reads it.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:15:This scenario validates the derived `quality_class` for `DLR-061`. It focuses on two points: `upsert.cjs` sets `quality_class` on every research SOURCE node it stores, derived from the first of its path, name, label and id that names a real location, and the `sourceDiversity` signal reads those derived classes on normal runs rather than only on fixtures that typed one in.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:19:If no producer sets `quality_class`, the source-diversity guard has nothing real to read. If the derivation runs on the wrong field, a free-text label can hide a repo path, and a leaf-supplied value can override the classification the runtime owns. Either failure lets a code-only research question pass the diversity guard it should block.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:30:- Prompt: `Upsert a research source with a repo test path and a leaf-supplied quality_class that disagrees, then confirm the stored class follows the path and that a question answered only from code files still blocks at the source diversity guard.`\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:31:- Expected signals: The stored `quality_class` is `repo-test` for the test path, the leaf-supplied value is gone, a question answered only from code files scores 1.0 and blocks, and code plus its tests scores 2.0 and passes. The ledger boundary holds too: a `.jsonl` path and a ledger-named `.json` are `ledger-state`, while a `.ts` or `.cjs` named for a ledger is `repo-code`.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:52:Command 1 prints the frozen vocabulary constant, the classifier and the derivation helper. Command 2 prints one vocabulary literal, `coverage-graph-query.ts:142`, so no second copy of the class names exists. Command 3 exits 0 with all cases passing, including the path-first case, the eight-class derivation case, the three source-diversity cases and the unclassified-source parity pin. Command 4 exits 0 with no output.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:65:If the classification is wrong, check the order in `deriveSourceQualityClass` first: it tries the path, then the name, then the label, then the id, and the first field that `classifySourceLocation` does not mark `unclassified` decides. A free-text field with spaces is `unclassified` and falls through. If the diversity score is wrong, check that the seeded fixtures carry paths, or a path-shaped name or label, since a fixture whose fields are all free text cannot produce a derived class, and an `unclassified` source adds no source kind to the count.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:87:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` | Derives `quality_class` on each SOURCE node in the node loop |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:90:| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/convergence-script.vitest.ts` | Source-diversity cases: 2.0, 1.0 with guard, code plus tests 2.0, an unclassified source not counted |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -rn \\\"quality_class\\\\|unclassified\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph 2>/dev/null | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116116935,"end":1795116117213}}}}
