{"type":"text","timestamp":1795116125372,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f5424884001ub44BV0TGEHP7u","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f542303d001iLMtPzJdFM43Ie","type":"text","text":"Iteration 9 next; I'll also check the command presentation's flag ergonomics for the remaining UX focus.\n\n","time":{"start":1795116124292,"end":1795116125372}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116125445,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f54248dc002Sd5WkRTUNGtzTa","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f542303d001iLMtPzJdFM43Ie","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac4c870395ae7aed","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"frontier-max\\|depth-mode\\|extend\" .skilled/commands/deep/review.md | head -20; echo \"===research presentation===\"; grep -n \"frontier-max\\|depth-mode\\|extend\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md | head -20"},"output":"3:argument-hint: \"<target> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n100:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1 (on a commit-range target, a merge commit with no diff of its own is pruned as `merge-no-own-diff` and a generated index rebuild as `generated-artifact`), admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6 with up to 8 depth-1 children under the review root, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), keeps node rows in `review/frontier-nodes.jsonl` (the reducer derives answered and budget-exhausted status from them on every reduce), holds open nodes as `searchDebt`, dispatches the active node's next uncovered dimension, turns a review stop candidate into another iteration while nodes stay open, and, once every node is closed and at least one was answered, forms a `frontier_drained` stop candidate that the legal-stop gates still decide, so the run can stop before its cap. A node needs one iteration per dimension in its universe, the four canonical dimensions less traceability when the config's `reviewDimensions` list leaves it out, plus any custom name, and the depth-1 band gets only `budgetSplit.depth1` (0.5) of `--max-iterations`, so set `--max-iterations` to at least `2 * ceil(nodes / lineages) * dimensions` to fund the depth-1 band. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(7, 2 × D × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes and D that universe, each counted once, and the seed step prints the derived budget. When D is four or more, the ceiling of 24 binds from the first seed, so one run cannot fund every node at every depth of a wide review; split a wide review with fan-out, where each lineage with no matrix `iterations` value sizes its own budget from its share of the seed, with D fixed at the canonical four because a lineage reviews only those. A lineage dealt no seed node, or a run whose seeds were all pruned, runs at its loop default instead: 12 iterations for a native lineage and 7 for a CLI one or a single run. The node cap stays half the budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. At about seven to eight minutes an iteration, a 24-iteration review can reach `maxDurationMinutes` (120) before its iteration cap. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n101:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n102:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n109:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_dimensions_clean` at once, so create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n110:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n===research presentation===\n3:argument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n107:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 frontier nodes from the topic before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows as new questions under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), steers Next Focus to the shallowest open node, and turns a convergence stop into another iteration while frontier nodes stay open. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(10, 2 × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes, 16 at the full six seeds, and the seed step prints the derived budget. A fan-out lineage with no matrix `iterations` value is sized the same way from its own round-robin share of the seed, with a floor of 12 for a native lineage and 10 for a CLI one, and a lineage dealt no seed node runs at that floor. The node cap stays half that budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n108:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n109:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n117:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:argument-hint: \"<target> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n100:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes from the review target before iteration 1 (on a commit-range target, a merge commit with no diff of its own is pruned as `merge-no-own-diff` and a generated index rebuild as `generated-artifact`), admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6 with up to 8 depth-1 children under the review root, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), keeps node rows in `review/frontier-nodes.jsonl` (the reducer derives answered and budget-exhausted status from them on every reduce), holds open nodes as `searchDebt`, dispatches the active node's next uncovered dimension, turns a review stop candidate into another iteration while nodes stay open, and, once every node is closed and at least one was answered, forms a `frontier_drained` stop candidate that the legal-stop gates still decide, so the run can stop before its cap. A node needs one iteration per dimension in its universe, the four canonical dimensions less traceability when the config's `reviewDimensions` list leaves it out, plus any custom name, and the depth-1 band gets only `budgetSplit.depth1` (0.5) of `--max-iterations`, so set `--max-iterations` to at least `2 * ceil(nodes / lineages) * dimensions` to fund the depth-1 band. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(7, 2 × D × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes and D that universe, each counted once, and the seed step prints the derived budget. When D is four or more, the ceiling of 24 binds from the first seed, so one run cannot fund every node at every depth of a wide review; split a wide review with fan-out, where each lineage with no matrix `iterations` value sizes its own budget from its share of the seed, with D fixed at the canonical four because a lineage reviews only those. A lineage dealt no seed node, or a run whose seeds were all pruned, runs at its loop default instead: 12 iterations for a native lineage and 7 for a CLI one or a single run. The node cap stays half the budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. At about seven to eight minutes an iteration, a 24-iteration review can reach `maxDurationMinutes` (120) before its iteration cap. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n101:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n102:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n109:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_dimensions_clean` at once, so create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n110:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n===research presentation===\n3:argument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n107:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 frontier nodes from the topic before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows as new questions under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), steers Next Focus to the shallowest open node, and turns a convergence stop into another iteration while frontier nodes stay open. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(10, 2 × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes, 16 at the full six seeds, and the seed step prints the derived budget. A fan-out lineage with no matrix `iterations` value is sized the same way from its own round-robin share of the seed, with a floor of 12 for a native lineage and 10 for a CLI one, and a lineage dealt no seed node runs at that floor. The node cap stays half that budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n108:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n109:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n117:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"frontier-max\\\\|depth-mode\\\\|extend\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/review.md | head -20; echo \\\"===research presentation===\\\"; grep -n \\\"frontier-max\\\\|depth-mode\\\\|extend\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116124380,"end":1795116125445}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116125454,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f54249ab001UrOwi7XZlBm7Dd","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f542303d001iLMtPzJdFM43Ie","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8fe0803bdc391df","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"frontier-max\\|depth-mode\\|extend\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -20"},"output":"58:  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart|completed-continue] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive), `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived) and `completed-continue` (from --extend=N: a completed run extended in place by N iterations, same sessionId and generation). `fork` is not accepted. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n59:  extend: \"[EXTEND] - Positive integer N from --extend=N. Sets lineage_mode to completed-continue and adds N iterations to a completed run. Default: unset.\"\n60:  extend_minutes: \"[EXTEND_MINUTES] - Positive integer M from --extend-minutes=M, the minutes an extension adds to the later of the prior maxDurationMinutes and the minutes already elapsed since createdAt. Only valid with --extend. Default: unset, which adds the prior maxDurationMinutes, and a run with no duration budget keeps none.\"\n66:  frontier_max_depth: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_DEPTH] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-depth=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxDepth: the deepest level the frontier may grow to. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps 3.\"\n67:  frontier_max_nodes: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_NODES] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-nodes=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: the run-wide frontier node cap. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps null, so the cap derives as half the iteration budget.\"\n311:  step_reject_extend_with_fanout:\n312:    description: \"Refuse --extend on a fan-out config before any lineage spawns\"\n321:    message: \"Usage error (extend-with-fanout): --extend extends a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n332:    message: \"Usage error (frontier-caps-with-fanout): --frontier-max-depth and --frontier-max-nodes apply to a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n405:            --depth-mode {depth_mode}\n425:          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n426:          - frontier_cap_values: \"When frontier_max_depth or frontier_max_nodes is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), else fail with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-value): --frontier-max-depth needs a positive integer' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Either one bound while depth_mode != 'expansive' fails with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-without-expansive): --frontier-max-depth only applies with --depth-mode=expansive' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock.\"\n514:      step_extend_completed_run:\n519:          --extend=N continues a finished run in the same session and generation. The\n527:          WORK_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-extend.XXXXXX\")\"\n530:            const [configPath, stateLogPath, extendRaw, extendMinutesRaw, workDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n534:            if (!/^[1-9][0-9]*$/.test(String(extendRaw))) {\n535:              fail(\"--extend needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(String(extendRaw)) + \".\");\n537:            const minutesRaw = String(extendMinutesRaw);\n539:              fail(\"--extend-minutes needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(minutesRaw) + \".\");\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"58:  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart|completed-continue] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive), `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived) and `completed-continue` (from --extend=N: a completed run extended in place by N iterations, same sessionId and generation). `fork` is not accepted. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n59:  extend: \"[EXTEND] - Positive integer N from --extend=N. Sets lineage_mode to completed-continue and adds N iterations to a completed run. Default: unset.\"\n60:  extend_minutes: \"[EXTEND_MINUTES] - Positive integer M from --extend-minutes=M, the minutes an extension adds to the later of the prior maxDurationMinutes and the minutes already elapsed since createdAt. Only valid with --extend. Default: unset, which adds the prior maxDurationMinutes, and a run with no duration budget keeps none.\"\n66:  frontier_max_depth: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_DEPTH] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-depth=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxDepth: the deepest level the frontier may grow to. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps 3.\"\n67:  frontier_max_nodes: \"[FRONTIER_MAX_NODES] - Positive integer N from --frontier-max-nodes=N, written to expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: the run-wide frontier node cap. Only valid with --depth-mode=expansive. Default: unset, which keeps null, so the cap derives as half the iteration budget.\"\n311:  step_reject_extend_with_fanout:\n312:    description: \"Refuse --extend on a fan-out config before any lineage spawns\"\n321:    message: \"Usage error (extend-with-fanout): --extend extends a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n332:    message: \"Usage error (frontier-caps-with-fanout): --frontier-max-depth and --frontier-max-nodes apply to a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n405:            --depth-mode {depth_mode}\n425:          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n426:          - frontier_cap_values: \"When frontier_max_depth or frontier_max_nodes is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), else fail with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-value): --frontier-max-depth needs a positive integer' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Either one bound while depth_mode != 'expansive' fails with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-without-expansive): --frontier-max-depth only applies with --depth-mode=expansive' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock.\"\n514:      step_extend_completed_run:\n519:          --extend=N continues a finished run in the same session and generation. The\n527:          WORK_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-extend.XXXXXX\")\"\n530:            const [configPath, stateLogPath, extendRaw, extendMinutesRaw, workDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n534:            if (!/^[1-9][0-9]*$/.test(String(extendRaw))) {\n535:              fail(\"--extend needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(String(extendRaw)) + \".\");\n537:            const minutesRaw = String(extendMinutesRaw);\n539:              fail(\"--extend-minutes needs a positive integer, and got \" + JSON.stringify(minutesRaw) + \".\");\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"frontier-max\\\\|depth-mode\\\\|extend\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116124587,"end":1795116125454}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1795116126575,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f542516f001aGQiQGAghdP41u","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f542303d001iLMtPzJdFM43Ie","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"a2ffa1628a805068fa4cd1b2ead97b57deecd6eb","cost":0.003131616,"tokens":{"input":1648,"output":224,"reasoning":1275,"cache":{"read":400704,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795116129092,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f5425b44001timQ0rdMLxOIOe","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5425176001TKbnW27K3facCz","type":"step-start","snapshot":"8d56ae3e20b6c4745a8896b63bb30eee5356d7ef"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116137196,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f5426acf001x2q7ZYHyxGR6YO","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5425176001TKbnW27K3facCz","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d69e20d3d6c94bb","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 9 - F-1-007 traceability: pivot retry, continuity and quality class against the packet\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension traceability. Node scope: the pivot library and mode scripts, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`, with packet docs, catalogs and playbooks as evidence.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (one rule restated across catalog, playbook and reference), operator UX (pivot refusal and retry text), cross-CLI/OS parity (the pivot path and event contract shared by both loops).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts`, `deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts` -- the requirement surfaces for this node.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md` and `loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md` -- the retry and pivot claims.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md` and `council/divergent-council-quorum-retry.md` -- the DLR-061 and DLR-062 scenarios.\n- Traceability sources: `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-001..REQ-009, `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008, `007-source-diversity-quality-class` REQ-001..REQ-007.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-001..REQ-009 match the pivot code, the retry event and the scoped seat count; `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 match the close rule and band budget; `007` REQ-001..REQ-007 match the classifier, the constant and the signal. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | The 012 retry, agreement and seat-scope cases exist by name; the 007 eight-class and signal cases exist; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | The pivot section states \"an accepted candidate becomes the next review direction through `restoredFocus`. The pivot writes no frontier node.\" That matches the code and confirms R3-P1-001 is a packet-text defect. The expansive-depth page's produced-evidence sentence remains the R2-P1-001 doc side. |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | DLR-061 names the path-first classifier, the eight classes, the unclassified parity pin and the signal threshold; DLR-062 names the retry scenario. Both match the code and the tests they cite. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:44` is the shipped-behavior sentence that contradicts AC-008 and agrees with `deep-review.yaml:1429`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22` states the sixth frontier-revisit source, the one-time quorum retry and the six-output ceiling, which match `divergent-pivot.ts:1507-1540` and `:1589`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:30-65` cites the classifier order and the signal cases; the order matches `upsert.cjs:343-351`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/council/divergent-council-quorum-retry.md` covers the one-time retry the pivot branch implements.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The command presentation's `--depth-mode` flag row is a single contract paragraph that restates the reference; that operator-UX cost belongs to the command-presentation node outside this lineage's partition (F-1-002/F-1-004), so it is recorded here as a deferred observation rather than a finding.\n- The catalog's pivot sentence and AC-008 cannot both be true; the code and catalog agree, so R3-P1-001's remediation is an AC/plan amendment unless the operator chooses the admission behavior.\n- The quality-class playbook does not address a Windows path shape; that is the R5-P2-001 advisory's documentation side.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Every 012 requirement resolves to a named test or a matching branch, including the attempt-scoped ids and the one-time retry.\n- The 007 classifier order, the frozen vocabulary and the unclassified exclusion each have a playbook case and an integration case.\n- The catalogs' retry and revisit claims match the code and the YAML gate.\n- Both loop-specific pivot scripts derive the same identity and count only their own pivot's seat returns.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A new catalog finding for the pivot sentence: it matches the code and is the evidence that R3-P1-001 is stale packet text.\n- A Windows path finding for the playbook: the code advisory R5-P2-001 already carries it; the playbook omission is its doc side.\n- A retry-parity finding between the two loops: both YAMLs and both scripts carry the same one-time rule.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability on F-1-003 (fan-out runner and merge clarity, duplication and change cost).\n- Reason: traceability is covered on all three nodes; maintainability is the last dimension and the fan-out merge carries the most cross-consumer machinery.\n- Required evidence: the merge's repeated rollup helpers, the prompt builders' duplicated pre-bound blocks, and the dashboards/report text the merge emits.\n- Rotation status: correctness, security and traceability covered on all nodes; maintainability uncovered on all three.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 9 - F-1-007 traceability: pivot retry, continuity and quality class against the packet\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension traceability. Node scope: the pivot library and mode scripts, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`, with packet docs, catalogs and playbooks as evidence.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (one rule restated across catalog, playbook and reference), operator UX (pivot refusal and retry text), cross-CLI/OS parity (the pivot path and event contract shared by both loops).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts`, `deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts` -- the requirement surfaces for this node.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md` and `loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md` -- the retry and pivot claims.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md` and `council/divergent-council-quorum-retry.md` -- the DLR-061 and DLR-062 scenarios.\\n- Traceability sources: `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-001..REQ-009, `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008, `007-source-diversity-quality-class` REQ-001..REQ-007.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-001..REQ-009 match the pivot code, the retry event and the scoped seat count; `010` REQ-005/REQ-008 match the close rule and band budget; `007` REQ-001..REQ-007 match the classifier, the constant and the signal. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | The 012 retry, agreement and seat-scope cases exist by name; the 007 eight-class and signal cases exist; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | The pivot section states \\\"an accepted candidate becomes the next review direction through `restoredFocus`. The pivot writes no frontier node.\\\" That matches the code and confirms R3-P1-001 is a packet-text defect. The expansive-depth page's produced-evidence sentence remains the R2-P1-001 doc side. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | DLR-061 names the path-first classifier, the eight classes, the unclassified parity pin and the signal threshold; DLR-062 names the retry scenario. Both match the code and the tests they cite. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/expansive-depth-mode.md:44` is the shipped-behavior sentence that contradicts AC-008 and agrees with `deep-review.yaml:1429`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/feature-catalog/severity-system/divergent-convergence-mode.md:22` states the sixth frontier-revisit source, the one-time quorum retry and the six-output ceiling, which match `divergent-pivot.ts:1507-1540` and `:1589`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/coverage-graph/source-quality-class-derivation.md:30-65` cites the classifier order and the signal cases; the order matches `upsert.cjs:343-351`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/council/divergent-council-quorum-retry.md` covers the one-time retry the pivot branch implements.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The command presentation's `--depth-mode` flag row is a single contract paragraph that restates the reference; that operator-UX cost belongs to the command-presentation node outside this lineage's partition (F-1-002/F-1-004), so it is recorded here as a deferred observation rather than a finding.\\n- The catalog's pivot sentence and AC-008 cannot both be true; the code and catalog agree, so R3-P1-001's remediation is an AC/plan amendment unless the operator chooses the admission behavior.\\n- The quality-class playbook does not address a Windows path shape; that is the R5-P2-001 advisory's documentation side.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Every 012 requirement resolves to a named test or a matching branch, including the attempt-scoped ids and the one-time retry.\\n- The 007 classifier order, the frozen vocabulary and the unclassified exclusion each have a playbook case and an integration case.\\n- The catalogs' retry and revisit claims match the code and the YAML gate.\\n- Both loop-specific pivot scripts derive the same identity and count only their own pivot's seat returns.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A new catalog finding for the pivot sentence: it matches the code and is the evidence that R3-P1-001 is stale packet text.\\n- A Windows path finding for the playbook: the code advisory R5-P2-001 already carries it; the playbook omission is its doc side.\\n- A retry-parity finding between the two loops: both YAMLs and both scripts carry the same one-time rule.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability on F-1-003 (fan-out runner and merge clarity, duplication and change cost).\\n- Reason: traceability is covered on all three nodes; maintainability is the last dimension and the fan-out merge carries the most cross-consumer machinery.\\n- Required evidence: the merge's repeated rollup helpers, the prompt builders' duplicated pre-bound blocks, and the dashboards/report text the merge emits.\\n- Rotation status: correctness, security and traceability covered on all nodes; maintainability uncovered on all three.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116133071,"end":1795116137196}}}}
