assifier found the POSIX-only split; the rest of the reducer and upsert path handled every state input without a shell or an out-of-packet write.\n - Iteration 6: reading the pivot config parser beside its writer confirmed the persistence contract is strict; the graph query path's allowlist and parameter binding closed the metadata and SQL surfaces.\n - Iteration 7: checking the feature catalog and playbooks against the fan-out code showed the catalog agrees with the implemented pivot handoff, which narrows the iteration 3 finding's fix to the packet text.\n - Iteration 8: matching each acceptance row to a named test showed the extension and evidence-edge requirements are pinned end to end; no requirement rests on prose alone.\n+- Iteration 9: the catalog's pivot sentence gave the cleanest evidence on the one open contradiction: the shipped docs agree with the code, so the acceptance row is the stale surface.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Iteration 8: matching each acceptance row to a named test showed the extension and evidence-edge requirements are pinned end to end; no requirement rests on prose alone.\\n- Iteration 9: the catalog's pivot sentence gave the cleanest evidence on the one open contradiction: the shipped docs agree with the code, so the acceptance row is the stale surface.\", \"oldString\": \"- Iteration 8: matching each acceptance row to a named test showed the extension and evidence-edge requirements are pinned end to end; no requirement rests on prose alone.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepsee