{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795116151612,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f542b33c0013gAMQdvx70hSoz","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f542aa7f001Zi5Ma5Sf0078Yg","type":"step-start","snapshot":"21ecc338d5a311396dba9e5e9d8a33b405960bb6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116157987,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f542bfed001Dt7Q95NZUogkXB","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f542aa7f001Zi5Ma5Sf0078Yg","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeaaf8c2313dd3ff","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 10 - F-1-003 maintainability: fan-out runner and merge change cost\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-003, dimension maintainability. Node scope: `fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` and their unit suites.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (every duplicated helper named and judged against the two-instance rule), operator UX (merged warnings and attribution text), cross-CLI/OS parity (the adapter switch and its fallback).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` -- prompt builders, adapter switch, budget and watchdogs.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` -- merge helpers, warning text and attribution output.\n- Traceability sources: `009-fanout-review-coverage-merge` REQ-001..REQ-006.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | The merge helpers restate the reducer rollup as R1-P2-004 records; no new maintainability contradiction. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-010/AC-011 match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3492-3515` keeps one adapter per executor kind and fails closed on an unknown kind, so a new kind has one registration point.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:946-1009` keeps each merge surface in its own function; the only duplicated arithmetic is the traceability rollup already recorded as R1-P2-004.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:1780-1800` writes the partition warning and the merge summary with named fields, so an operator can tell a missing node from an open one.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The native and CLI prompt builders carry two PRE-BOUND lists; they differ only in the surfaces each delivery path needs (`review_target_type`, the lineage artifact dir), and two instances do not earn a shared builder under `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4.\n- `fanout-run.cjs` is a large file because it owns adapters, prompt rendering, budget derivation, containment and watchdogs; no single change in this range required touching more than one of those groups, so it is not reported as a cohesion defect.\n- The review and research YAML retry blocks are literal twins; the per-loop workflow split is deliberate and the compiled-contract check is the existing drift guard.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- One adapter map covers all nine executor kinds and throws on an unknown one.\n- The merge's helpers are separated by rule, and the only duplicated rule is already a finding.\n- Warning and summary text names the missing, open or failed item instead of printing a generic failure.\n- The per-lineage budget note names the lineage and its derived share, so an operator can trace a budget without reading the config.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Extracting the PRE-BOUND block into a shared builder: two delivery paths, two lists, no third caller.\n- Reporting file size or file count as a maintainability defect: no concrete change in this range paid a cost for it.\n- A lint-style duplication finding for the two YAML retry blocks: the workflows are separate contracts and the contract-drift check is the existing guard.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability on F-1-005 (reducer and upsert clarity, duplication and change cost).\n- Reason: F-1-003 is complete across all four dimensions; F-1-005 carries the shared reducer helpers and the evidence derivation that later changes will touch.\n- Required evidence: the two reducers' parallel frontier helpers, the upsert's derived-evidence helpers, and the strategy/dashboard rendering paths.\n- Rotation status: F-1-003 complete; F-1-005 and F-1-007 have maintainability left.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 10 - F-1-003 maintainability: fan-out runner and merge change cost\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-003, dimension maintainability. Node scope: `fanout-run.cjs`, `fanout-merge.cjs` and their unit suites.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (every duplicated helper named and judged against the two-instance rule), operator UX (merged warnings and attribution text), cross-CLI/OS parity (the adapter switch and its fallback).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` -- prompt builders, adapter switch, budget and watchdogs.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs` -- merge helpers, warning text and attribution output.\\n- Traceability sources: `009-fanout-review-coverage-merge` REQ-001..REQ-006.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | The merge helpers restate the reducer rollup as R1-P2-004 records; no new maintainability contradiction. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-010/AC-011 match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3492-3515` keeps one adapter per executor kind and fails closed on an unknown kind, so a new kind has one registration point.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:946-1009` keeps each merge surface in its own function; the only duplicated arithmetic is the traceability rollup already recorded as R1-P2-004.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:1780-1800` writes the partition warning and the merge summary with named fields, so an operator can tell a missing node from an open one.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The native and CLI prompt builders carry two PRE-BOUND lists; they differ only in the surfaces each delivery path needs (`review_target_type`, the lineage artifact dir), and two instances do not earn a shared builder under `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4.\\n- `fanout-run.cjs` is a large file because it owns adapters, prompt rendering, budget derivation, containment and watchdogs; no single change in this range required touching more than one of those groups, so it is not reported as a cohesion defect.\\n- The review and research YAML retry blocks are literal twins; the per-loop workflow split is deliberate and the compiled-contract check is the existing drift guard.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- One adapter map covers all nine executor kinds and throws on an unknown one.\\n- The merge's helpers are separated by rule, and the only duplicated rule is already a finding.\\n- Warning and summary text names the missing, open or failed item instead of printing a generic failure.\\n- The per-lineage budget note names the lineage and its derived share, so an operator can trace a budget without reading the config.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Extracting the PRE-BOUND block into a shared builder: two delivery paths, two lists, no third caller.\\n- Reporting file size or file count as a maintainability defect: no concrete change in this range paid a cost for it.\\n- A lint-style duplication finding for the two YAML retry blocks: the workflows are separate contracts and the contract-drift check is the existing guard.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability on F-1-005 (reducer and upsert clarity, duplication and change cost).\\n- Reason: F-1-003 is complete across all four dimensions; F-1-005 carries the shared reducer helpers and the evidence derivation that later changes will touch.\\n- Required evidence: the two reducers' parallel frontier helpers, the upsert's derived-evidence helpers, and the strategy/dashboard rendering paths.\\n- Rotation status: F-1-003 complete; F-1-005 and F-1-007 have maintainability left.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116154861,"end":1795116157987}}}}
