{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795116199421,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f5436dfd001zsC2kek6ZzIvU3","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54363a5001tCjtqYbVNGXqmY","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d1ec85b54545929f44d4f85ffd257309b45b7a12"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1795116209036,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f543815a002R1kIfzqYYBFJU1","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54363a5001tCjtqYbVNGXqmY","type":"text","text":"Two maintainability passes remain. Writing iterations 11 and 12.\n\n","time":{"start":1795116204378,"end":1795116209036}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116209049,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f54381a4001YZmIT3BYK0DHN2","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54363a5001tCjtqYbVNGXqmY","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6d7e7a8a8e44c5c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 11 - F-1-005 maintainability: reducer and upsert change cost\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-005, dimension maintainability. Node scope: the two reducers, `upsert.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` and the five `runtime/lib` folders.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (the shared predicate and the two reducers' helpers), operator UX (dashboard and strategy rendering), cross-CLI/OS parity (one rule in one module for both loops).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- frontier projection, strategy and dashboard renderers, lineage state.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- the parallel frontier helpers.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` -- the shared `reviewOmitsTraceability` / `reviewUnfinishedCoreProtocols` predicates.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` -- derived-evidence helpers and the node loop.\n- Traceability sources: `006-state-log-leaf-fields` REQ-001..REQ-004, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-018.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | The shared predicates live in one module and both consumers import them; no maintainability contradiction. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-004/AC-018/AC-019 match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:18` imports `reviewOmitsTraceability` and `reviewUnfinishedCoreProtocols` from `convergence.cjs`, so one predicate decides what the stop gate owes and what the reducer's universe contains.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2390-2492` keeps every strategy section update behind an anchor helper, with a warning path when an anchor is missing.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs:265-300` separates finding collection, id resolution and evidence derivation into named helpers.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2452-2530` mirrors the review reducers' node helpers but keeps its own question-resolution rule, so the divergence is contract, not drift.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The two reducers repeat the marker regex and the visit ranking. This is the second instance; `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4 keeps it separate until a third consumer appears, and the review path's `frontierNodeId`/store-active attribution is not the research path's focus-marker rule.\n- `convergence.cjs` owns two predicates the reducer imports; the alternative is a third small module for two functions, which moves the cost rather than removing it.\n- The reducer's three writers use plain `fs.writeFileSync` while the merge uses realpath-guarded readers; the asymmetry predates the range and is recorded as hardening, not a maintainability finding.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Every strategy section update has one anchor helper and a missing-anchor warning instead of a partial rewrite.\n- The frontier projection, the band budget and the registry build are separated by rule.\n- The upsert's finding-id resolution and evidence derivation are separate helpers with a single caller each.\n- Both reducers keep loop-specific rules local and share the frontier primitives through `frontier-admit.cjs`.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Extracting the two reducers' marker/visit helpers at two instances: no third consumer, and the attribution rules differ by contract.\n- Moving the two convergence predicates into a new module: it relocates a two-caller helper without shrinking the surface.\n- Reporting the plain writers as a maintainability defect: the asymmetry predates the range and is a hardening note.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability on F-1-007 (pivot and coverage-graph change cost).\n- Reason: F-1-005 is complete across all four dimensions; F-1-007 is the last maintainability pass and its attempt handling is the most intricate new state machine.\n- Required evidence: the pivot's attempt transition writes, the library/YAML retry split, the graph vocabulary and the per-mode script duplication.\n- Rotation status: F-1-003 and F-1-005 complete; F-1-007 has maintainability left.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-011.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-011.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-011.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 11 - F-1-005 maintainability: reducer and upsert change cost\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-005, dimension maintainability. Node scope: the two reducers, `upsert.cjs`, `convergence.cjs`, `verify-iteration.cjs`, `dispatch-iteration.cjs` and the five `runtime/lib` folders.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (the shared predicate and the two reducers' helpers), operator UX (dashboard and strategy rendering), cross-CLI/OS parity (one rule in one module for both loops).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- frontier projection, strategy and dashboard renderers, lineage state.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs` -- the parallel frontier helpers.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` -- the shared `reviewOmitsTraceability` / `reviewUnfinishedCoreProtocols` predicates.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` -- derived-evidence helpers and the node loop.\\n- Traceability sources: `006-state-log-leaf-fields` REQ-001..REQ-004, `011-review-frontier-mode` REQ-018.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | The shared predicates live in one module and both consumers import them; no maintainability contradiction. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-004/AC-018/AC-019 match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:18` imports `reviewOmitsTraceability` and `reviewUnfinishedCoreProtocols` from `convergence.cjs`, so one predicate decides what the stop gate owes and what the reducer's universe contains.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2390-2492` keeps every strategy section update behind an anchor helper, with a warning path when an anchor is missing.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs:265-300` separates finding collection, id resolution and evidence derivation into named helpers.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2452-2530` mirrors the review reducers' node helpers but keeps its own question-resolution rule, so the divergence is contract, not drift.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The two reducers repeat the marker regex and the visit ranking. This is the second instance; `prevent-overengineering.md` section 4 keeps it separate until a third consumer appears, and the review path's `frontierNodeId`/store-active attribution is not the research path's focus-marker rule.\\n- `convergence.cjs` owns two predicates the reducer imports; the alternative is a third small module for two functions, which moves the cost rather than removing it.\\n- The reducer's three writers use plain `fs.writeFileSync` while the merge uses realpath-guarded readers; the asymmetry predates the range and is recorded as hardening, not a maintainability finding.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Every strategy section update has one anchor helper and a missing-anchor warning instead of a partial rewrite.\\n- The frontier projection, the band budget and the registry build are separated by rule.\\n- The upsert's finding-id resolution and evidence derivation are separate helpers with a single caller each.\\n- Both reducers keep loop-specific rules local and share the frontier primitives through `frontier-admit.cjs`.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Extracting the two reducers' marker/visit helpers at two instances: no third consumer, and the attribution rules differ by contract.\\n- Moving the two convergence predicates into a new module: it relocates a two-caller helper without shrinking the surface.\\n- Reporting the plain writers as a maintainability defect: the asymmetry predates the range and is a hardening note.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability on F-1-007 (pivot and coverage-graph change cost).\\n- Reason: F-1-005 is complete across all four dimensions; F-1-007 is the last maintainability pass and its attempt handling is the most intricate new state machine.\\n- Required evidence: the pivot's attempt transition writes, the library/YAML retry split, the graph vocabulary and the per-mode script duplication.\\n- Rotation status: F-1-003 and F-1-005 complete; F-1-007 has maintainability left.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-011.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116204452,"end":1795116209049}}}}
