{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795116212920,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f543a2b8001sk3WrEPNEbiw8q","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f543973a0010cObP0NXNVS21W","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a2c0ce8afaca1d42800e026f665d27d2f478da9d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116218871,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f543a2be001zEZeIX0tLHqsp5","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f543973a0010cObP0NXNVS21W","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe4fb17e321cb2f","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 12 - F-1-007 maintainability: pivot and coverage-graph change cost\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension maintainability. Node scope: the pivot library and mode scripts, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`.\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (the double config write and the two retry controls named and judged), operator UX (attempt and failure text), cross-CLI/OS parity (per-loop paths and vocabularies).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts` -- attempt transition, retry loop, event ids and paths.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs` -- the subcommand surface the workflow drives.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts` -- the per-loop seed builders.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts`, `coverage-graph-query.ts` -- the per-loop vocabularies and safe metadata.\n- Traceability sources: `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-001..REQ-009, `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The attempt-1 to attempt-2 config transition writes the config twice and the second write bypasses the conflict check** -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1296 -- When a retry opens, `preparePivotTransaction` calls `persistConfig(paths.configPath, openingRecord)` to replay the attempt-1 record unchanged, then `writeStateIfChangedAtomic(paths.configPath, configRecord, ...)` to adopt attempt 2. `persistConfig` is the guarded writer (it refuses a conflicting existing config), and `writeStateIfChangedAtomic` is the raw atomic writer, so the second call is the only write in the pivot that can replace a config without the guard. A reader must reconstruct why the replay exists, and a future caller that adds a third attempt or a migrated config shape has to re-derive the same two-step order; a crash between the writes leaves attempt 1 persisted with the attempt-failed event durable, which is only safe because the next prepare re-enters this branch.\nFinding class: instance-only\nScope proof: the only `writeStateIfChangedAtomic` call in the file is this branch (`:1299`); every other config write goes through `persistConfig`. The comment at `:1289-1298` explains the replay but not the guard asymmetry.\nAffected surface hints: [\"divergent-pivot.ts preparePivotTransaction\", \"persistConfig\", \"writeStateIfChangedAtomic\", \"attempt transition\"]\nCase: a later change adds an attempt-3 path and copies `persistConfig` alone; the attempt-2 record no longer replays, `persistConfig` throws a conflict, and the retry fails at prepare instead of reporting a pivot failure.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-007's attempt identity and config parse match; the double write is an implementation detail the REQ does not name. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `012` AC rows match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1490-1535` writes the retryable attempt failure with its own event id and lifecycle, which the YAML retry step reads.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs:15-25` documents that prepare is mode-owned while record-seat and finalize act on the persisted transaction, which is why finalize accepts the caller's paths.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:225-229` keeps one relation vocabulary per loop, so the research `DERIVED_FROM` edge cannot leak into a review graph.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The library `runDivergentPivot` retries in-process while the YAML re-enters `step_prepare_divergent_pivot`; the two controls exist because the library is the packaged API and the workflow must orchestrate native seat dispatch across steps. They are ruled out as a duplication defect, not as a maintainability fix target.\n- `finalize` trusts the caller's paths JSON; only the workflow calls it, and the pivot paths are built once by prepare. The trust note is already recorded in the security iteration.\n- The review and research pivot scripts both build a seat list and identity; the seats and trigger text differ by loop, so the shared part is the library's transaction, not the builders.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Attempt 1 keeps its historical ids and paths, and attempt 2 has a distinct prefix, so an older pivot still loads.\n- The retry event is distinct from `pivot_failed`, and the workflow reads its `retryable` flag rather than guessing from the reason.\n- Every config write has a stated replay rule; only the one transition needs the two-step order, and it is documented.\n- The graph vocabularies are per loop and the safe metadata list is one frozen constant.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Collapsing the library retry loop and the YAML retry step: different owners and different dispatch models.\n- A duplication finding for the two mode-specific pivot builders: the shared transaction lives in the library; the builders carry genuinely different seats and triggers.\n- A vocabulary finding for `DERIVED_FROM`: it is research-only and the review graph never emits it.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining. All three dealt nodes cover correctness, security, traceability and maintainability; the frontier is answered and the run proceeds to synthesis with stop reason `converged` / reasonDetail `frontier_drained`.\n- Reason: the dealt frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node, which is the legal `frontier_drained` candidate once the stop gates pass.\n- Required evidence: the findings registry, the merged state log and the iteration files this synthesis reads.\n- Rotation status: complete.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-012.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-012.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-012.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 12 - F-1-007 maintainability: pivot and coverage-graph change cost\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `deepseek` (session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineageMode new).\\n- Frontier node: F-1-007, dimension maintainability. Node scope: the pivot library and mode scripts, `continuity-thread.cjs` and `runtime/lib/coverage-graph`.\\n- Operator review focus covered in this iteration: overengineering (the double config write and the two retry controls named and judged), operator UX (attempt and failure text), cross-CLI/OS parity (per-loop paths and vocabularies).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts` -- attempt transition, retry loop, event ids and paths.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs` -- the subcommand surface the workflow drives.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/divergent-review-pivot.ts`, `deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts` -- the per-loop seed builders.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts`, `coverage-graph-query.ts` -- the per-loop vocabularies and safe metadata.\\n- Traceability sources: `012-pivot-hygiene` REQ-001..REQ-009, `010-research-frontier-mode` REQ-005/REQ-008.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The attempt-1 to attempt-2 config transition writes the config twice and the second write bypasses the conflict check** -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1296 -- When a retry opens, `preparePivotTransaction` calls `persistConfig(paths.configPath, openingRecord)` to replay the attempt-1 record unchanged, then `writeStateIfChangedAtomic(paths.configPath, configRecord, ...)` to adopt attempt 2. `persistConfig` is the guarded writer (it refuses a conflicting existing config), and `writeStateIfChangedAtomic` is the raw atomic writer, so the second call is the only write in the pivot that can replace a config without the guard. A reader must reconstruct why the replay exists, and a future caller that adds a third attempt or a migrated config shape has to re-derive the same two-step order; a crash between the writes leaves attempt 1 persisted with the attempt-failed event durable, which is only safe because the next prepare re-enters this branch.\\nFinding class: instance-only\\nScope proof: the only `writeStateIfChangedAtomic` call in the file is this branch (`:1299`); every other config write goes through `persistConfig`. The comment at `:1289-1298` explains the replay but not the guard asymmetry.\\nAffected surface hints: [\\\"divergent-pivot.ts preparePivotTransaction\\\", \\\"persistConfig\\\", \\\"writeStateIfChangedAtomic\\\", \\\"attempt transition\\\"]\\nCase: a later change adds an attempt-3 path and copies `persistConfig` alone; the attempt-2 record no longer replays, `persistConfig` throws a conflict, and the retry fails at prepare instead of reporting a pivot failure.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `012` REQ-007's attempt identity and config parse match; the double write is an implementation detail the REQ does not name. The iteration 3 REQ-007 admission claim remains the only partial. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `012` AC rows match; AC-008 remains outstanding. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1490-1535` writes the retryable attempt failure with its own event id and lifecycle, which the YAML retry step reads.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs:15-25` documents that prepare is mode-owned while record-seat and finalize act on the persisted transaction, which is why finalize accepts the caller's paths.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:225-229` keeps one relation vocabulary per loop, so the research `DERIVED_FROM` edge cannot leak into a review graph.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The library `runDivergentPivot` retries in-process while the YAML re-enters `step_prepare_divergent_pivot`; the two controls exist because the library is the packaged API and the workflow must orchestrate native seat dispatch across steps. They are ruled out as a duplication defect, not as a maintainability fix target.\\n- `finalize` trusts the caller's paths JSON; only the workflow calls it, and the pivot paths are built once by prepare. The trust note is already recorded in the security iteration.\\n- The review and research pivot scripts both build a seat list and identity; the seats and trigger text differ by loop, so the shared part is the library's transaction, not the builders.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Attempt 1 keeps its historical ids and paths, and attempt 2 has a distinct prefix, so an older pivot still loads.\\n- The retry event is distinct from `pivot_failed`, and the workflow reads its `retryable` flag rather than guessing from the reason.\\n- Every config write has a stated replay rule; only the one transition needs the two-step order, and it is documented.\\n- The graph vocabularies are per loop and the safe metadata list is one frozen constant.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Collapsing the library retry loop and the YAML retry step: different owners and different dispatch models.\\n- A duplication finding for the two mode-specific pivot builders: the shared transaction lives in the library; the builders carry genuinely different seats and triggers.\\n- A vocabulary finding for `DERIVED_FROM`: it is research-only and the review graph never emits it.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining. All three dealt nodes cover correctness, security, traceability and maintainability; the frontier is answered and the run proceeds to synthesis with stop reason `converged` / reasonDetail `frontier_drained`.\\n- Reason: the dealt frontier holds no open or active node and at least one answered node, which is the legal `frontier_drained` candidate once the stop gates pass.\\n- Required evidence: the findings registry, the merged state log and the iteration files this synthesis reads.\\n- Rotation status: complete.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-012.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116212926,"end":1795116218871}}}}
