{"type":"text","timestamp":1795116272231,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f54472c30024c3vrfCSh8vee1","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54457cd001wxeGTW5WlylRGj","type":"text","text":"Now I'll compile the synthesis report and run the workflow's closeout.\n\n","time":{"start":1795116266179,"end":1795116272231}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116272248,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f54472f2001YAl6me1sRnLRlq","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f54457cd001wxeGTW5WlylRGj","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8da5d4874c23bd6c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Report - expansive-depth program (fan-out lineage deepseek)\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n**Verdict: CONDITIONAL** (active P0 = 0, active P1 = 2, active P2 = 6; `hasAdvisories = true`).\n\nThe detached `deepseek` lineage reviewed range `21c4b325b5a..de32abbb74d` over `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop`, `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/agents` and the `.claude`, `.codex`, `.pi`, `.dsh` and `.vibe` agent mirrors. It completed 12 iterations across the three dealt frontier nodes (`F-1-003`, `F-1-005`, `F-1-007`) and all four configured dimensions. Scope: runtime code and tests, command YAML and presentation, skill docs, feature catalogs and playbooks; `specs/` evidence was used for traceability only.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\nCONDITIONAL routes to `/speckit:plan`. Two P1 findings need a decision before release:\n\n- the frontier `answered` projection counts `thought`/`stuck` records as dimension evidence (R2-P1-001);\n- the packet's REQ-007/AC-008 promise pivot-candidate admission the workflow does not perform (R3-P1-001), where the shipped catalog and the workflow agree on the implemented behavior.\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | Evidence |\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|----------|\n| R2-P1-001 | P1 | correctness | A `thought` iteration covers a frontier dimension and spends node depth | `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1971-1984`, `frontier-admit.cjs:90`, `deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:238` |\n| R3-P1-001 | P1 | traceability | REQ-007 and AC-008 promise pivot-candidate admission the pivot branch never performs | `deep-review.yaml:1429`, `:1541-1547`; `011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147`, `acceptance-criteria.md:63`, `plan.md:67/71` |\n| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | Detached lineage contract names a FRONTIER block the CLI prompt never renders | `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1791`, `deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:28` |\n| R1-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | Frontier steering and projection order by locale collation while the merge orders by code unit | `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1924`, `:2016`; `deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2447`, `:2512`; `fanout-merge.cjs:928` |\n| R1-P2-003 | P2 | correctness | A single lineage that omits `graphCoverageMode` erases the mode the others agree on | `runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:1003` |\n| R1-P2-004 | P2 | correctness | The merge re-implements the reducer's traceability summary arithmetic | `runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:982`, `reduce-state.cjs:1652-1665` |\n| R5-P2-001 | P2 | security | Source-quality classification assumes POSIX separators, so Windows-separated paths lose their spec and test classes | `runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs:330` |\n| R12-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | The attempt-1 to attempt-2 config transition writes the config twice and the second write bypasses the conflict check | `runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1296-1309` |\n\nR2-P2-001 (locale ordering on the reducer/steering surface) was merged into R1-P2-002 as a refinement.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **Frontier evidence integrity** (R2-P1-001): filter `thought`/`stuck` out of the frontier visit and dimension-coverage path, matching the review doctrine and the research reducer's question-coverage rule.\n2. **Packet truth** (R3-P1-001): amend REQ-007, AC-008 and plan lines 67/71 to \"the accepted direction becomes `next_dimension` and writes no frontier node\", or implement the admission the AC describes. The catalog and code agree on the former.\n3. **Fan-out prompt and ordering** (R1-P2-001, R1-P2-002): render the FRONTIER block in the detached CLI prompt, or remove the contract reference to it; replace `localeCompare` node ordering with the code-unit comparator the merge uses.\n4. **Merge coverage edges** (R1-P2-003): record a mode disagreement explicitly instead of collapsing it to `null`; collapse R1-P2-004 into the reducer's `buildTraceabilityRollup` when the shared helper is next touched.\n5. **Cross-OS and bookkeeping hardening** (R5-P2-001, R12-P2-001): classify paths on both separators; make the attempt transition one guarded write helper.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- Frontier visit evidence must exclude every status the doctrine calls evidence-free (`thought`, `stuck`), not only `error`/`timeout`.\n- The pivot handoff is `restoredFocus` → `next_dimension`, with no frontier node; REQ-007/AC-008 should say so unless admission is chosen.\n- `--depth-mode` fan-out prompts must carry the node identity and dimension the leaf contract references.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- One code change for R2-P1-001 with a reducer case for a `thought` record and a `stuck` record.\n- One packet-text change for R3-P1-001 (or a feature worth its own phase if admission is chosen).\n- One prompt change for R1-P2-001 plus a golden prompt test; one comparator change for R1-P2-002.\n- Two P2 code changes for R5-P2-001 and R12-P2-001; R1-P2-003/R1-P2-004 as a single merge-hardening change.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Status | Notes |\n|----------|--------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | 001, 006, 007, 010, 012 match; 011 REQ-007/AC-008 admission claim does not. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-004, AC-005, AC-010, AC-011, AC-018, AC-019 match; AC-008 does not. |\n| `skill_agent` | pass | Skill and agent definition share the depth-mode, veto and frontier-row contract. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | Canonical agent and five mirrors carry the new frontier contract. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | Catalogs match except the expansive-depth \"produced evidence\" sentence (R2-P1-001 doc side). |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | DRV-081, DRV-083, DLR-061 and DLR-062 name existing commands and cases. |\n\n## 8. Resource Map Coverage Gate\n\nOmitted: no `resource-map.md` exists in the packet, so the gate does not apply.\n\n## 9. Deferred Items\n\n- P2 advisories: R1-P2-001..004, R5-P2-001, R12-P2-001.\n- The command presentation's `--depth-mode` flag row is a contract-length paragraph that restates the reference; that operator-UX cost belongs to the command-presentation node outside this lineage's partition.\n- Residual hardening (pre-existing, not range findings): the reducer's plain file writers lack a symlink guard; a corrupt lineage state log aborts the whole merge; `dispatch-iteration.cjs:835` falls back to `/tmp` instead of `os.tmpdir()`.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n- **Run:** session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`, artifact directory `review/lineages/deepseek`.\n- **Iterations:** 12, each recorded through the append gateway with route proof and an append-only delta. Frontier nodes: F-1-003, F-1-005, F-1-007; each answered on all four dimensions.\n- **Stop:** `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained`; no open or active frontier node, three answered, stop gates and graph decision still apply.\n- **Replay:** the registry was rebuilt from the state log and deltas on every reduce; convergence score 0.95, search debt 0, corruption 0.\n- **Coverage:** all four configured dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) across three nodes = 12 node visits; ledger revisions 3-13.\n- **Residual risk:** the two P1s are not release blockers for the review loop's utility but block a PASS; the P1 traceability item can be closed by packet amendment if the operator confirms the shipped no-node behavior.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Deep Review Report - expansive-depth program (fan-out lineage deepseek)\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n**Verdict: CONDITIONAL** (active P0 = 0, active P1 = 2, active P2 = 6; `hasAdvisories = true`).\\n\\nThe detached `deepseek` lineage reviewed range `21c4b325b5a..de32abbb74d` over `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop`, `.skilled/commands/deep`, `.skilled/agents` and the `.claude`, `.codex`, `.pi`, `.dsh` and `.vibe` agent mirrors. It completed 12 iterations across the three dealt frontier nodes (`F-1-003`, `F-1-005`, `F-1-007`) and all four configured dimensions. Scope: runtime code and tests, command YAML and presentation, skill docs, feature catalogs and playbooks; `specs/` evidence was used for traceability only.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\nCONDITIONAL routes to `/speckit:plan`. Two P1 findings need a decision before release:\\n\\n- the frontier `answered` projection counts `thought`/`stuck` records as dimension evidence (R2-P1-001);\\n- the packet's REQ-007/AC-008 promise pivot-candidate admission the workflow does not perform (R3-P1-001), where the shipped catalog and the workflow agree on the implemented behavior.\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | Evidence |\\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|----------|\\n| R2-P1-001 | P1 | correctness | A `thought` iteration covers a frontier dimension and spends node depth | `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1971-1984`, `frontier-admit.cjs:90`, `deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:238` |\\n| R3-P1-001 | P1 | traceability | REQ-007 and AC-008 promise pivot-candidate admission the pivot branch never performs | `deep-review.yaml:1429`, `:1541-1547`; `011-review-frontier-mode/spec.md:147`, `acceptance-criteria.md:63`, `plan.md:67/71` |\\n| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | Detached lineage contract names a FRONTIER block the CLI prompt never renders | `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1791`, `deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:28` |\\n| R1-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | Frontier steering and projection order by locale collation while the merge orders by code unit | `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1924`, `:2016`; `deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2447`, `:2512`; `fanout-merge.cjs:928` |\\n| R1-P2-003 | P2 | correctness | A single lineage that omits `graphCoverageMode` erases the mode the others agree on | `runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:1003` |\\n| R1-P2-004 | P2 | correctness | The merge re-implements the reducer's traceability summary arithmetic | `runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs:982`, `reduce-state.cjs:1652-1665` |\\n| R5-P2-001 | P2 | security | Source-quality classification assumes POSIX separators, so Windows-separated paths lose their spec and test classes | `runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs:330` |\\n| R12-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | The attempt-1 to attempt-2 config transition writes the config twice and the second write bypasses the conflict check | `runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts:1296-1309` |\\n\\nR2-P2-001 (locale ordering on the reducer/steering surface) was merged into R1-P2-002 as a refinement.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **Frontier evidence integrity** (R2-P1-001): filter `thought`/`stuck` out of the frontier visit and dimension-coverage path, matching the review doctrine and the research reducer's question-coverage rule.\\n2. **Packet truth** (R3-P1-001): amend REQ-007, AC-008 and plan lines 67/71 to \\\"the accepted direction becomes `next_dimension` and writes no frontier node\\\", or implement the admission the AC describes. The catalog and code agree on the former.\\n3. **Fan-out prompt and ordering** (R1-P2-001, R1-P2-002): render the FRONTIER block in the detached CLI prompt, or remove the contract reference to it; replace `localeCompare` node ordering with the code-unit comparator the merge uses.\\n4. **Merge coverage edges** (R1-P2-003): record a mode disagreement explicitly instead of collapsing it to `null`; collapse R1-P2-004 into the reducer's `buildTraceabilityRollup` when the shared helper is next touched.\\n5. **Cross-OS and bookkeeping hardening** (R5-P2-001, R12-P2-001): classify paths on both separators; make the attempt transition one guarded write helper.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- Frontier visit evidence must exclude every status the doctrine calls evidence-free (`thought`, `stuck`), not only `error`/`timeout`.\\n- The pivot handoff is `restoredFocus` → `next_dimension`, with no frontier node; REQ-007/AC-008 should say so unless admission is chosen.\\n- `--depth-mode` fan-out prompts must carry the node identity and dimension the leaf contract references.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- One code change for R2-P1-001 with a reducer case for a `thought` record and a `stuck` record.\\n- One packet-text change for R3-P1-001 (or a feature worth its own phase if admission is chosen).\\n- One prompt change for R1-P2-001 plus a golden prompt test; one comparator change for R1-P2-002.\\n- Two P2 code changes for R5-P2-001 and R12-P2-001; R1-P2-003/R1-P2-004 as a single merge-hardening change.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|--------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | 001, 006, 007, 010, 012 match; 011 REQ-007/AC-008 admission claim does not. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | AC-004, AC-005, AC-010, AC-011, AC-018, AC-019 match; AC-008 does not. |\\n| `skill_agent` | pass | Skill and agent definition share the depth-mode, veto and frontier-row contract. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | Canonical agent and five mirrors carry the new frontier contract. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | Catalogs match except the expansive-depth \\\"produced evidence\\\" sentence (R2-P1-001 doc side). |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | DRV-081, DRV-083, DLR-061 and DLR-062 name existing commands and cases. |\\n\\n## 8. Resource Map Coverage Gate\\n\\nOmitted: no `resource-map.md` exists in the packet, so the gate does not apply.\\n\\n## 9. Deferred Items\\n\\n- P2 advisories: R1-P2-001..004, R5-P2-001, R12-P2-001.\\n- The command presentation's `--depth-mode` flag row is a contract-length paragraph that restates the reference; that operator-UX cost belongs to the command-presentation node outside this lineage's partition.\\n- Residual hardening (pre-existing, not range findings): the reducer's plain file writers lack a symlink guard; a corrupt lineage state log aborts the whole merge; `dispatch-iteration.cjs:835` falls back to `/tmp` instead of `os.tmpdir()`.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n- **Run:** session `fanout-deepseek-1795113418367-pvzn7z`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`, artifact directory `review/lineages/deepseek`.\\n- **Iterations:** 12, each recorded through the append gateway with route proof and an append-only delta. Frontier nodes: F-1-003, F-1-005, F-1-007; each answered on all four dimensions.\\n- **Stop:** `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained`; no open or active frontier node, three answered, stop gates and graph decision still apply.\\n- **Replay:** the registry was rebuilt from the state log and deltas on every reduce; convergence score 0.95, search debt 0, corruption 0.\\n- **Coverage:** all four configured dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) across three nodes = 12 node visits; ledger revisions 3-13.\\n- **Residual risk:** the two P1s are not release blockers for the review loop's utility but block a PASS; the P1 traceability item can be closed by packet amendment if the operator confirms the shipped no-node behavior.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116266226,"end":1795116272248}}}}
