{"type":"text","timestamp":1795116312835,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"id":"prt_1f545227c001q7fIiYVo3BA30a","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5450f72001knGC5GXKyhTbVG","type":"text","text":"The closeout flagged a pre-existing false invariant triggered by the documented `refines` path (it reports incomplete as a warning, not an error). I'll record that honestly and complete the workflow's terminal record.\n\n","time":{"start":1795116311164,"end":1795116312835}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795116312862,"sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","part":{"partID":"prt_1f54523570016xCsWL7jRC4x8o","sessionID":"ses_e0acc529fffetdTx9mE3m9n6Pl","messageID":"msg_1f5450f72001knGC5GXKyhTbVG","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae22abef92827314","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- **Residual risk:** the two P1s are not release blockers for the review loop's utility but block a PASS; the P1 traceability item can be closed by packet amendment if the operator confirms the shipped no-node behavior.\n- **Synthesis closeout warning:** `synthesis-closeout.cjs` staged `synthesis_incomplete` (severity `warning`) with `structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry`, because iteration 2 recorded the refinement R2-P2-001 and the reducer merged it into R1-P2-002 while the closeout counts iteration finding ids against registry findings. Both the closeout count and the `refines` mechanism predate this range, so this is a pre-existing false positive rather than a range finding; the report and registry are complete and the warning is recorded as-is.","oldString":"- **Residual risk:** the two P1s are not release blockers for the review loop's utility but block a PASS; the P1 traceability item can be closed by packet amendment if the operator confirms the shipped no-node behavior.","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md\n@@ -77,4 +77,5 @@\n - **Stop:** `converged` with reasonDetail `frontier_drained`; no open or active frontier node, three answered, stop gates and graph decision still apply.\n - **Replay:** the registry was rebuilt from the state log and deltas on every reduce; convergence score 0.95, search debt 0, corruption 0.\n - **Coverage:** all four configured dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) across three nodes = 12 node visits; ledger revisions 3-13.\n - **Residual risk:** the two P1s are not release blockers for the review loop's utility but block a PASS; the P1 traceability item can be closed by packet amendment if the operator confirms the shipped no-node behavior.\n+- **Synthesis closeout warning:** `synthesis-closeout.cjs` staged `synthesis_incomplete` (severity `warning`) with `structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry`, because iteration 2 recorded the refinement R2-P2-001 and the reducer merged it into R1-P2-002 while the closeout counts iteration finding ids against registry findings. Both the closeout count and the `refines` mechanism predate this range, so this is a pre-existing false positive rather than a range finding; the report and registry are complete and the warning is recorded as-is.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- **Residual risk:** the two P1s are not release blockers for the review loop's utility but block a PASS; the P1 traceability item can be closed by packet amendment if the operator confirms the shipped no-node behavior.\\n- **Synthesis closeout warning:** `synthesis-closeout.cjs` staged `synthesis_incomplete` (severity `warning`) with `structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry`, because iteration 2 recorded the refinement R2-P2-001 and the reducer merged it into R1-P2-002 while the closeout counts iteration finding ids against registry findings. Both the closeout count and the `refines` mechanism predate this range, so this is a pre-existing false positive rather than a range finding; the report and registry are complete and the warning is recorded as-is.\", \"oldString\": \"- **Residual risk:** the two P1s are not release blockers for the review loop's utility but block a PASS; the P1 traceability item can be closed by packet amendment if the operator confirms the shipped no-node behavior.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/deepseek/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795116311383,"end":1795116312862}}}}
